module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode

// ONE ROW PER FAILURE CLASS, BECAUSE ONE SENTENCE PER FLEET WAS THE DEFECT.
//
// These classes lived in a single 11,751-character `p(text:)` blob in gunbc.design_document. Every
// lane that named a new class appended to that one line, so two lanes naming two UNRELATED classes
// collided on every merge -- five conflict cycles on one PR in one night, every resolution purely
// additive, zero sentences ever lost. That is textual contention standing in for semantic
// contention: the classes are independent, and only the line was shared. Split into rows, two lanes
// touch two declarations and never collide, while two lanes editing the SAME class still conflict --
// which is correct, because that is real disagreement about one fact (DESIGN section 2).
//
// THIS CUT IS MECHANICAL AND ITS ORACLE IS AN EMPTY DIFF. Each row carries its authored sentence
// BYTE-FOR-BYTE and the projection renders them in roster order, so regenerating DESIGN.md after the
// split produces no change at all. Sorting the rows by identity would reorder the paragraph and
// destroy that oracle -- a projection defect would then be indistinguishable from an intended edit --
// so order is carried by the roster and determinism comes from the roster being source-ordered.
//
// WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: the analytic fields (misleading surface, actual question, failure
// mechanism, required guard) that these rows will eventually carry. Filling them for seventeen
// classes means authoring analysis that does not exist in the text today, which is semantic
// rewriting inside a structural cut and has no oracle. They land in a follow-up where each class is
// a readable diff.
//
// WHY `evidence` STAYS EMPTY ON EVERY ROW, recorded so the next author does not fill in seventeen
// empty lists and call it citation hygiene. The field is a typed `DeclarationRef` list and a typed
// citation is genuinely better than a symbol spelled inside `authored` -- but measured today,
// nothing resolves it and nobody reads it. `v2.lens.cited_symbol_resolution` takes its population
// from `hand_authored_production_doc_declaration_refs` (HandAuthoredDocBind primary_work plus
// additional_works) and this carrier is not in it; `gunbc.design_document` projects `.authored`
// alone, so a populated `evidence` renders nowhere; and that lens has not executed on a push since
// the 2026-08-23 directive deleted its job, which its own `cited_symbol_required_check_note`
// records as a declared rung drop to mitigatable. A citation that no resolver covers and no reader
// sees is not partial coverage -- it is the decoration DESIGN section 4b calls worse than absent,
// because it will be cited as coverage. THE OCCASION MATTERS: this was decided in the diff that
// repaired a specimen whose whole defect was three symbols nothing ever checked, and populating an
// unchecked field there would have reproduced the finding inside its own repair.
// dissolve-on: the cited-symbol law's own trigger -- enrollment widens to every structural
// DeclarationRef carrier when the Node-tree reader lands. At that point these rows carry resolvable
// evidence and the symbols in `authored` become the redundant half.
//
// WHY EVERY ROW IS ONE LINE, and it is a merge property rather than a formatting taste.
//
// The split above removed the shared LINE and left a shared BLOCK TAIL. Every row ended with the
// same two lines -- `evidence: [],` and `}` -- so when two lanes each appended a row, the three-way
// merge factored that identical suffix out of the conflict region: ONE tail below the markers for
// TWO half-blocks above them. Measured with `git merge-file` against this file at merge base
// d0009ca531, two synthetic lanes each appending one row: the region opens at both lanes' `data`
// line and closes after their `authored:` line, and the purely additive resolution -- delete the
// markers, keep both sides, which is what "every resolution purely additive, zero sentences ever
// lost" means for a roster -- yields a first block whose closing lines belong to the second.
//
// A one-line row has no tail to lose. The only suffix a merge can factor out of the region is the
// blank separator between rows, which carries nothing, so both sides of every region are WHOLE
// declarations and the additive resolution is total. What this does NOT do is remove the conflict --
// two lanes appending still collide at this file's two append points, and that pressure is a carrier
// question, not this one.
//
// THE RUNG, STATED HONESTLY BECAUSE THIS PARAGRAPH IS WHAT THE NEXT APPENDER READS. The population
// carries no severable tail. The SHAPE IS NOT ENFORCED -- no lens covers row shape on this carrier
// -- so one hand-authored multi-line row restores the two-line tail and the whole geometry with it.
// The invalid state therefore stays WRITABLE and this is mechanically preventable at best, not
// structural; calling the shape construction would be the rung inflation DESIGN section 4b(1) names,
// sitting in the annotation an author consults before appending. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the
// capability and not as an artifact that would contribute to one: a row-shape obligation DECIDED for
// every declaration of a growth-surface type rather than observed on the rows that happen to exist
// -- the corpus already reads declared types per declaration through `v2.std.decl_index`
// `data_decl_type_facts`, and what is missing is a producer carrying each declaration's source
// EXTENT, sufficient for refusing a multi-line row of such a type at authoring time. Until that
// exists, the shape is a convention held by review and by this paragraph.
//
// THE LOSS STATES ARE MEASURED AND THE SET IS COMPLETE, which is why no check is written here.
// Against a gunbc built from source at d0009ca531, severing a multi-line row is loud in every one of
// the three ways the two-line tail can be cut: losing BOTH lines and losing `}` alone are PARSE
// refusals at the module index (`expected expression, found Eq` -- a `data` keyword landing in
// record-field position), and losing `evidence: [],` alone is a RESOLVE refusal (`missing required
// field 'evidence' in literal of type 'RecurringFailureMode'`). Nothing silent was found in that
// set. A brace-balance or declared-versus-rostered check would be the DESIGN section 4b decoration:
// permanently green, because the only corpus it could fire on never reaches it.

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, List }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef }

type RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: NonEmptyStr
  authored: String
  evidence: List<DeclarationRef>
}

data hollow_alias: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "hollow_alias" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "hollow alias (minimality ≠ grounding)", evidence: [] }

data state_space_conflation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "state_space_conflation" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "state-space conflation (an `Option`/`None` meaning >2 things — split into named variants; its most-repeated form here is **not-applicable rendered as malformed** — one reason symbol over \"the input is wrong\" and \"this strategy had nothing to say about it\", which have opposite owners and opposite repairs. Found three times in three stages by one lane (#8801 and #8828 in body lowering, `parse_g0_tokens_remain` in parse), always by reading the producer and never from the message. Recognition rule: if the arm sits downstream of a search, lookup or alternative that returned `Absent`, it is not-applicable and needs its own reason. A SECOND FORM, which does not match that shape and is the same class: **a dichotomy stated over a domain with three states.** Specimen (gunbc#9324): the `floor_resource_sample` comment documented `pswpin` rising with `pgmajfault` as swap and `pgmajfault` rising with `pswpin` flat as mapping churn — two arms over three states, since BOTH FLAT is quiet. Churn is a defect this lane owns and quiet is the absence of one, so the missing arm inverts the verdict. The mechanism of the misread is what the recognition rule keys on: `pgmajfault rises` and `pswpin flat` are two conditions and only their CONJUNCTION is churn, so a reader matching on the cheaper condition alone selects churn for a state that satisfies `pswpin flat` and nothing else — which zero-and-zero does. **Recognition rule for this form: for every arm of a stated dichotomy, enumerate the domain and check that each arm's conditions are required jointly.** What made it invisible rather than merely wrong is that BOTH readers landed on the same arm — 26 intervals so classified by one and 6 by another, neither having compared notes — and agreement reads as confirmation. THAT IS A PROMPT TO RE-DERIVE, NOT A DIAGNOSTIC, and the distinction is load-bearing: convergent readings are equally produced by shared assumptions, a common heuristic, ambiguity in the subject, or one reader having anchored on the other, and n=2 on one specimen cannot separate those from a defect in the rule. What survives is only the weaker direction — agreement between readers of one rule is not independent evidence about that rule, because the shared input is a shared potential defect, so it licenses re-deriving from the domain and never a conclusion about which cause produced it.) **A THIRD FORM, and the one that is hardest to rank because nothing is wrong today: A STATE THAT IS ALREADY LOAD-BEARING AND CARRIED AS AN AD-HOC SPELLING RATHER THAN A CONSTRUCTOR.** Specimen (2026-09-01): the identity key threaded through v1.compiler.coercion has THREE inhabitants -- a real declaring module path, the synthetic <kernel:NAME> that v1.std.core kernel_span mints for kernel nodes, and the empty string meaning unknown -- while every consumer discriminates only empty from non-empty. lookup_checkpoint and type_realization_decision therefore read <kernel:String> as a KNOWN declaration and proceed to the spelling-keyed arm; decl_file_declares_structurally compares that synthetic identity against a roster of real paths with contains, which no <kernel:NAME> can ever match, so the structural gate is unreachable for a kernel-resolved reference BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by decision. The key reaches those gates with exactly that value through type_reference_decl_file, from v1.compiler.emit coerce_primitive_type and v1.compiler.emit_rust rust_named_type_base and rust_applied_type_base. **What makes this the third form rather than an instance of the first two is the evidence that the state is REAL: the tree already handles it, three times, by string prefix.** numeric_realization_declaring_modules carries the literal \"<kernel:\" as a row in a roster of MODULE PATHS; is_kernel_minted_file is a substring predicate over the same spelling; and v1.compiler.env resolved_node_is_kernel_identity_for_name owns the same fact by EXACT EQUALITY, its own note recording that a substring or prefix test is a second, weaker authority for it. **Recognition rule for this form: when a value's domain is carried in a type that cannot express one of its inhabitants, look for the inhabitant being recognised by SPELLING somewhere -- a prefix test, a magic string in a roster of real values, a sentinel. Each such site is a consumer that already knows the state exists, and their number is the count of authorities the missing constructor has spawned.** NO WRONG ANSWER IS CLAIMED FOR THE SPECIMEN AND NONE WAS MEASURED: for the kernel names reaching those gates today the spelling-keyed answer is the correct one, which is exactly why it never surfaced -- the class is filed on the state space, not on an output, and a form that produces no incident is the one that will be found last. **CLIMB RECEIPT (2026-09-02), appended rather than replacing the filing above, because DESIGN section 4b(4) keeps a class's discriminating evidence enrolled AFTER the climb rather than dissolving it with the production machinery.** The missing constructor now exists: std.coercion TypeDeclarationProvenance is CorpusDeclared | KernelMinted | DeclarationIdentityAbsent, minted by v1.std.core declaration_provenance_of, which decides the kernel arm by EXACT EQUALITY against kernel_span -- the minter itself -- rather than by a prefix test over its output. All four spelling authorities this row counted are gone: the literal \"<kernel:\" row is deleted from numeric_realization_declaring_modules, is_kernel_minted_file is deleted, and the two gates that substring-compared a synthetic identity against real paths now take the coproduct, so the structural gate's unreachability for a kernel-resolved reference stops being BY CONSTRUCTION and becomes BY DECISION -- a named arm answering false. **WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, because this row's own honesty is the thing being climbed:** no wrong answer was found before and none is fixed now; every answer is preserved bit for bit, which is why the climb is in the STATE SPACE and not in an output. The empty-string inhabitant is likewise gone from the channel, and the bare-table answer it used to reach silently is now the named ground GroundedByUnidentifiedBareRow, so a declared rung drop that was previously indistinguishable from a properly-keyed answer is countable and refusable. **THE RECOGNITION RULE IS CORROBORATED AND THE CORROBORATION IS INDEPENDENT.** gunbc.type_reference_decl_file_occurrence_census reached this same four-authority set from the opposite direction -- that census asked what each of thirty-nine occurrences NEEDS, this row asked what the identity key can HOLD -- and the counts agreed. **WHAT SURVIVES UNCLIMBED, stated so the row is not read as closed:** CorpusDeclared still carries a file path matched by contains, so the surviving arm answers WHAT A DECLARATION REALIZES AS positionally. v1.compiler.infer_env global_bare_fallback_invariant already states the terminal key for it -- filepaths are irrelevant, the declared module path is the containment tree -- and re-keying that arm needs a declaration reference at each gate, which is a separate change.\n\n**A FOURTH FORM, MEASURED 2026-09-02 (quick-crab-396), AND IT SITS IN THE INTERPRETER RATHER THAN IN ANY MODEL: DECLARED OPTIONAL AND CONSTRUCTED ABSENT ARE TWO STATES WEARING ONE SPELLING.** A record field declared `T?` is read by authors -- and by this document's own §2 reasoning about optional carriers -- as optional-with-a-none-default. It is not. A literal that OMITS the field typechecks, and a later read of that field REFUSES at evaluation with `NoSuchField { type_name, field }`. So `T?` means mandatory-at-construction-and-typed-optional, and the two states the spelling conflates are `the field is absent because the author wrote none` and `the field is absent because the literal predates it`. EVIDENCE, a two-row probe with a positive control, which is what makes it a finding rather than a conjecture about one type: `type Widget { name: String  tag: Int? }` with `Widget { name: \"w\" }` refuses on `.tag` with `NoSuchField { type_name: \"Widget\", field: \"tag\" }`, while `Widget { name: \"w\", tag: Present { value: 3 } }.tag` reads back correctly -- so the mechanism is neither `reads fail` nor `this type is broken`, it is omission-with-no-default, and it is GENERAL to any record type. RUNG: this is FAIL-CLOSED and explicitly NOT silent wrongness -- the interpreter refuses rather than answering the false that a reader would expect -- which is the whole of the good news and it is what sets the rung at mitigatable rather than below the ladder. WHAT THE CORPUS CURRENTLY BELIEVES INSTEAD, and this is the reason the row exists: two carriers filed this on 2026-08-27 as `a nested compile is not evaluable in the interpreter, refusing with NoSuchField Node.ident` -- v1.tests.claim.reference_derived_disposition_census_witness_test and a sibling paragraph in v1.compiler.emit_rust. Nested compiles are one POPULATION that happens to construct Nodes through helpers omitting v1.std.core Node's `ident` and then read it; they are not the class, and the repair that description suggests (route around the nested pipeline with a host builtin) does not touch the cause. **POPULATION: UNENUMERATED, and stated as such rather than guessed.** It is every record type in the corpus carrying an optional field together with a literal that omits it; `v1.std.core Node.ident` is one specimen and the probe above is another. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: construction that supplies every declared field, so that a literal omitting an optional field is either unwritable or carries the absent value -- at which point the distinction between the two absences is made at construction and no read can encounter a field that was never written. NOT REPAIRED HERE BY RULING: a defaulting change alters evaluation semantics corpus-wide and needs its own subject, population and review.", evidence: [] }

data absorbing_fallback: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "absorbing_fallback" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "absorbing fallback (a failure arm that widens — rerun everything, scan all keys, always run — instead of refusing; ⊤-as-answer conflated with ⊤-as-ignorance; the deficit's frequency zeroed by construction, the corpus-denominated cost breaking the budget later)", evidence: [] }

data empty_observation_narrow: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "empty_observation_narrow" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**empty-observation narrow** (the absorbing fallback's mirror: ⊥-as-answer conflated with ⊥-as-ignorance — an observation that could not express what changed rendered as the verdict \"nothing is affected\", so the run narrows to nothing instead of widening. Strictly worse than the widen §5 already forbids: a widen is merely expensive, a narrow is silently uncovered. Live specimen: a push whose baseline ref *is* the pushed ref diffs the commit against itself, and the witness floor reported the resulting zero-path observation as \"N unaffected (import-closure, skipped without resolve)\" — receipt, two main pushes reporting an identical `4118 unaffected` on different commits, a skip count that cannot be a function of the diff. The tell that one observation is wrong rather than three local choices reasonable: its consumers disagree — compile-clean widened to whole-tree, regen gated on the event name, the witness floor skipped) **RECEIPT, AND IT MOVES THE CLASS FROM AN OBSERVATION'S EXPRESSIVENESS TO AN ANALYSIS'S RANGE** (quick-crab-396, 2026-09-02). Authoring a coproduct arm named `Refused`, I ran a corpus-wide collision census over TYPE names, got a clean answer, and authored the name. required-regen then refused: `variant 'Refused' appears in both 'TypeRealizationDecision' and 'EmitterOutcome'`, and re-running the census over VARIANT spellings found `Refused` live in SIX declaring types. THE DEFECT WAS NOT A MISSING ANALYSIS. The compiler already computes exactly this collision -- it is what refused -- but it computes it during v2 self-compile over ONE RESOLVED CLOSURE, and the question being asked was about the CORPUS. Same subject, two ranges. From the author's seat the narrow analysis's silence was indistinguishable from a negative result, which is this row's own conflation with the scope quantifier moved: not an observation that could not EXPRESS what changed, but one that could not REACH where the answer lived. WHY IT IS FILED HERE RATHER THAN AS A NEW CLASS: the mechanism is identical and only the axis differs, and DESIGN section 2 prices a fresh authority for an existing concept as a failed decomposition. RECOGNITION RULE: when a check answers clean, ask what POPULATION it ranged over and whether that is the population the question was about -- an analysis scoped to the wrong range is, from the caller's seat, indistinguishable from an analysis that does not exist. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for this instance, named as the capability and not as an artifact: A CORPUS-WIDE NAMESPACE CENSUS OVER EVERY TYPE DECLARATION AND EVERY COPRODUCT ARM, sufficient to answer 'is this spelling already declared anywhere in the corpus' before a name is authored, rather than after emission. ONE census over the one Node tree, not a second check beside the type-name one -- two checks over one namespace is the range split that produced this instance.", evidence: [] }

data cache_impurity: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "cache_impurity" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "cache impurity (key on declared-input content; byte-identical cached-vs-cold is the purity oracle)", evidence: [] }

data reflection_evidence_structural_proof: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "reflection_evidence_structural_proof" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "reflection evidence ≠ structural proof (prove a read axis by execution, with a no-host-enumeration control)", evidence: [] }

data coercion_proven_by_normalized_round_trip: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "coercion_proven_by_normalized_round_trip" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "coercion proven by normalized round-trip, not a golden string", evidence: [] }

data parallel_representation_debt: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "parallel_representation_debt" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "parallel-representation debt (an honestly-marked scaffold duplicating a canonical fact is still a violation)", evidence: [] }

data internal_review_finds_missing_tests_external: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "internal_review_finds_missing_tests_external" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "internal review finds missing tests, external review finds missing checks", evidence: [] }

data unmarked_workaround: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "unmarked_workaround" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "unmarked workaround (an author-side absorbing fallback — routing around an obstacle with no dissolution trigger; the line-stop signal, never a landing state)", evidence: [] }

data self_authorized_dissolution: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "self_authorized_dissolution" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**self-authorized dissolution** (temporary work treated as admissible because the author named its future deletion — a trigger is a lifecycle fact, not permission; without an operator verdict, marked debt is rejected exactly like unmarked debt)", evidence: [] }

data positional_citation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "positional_citation" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "positional citation (a `file:line` pointer where a symbol was available — see §3). **THE EDIT FORM IS THE SAME CLASS AND IT ALSO WRITES.** An edit anchored on NEIGHBOURING TEXT -- sed on a surrounding line, a string replace keyed on the adjacent entry, an insert before a named sibling -- is a positional handle by another spelling, and it decays for the identical reason: anything that changes above or beside the anchor invalidates it. The difference is the consequence. A stale citation misleads a reader who can still see the text; a stale ANCHOR silently does NOTHING, because a replace that matches zero times reports success. **RECEIPT (sunny-gull-270, 2026-09-02, this carrier).** Appending the row `hedged_benefit_leaves_the_harm_axis_unexamined` needed two edits: the declaration and the roster-list entry. The roster append was anchored on `one_refusal_two_destinations,` followed by the closing bracket. Between reading the file and writing it, main gained `liveness_probe_read_as_currency` as the new last entry, so the anchor stopped matching, the declaration landed and the roster entry did not, and NOTHING FAILED -- the result would have been a declared-but-unrostered class, exactly the half-applied state a roster cannot detect about itself. **WHAT CAUGHT IT IS THE TRANSFERABLE PART, and it is not vigilance: `grep -c` returning 1 where 2 was owed.** The instruction is to CHECK THE RESULT RATHER THAN THE ACTION, because a no-op edit and a successful one are indistinguishable at the actuator -- the same discipline that catches a stale citation by reading `git show origin/main:<path>` rather than the working tree, which a manager on this same exchange used to avoid refuting a correct citation from a pinned checkout. Two instances, one root: a read and a write separated by someone else's push. **RECOGNITION RULE: any edit whose anchor is text the edit does not own. State the expected post-condition as a COUNT before applying it, and assert the count afterwards; if you cannot say what the count should become, the edit is not specified.**", evidence: [] }

data bound_shaped_closure: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "bound_shaped_closure" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**bound-shaped closure** (a requirement is satisfied by a number that is real, and the row it satisfies stops ranking for work. Distinct from prefix-of-the-truth, which is about what a PRODUCER reports: this is about what a CONSUMER concludes from a satisfied clause. Receipt (gunbc#9418): §4b(3) asks a declared drop for a bounded population; a whole-root emit census answers three; the emitter's first gate had returned ahead of every later check, and clearing it showed eight more that had been standing the whole time. Publishing three as THE population would have discharged 4b(3) with an honest measurement and left the class reading as closed — worse than the UNCOUNTED it replaced, because an unmet clause still ranks and a met one does not. The tell is that the satisfying figure comes from a mechanism that STOPS: a first match, an early return, a capped scan, a truncated list. **Recognition rule: before a number discharges a requirement, ask what the producer does AFTER it has enough to answer — if it returns, the number bounds the producer's patience and not the population.**)", evidence: [] }

data authority_substitution: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "authority_substitution" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**authority substitution** (fact F lives in carrier A; operation O is governed by carrier B; A is cited as the evidence that O changed; no A→B relation is claimed by either carrier. Nothing asserted is false — the *entailment* is invented, which is why review reads past it: both halves check out and only the arrow between them is missing. It is §3's single-authority rule read in the direction authors actually violate it — not two authorities for one fact, but one authority borrowed to answer for another's. Receipt (gunbc#8865): an expecting-red probe was enrolled in `gunbc.explicit_witness_admission`, which DOCUMENTS a known red, and the PR asserted the required floor therefore held it; the floor gates on `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` and nothing relates the two, so CI went red on a row its author had recorded as expected. The general tell is a sentence of the form *I registered it in A, so B now does X* where B is never named — and its structural fix is never a broader guard joining every A row to B, since that manufactures exactly the entailment being invented; the guard must carry the narrow predicate, with its exceptions declared.)", evidence: [] }

data reachability_read_as_occupancy: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "reachability_read_as_occupancy" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**reachability read as occupancy** (a guard's arm, disposition or check is deleted because nothing currently lands in it. Three questions are in play and only the first two decide whether it should exist: *mechanism existence* — can any governing authority produce this state; *join reachability* — can that mechanism classify an element of THIS operation's denominator; *current occupancy* — does anything receive it today. **Yes / yes / zero is a healthy guard being quiet, not a dead one**, and deleting it removes a live wall while looking principled. The distinction is load-bearing because it borders a true rule pointing the other way: a check whose RED IS UNREACHABLE — no authorable input can produce it — is a decoration, permanently green and worse than absent, because it is cited as coverage. Unreachable means the red cannot be produced at all; empty means it can and nothing does. Two corollaries, each from a lane that got it wrong first. Reachability is judged against what a FIXTURE MAY AUTHOR, never what the accepted corpus contains — a regression probe is an invalid program by definition, so a state no `Accepted` program holds is usually still authorable as source, and scoping reachability to corpus-expressible is this same conflation one layer out. And an arm is reachable relative to ONE operation: `gunbc.scm`'s path-exclusion disposition is unreachable from the floor's own fold, which drops excluded subjects before inventory, yet reachable from a join over admission ROWS, which exclusion never removes — so *the arm's reachability is a property of the denominator of the operation that returns it, not of what some lower mechanism observes internally*. Both halves were found the same day by separate lanes, from opposite directions. **THE DISCRIMINATING COUNTER-SPECIMEN, which this row needed and did not have (gunbc XL-0-RECEIPT, 2026-09-01):** `gunbc.floor_component_receipt` and `gunbc.floor_component_receipt_document` were a well-built pair — schema, artifact name, path, a typed subject carrying workflow name / run id / head sha, a decoder with typed `ReceiptMemberAbsent` and `ReceiptMemberMalformed` causes, and an event-subject join refusing over three distinct mismatch arms. Read against the three questions the answer is not yes/yes/zero but **NO at the first**: nothing anywhere writes `target/floor-component-receipt.json`, no Rust carries the schema string, and `witnesses.yml` uploads four artifacts of which the receipt is not one. Their reader was the `falsifier-alert.yml` job, deleted in the 2026-08-15 CI cut. **The join is UNREACHABLE, not merely unoccupied, and that is the whole difference between retiring a dead model and deleting a live guard** — a quiet guard has a producer that could fill it, this had none. The census must be run per medium, since a survivor stops being reached silently: import graph (only its own witness test), `*_test.dag` discovery (that test is a PEER of the subject, not a guard over a survivor), workflow argv, Cargo `[[bin]]`, Rust (one string literal used as a test label, not a call), and roster rows (two `gunbc.non_fold_residue` frontier rows). **The second, costlier half — what the prose did while the model sat dead — is its own class and is rostered separately as `unbacked_execution_claim`;** what belongs HERE is only the consequence for this rule: a dead model is not harmless while it waits, because **a good model with no consumer is still residue (§6), and residue that describes itself in the present tense actively manufactures false premises.** Disposition landed: both modules and their witness test deleted, the two frontier rows removed, and every surviving citation of them rewritten to the past tense with the deletion and its date recorded — because a citation left naming a deleted symbol fakes a grep hit for the next reader.)", evidence: [] }

data total_at_the_level_examined_blind: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "total_at_the_level_examined_blind" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**total at the level examined, blind one level down** (a judgment is exhaustive over the type it matches and says nothing about the distinction that actually decides the outcome, which lives inside one of its arms. **The pairing is the whole content: the match is exhaustive AND wrong**, and the exhaustiveness is what hides it — there is no missing arm to report, no warning, nothing incomplete, so neither a reviewer reading the match nor a wildcard-free lens can see it. Specimen with a mutation receipt (gunbc.scm, 2026-08-22), **repaired on main 2026-08-25 by gunbc#8973 and kept in the past tense because the mechanism recurs while this instance does not**: a publication fold matched one outer arm carrying a JSON codec's entire refusal enum. It was total over that codec's refusal type, and the enum's arms carried three different publication remedies — a reader limitation, an absent-object problem over a well-formed document, and malformed bytes. Only the third may supersede a head slot, so the collapsed form let an OLDER READER OVERWRITE A NEWER WRITER'S DOCUMENT: data loss produced by the reader's own limitation, from a match that compiled and looked complete. Executed both ways — descending, four witnesses passed; collapsed, the witness driving all three remedies through the single outer arm went red; a temporary decode arm made the fold non-exhaustive; restored control passed. **None of this row's three cited symbols resolved on main, and they failed in two different ways** — measured across main's whole history, not just its head. `repository_load_disposition`, the function this row said performed the collapse, has NEVER existed as code on main: it appears only in this carrier and in the projection, and it names a declaration from the CLOSED attempt gunbc#8940, whose branch was retained in history and never landed. So the row cited a function that was fabricated on the day it was written. `RepositoryDecodeImageRefusal` and `ImageRefusal` were real — they landed with gunbc#8807 and gunbc#8840 and were deleted by gunbc#8965 on 2026-08-23 when the fused format was cut — so those two went stale one day later, by the ordinary route a citation rots when the thing it names is removed. The two halves matter separately because they have different remedies: a fabricated name is caught by resolving symbols before writing them, a deleted one only by a resolver that reruns. Either way a reader applying this entry's own recognition rule grepped for a match that was not there. That is §3's stale-citation class sitting inside the authority that names it, and it is recorded here rather than quietly deleted because a specimen whose symbols cannot be resolved is the failure this row exists to teach, one level up. **What landed is stronger than descending**, and the difference is the reusable part: the remedy vocabulary was hoisted into a module that names no format — `gunbc.scm.load_standing` `LoadStanding`, and each format now classifies its own refusals into it (`gunbc.scm.commit_closure_json_v2` `closure_document_load_standing`). Descending inside one codec's enum would have closed the collapse and left the consumer still matching on a format's vocabulary; hoisting leaves the consumer no format arms to collapse, so the next format is a new classifier rather than a new way to reintroduce this defect. **THE HOISTING WAS NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT, and this sentence is the fourth citation in this row to have gone stale.** It read that the permission was derived `by one total function`, naming `standing_may_supersede_generation` — a `LoadStanding -> Bool` carrying neither the slot the observation was made on nor the generation examined, so a caller could apply it to a slot the evidence never described or to a generation that had moved since it was read. gunbc#9258 deleted it and replaced the destination with `gunbc.scm.supersession` `supersede_head_slot`, where evidence is minted FROM the slot by `observe_generation` — a caller cannot state which generation it examined, only examine one — and the swap refuses unless the slot still holds it. The deletion left this sentence naming a declaration that no longer resolves, one day after it was written, which is the same rot this row already records twice above and is corrected here for the same reason. Second, independent specimen the same day, in the compiler itself: a census of the fourteen declared-type positions the grammar admits found five accepting a plain kernel value where a coproduct is declared — the judgment is present and total at the level it examines, and never descends. **The tell is a `_` or a bare binding in the arm that carries the payload**, and the test is not whether the match is complete but whether every cause it collapses shares one remedy; the fix is to descend so a new inner arm fails to compile HERE, rather than silently inheriting whichever remedy the outer arm happened to name.)", evidence: [] }

data execution_provenance_loss: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "execution_provenance_loss" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**execution-provenance loss** (a reported value is consumed as though an observation produced it, while the carrier holds no proof the observation path ran. **Distinct from state-space conflation, and the repair law is what separates them**: there the carrier cannot represent the distinction and the fix is to split the states; here the carrier already has the state — the consumer simply cannot tell whether it was *reached*, and the fix is to bind an execution receipt to the value. Three specimens in one night, all on main, none of them a missing variant. `known_red_held=206` is `36 held + 170 that RUNTIME-ERRORED`: the substrate splits those into distinct arms, so the states exist; what the quoted figure loses is *did the assertion run*, and an expected-red row that threw is not evidence the red is expected — it is a row whose assertion never executed. A floor whose `TerminalLedgerUnrenderable` count is `0` reads identically whether the ledger checks passed or preparation refused before a ledger existed. And a `.dag` board of `E0599=23 E0308=128` reads identically whether cargo ran or normalize refused upstream of it. **The receipt that makes this worth a row rather than a caution:** for three hours after #8976 put a §4c-illegal annotation inside a match body, the compiler refused at strict preparation while downstream measurements kept producing valid-looking values — one lane concluded a defect was closed, another concluded the same defect was still firing, both citing runs where it could not appear at all; three separate A/B comparisons reported perfect agreement, one because both arms were broken identically, one because a missing flag meant no arm executed, and one because the defect had been fixed between runs so both arms were the same bytes. Every one of those is downstream of a single fact: **a masked run and a clean run rendered identically.** Recognition rule: if a count of zero and an unreached stage produce the same output, the number is not an observation. The construction move, and it is stronger than naming known masks because it also forecloses the undiscovered ones: any stage capable of preventing a downstream observation from executing must participate in the observation carrier, so `refused before stage N` cannot inhabit the same carrier as `stage N executed with zero findings` — a known mask is a hole someone found, execution provenance is what stops an unfound hole from masquerading as a measurement.)", evidence: [] }

data remediation_mutated_view: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "remediation_mutated_view" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "remediation-mutated view (the standard response to a signal OVERWRITES the surface most readers query it through, so the population becomes unreconstructible AT THAT LEVEL and the reader concludes the evidence is gone. It usually is not: the defect is reading a MUTABLE PROJECTION as if it were the record, and a level below it there is generally an immutable one the same query reaches intact. Receipt, and the inversion belongs BESIDE it rather than after it: a fleet event terminated eight witnesses runs inside 49 seconds; every lane re-ran; a re-run REPLAYS the original merge ref and OVERWRITES the run-level conclusion, so queried through run conclusions the population was invisible -- zero of twenty-one -- while queried through the run's attempt records it was complete and exact hours later. Two independent reconstructions from the mutated view reported five and six of the eight: each correct, each incomplete, same cause -- so the mutated view fails SILENTLY and PARTIALLY, which is worse than failing empty. The rule is therefore NOT capture-or-lose-it: capture before remediating, or reconstruct from the immutable record, never from the mutable one. Stating only the first half is worse than saying nothing, because a lane that has already remediated reads it as a verdict that its evidence is gone and stops looking -- which is what produced the zero of twenty-one. Recognition rule: before concluding a population is unrecoverable, ask WHICH LEVEL you queried and whether the remedy WRITES to it.)", evidence: [] }

data diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "diagnostic name accurate about the situation, silent about the mechanism (a diagnostic's NAME describes the state it was raised in faithfully and says nothing about WHICH PREDICATE produced it, so a reader who treats the name as a cause builds a coherent story with no load-bearing contact with the code. Nothing in the name is wrong, which is why review reads past it. THREE RECEIPTS IN ONE NIGHT FROM THREE READERS, provenance stated per receipt because a row about untraced names must not itself rest on an untraced relay. FIRST, measured by this row's author, and it leads because the reader was the author of the story: rustc labels reading `expected Rc<Vector<i64>>, found String` at 49 sites plus 2 reversed, from which a representation fork was inferred -- the model type `Symbol` rendering as `String` in parameter position and a vector in field position -- and published. Measured: `Symbol` renders CONSISTENTLY as `String`, `Connective.Atom` carries `identity: String`, and the `.dag` is well-typed with the same declared type on both sides. The published mechanism was wrong; the label was a faithful description of a mismatch the type-checker had computed. AND THE CHECK FAILED THE SAME WAY THE READING DID, which is the most instructive part rather than decoration: a grep for the printed type name returned zero and zero was read as absence, when the emitted source spells `Rc<Vec<i64>>` and `lib.rs` carries `use im::Vector as Vec`, so rustc was printing the resolved underlying name. A name was read as a fact about the tree twice in one investigation, once in the diagnostic and once in the refutation of it. WHAT THE 49 SITES ACTUALLY ARE, and it is UNCHASED: `Rc<Vec<i64>>` is how `List<Int>` renders, so they read expected `List<Int>` found `String` -- an ordinary mechanism, and a real one. The amendment closed the wrong explanation, not the defect. SECOND, reported by quick-bat-372 and independently verified: `MethodNotFound` names the situation correctly and does not say which predicate gates it -- `method_existence_decision` gates on `kernel_profile_lookup`, so a fully resolved USER product with no kernel profile answers `MethodExistenceUndecided`. THIRD, same provenance: `FieldNotFound` names a concept never emitted for field ACCESS at all, established by exhausting its three construction sites -- two pattern bindings and one guarded by a record literal's field names. WHY IT EARNS A ROW: two of the three would have shipped as PERMANENTLY-GREEN WITNESS ARMS, an assertion that a wall fired over a wall that cannot fire for that input, which is section 4b's decoration-cited-as-coverage reached by a route no other row names -- and all three were caught by reading the PRODUCER rather than by review. WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: three instances in one night is a suggestive rate and not a base rate; all three surfaced while several lanes were unusually deep in diagnostic populations, so the frequency is a property of that work rather than of the corpus. Recognition rule: before treating a diagnostic name as a mechanism, read the function that produces it and find the predicate that gates it; if you cannot name that predicate, you have a situation and not a cause. A grep for the type name is a cheap first pass, not a sufficient check: rustc prints resolved names while source spells aliases, so `use X as Y` defeats the search in both directions and a zero can be confident and wrong. Read the producer. AMENDED 2026-08-28 -- THE PRODUCER'S OWN PROSE IS ALSO A NAME, so `read the producer` is necessary and NOT SUFFICIENT. The three receipts above are all DIAGNOSTIC names; the same failure reaches COMMENTS, and it is harder to see there because a comment is where a reader goes to ESCAPE the name. Two variants, and the ranking is the whole point. STALE prose is FALSIFIABLE BY READING: what it says is contradicted by the code as it stands, so a reader who checks the producer can always catch it. THAT IS NOT THE SAME AS SELF-CORRECTING, and an earlier revision of this row said it was -- `it rots when the code moves, and whoever next touches that code notices` -- which THIS ROW'S OWN SECOND RECEIPT REFUTES (review 57329): the deleted/still-here contradiction is LIVE in the tree today, and it was found by a reader who had gone there for an unrelated reason, NOT by the next person to touch the code. So the ranking below is about FALSIFIABILITY and not about correction rate. Stale prose persists exactly as long as nobody reads it, which is indefinitely; what makes it the lesser of the two is that a reader who does check is guaranteed to see the disagreement. WRONG-MECHANISM-CORRECT-CONCLUSION is NOT self-limiting: nothing it says is falsified by moving the code, so it survives every refactor, and the defect it names really existing READS AS CONFIRMATION of the explanation it gives -- load-bearing misinformation with a correct headline, routing every future reader to the wrong repair. RECEIPT, read independently by three readers rather than relayed: the comment above the floor's live-tree scan says its two computations `cannot agree except by coincidence` because one is a syntactic scan and the other falls through to `effect_reach_derived_reads_live_tree_for_entry`, a SEMANTIC reachability derivation -- locating the cause in the import graph. Read the control flow: `reads_live_tree_effective` calls `parse_entry_live_tree_disposition` first, and an UNDECLARED file reaches `Ok(declared.unwrap_or(true))`, so the function RETURNS before the derivation is consulted. The largest and simplest disagreement class is decided before the import graph is reached, and the mechanism the comment names has nothing to do with it. A SECOND RECEIPT FROM THE SAME PARAGRAPH, in the stale variant: it states the floor's copy is DELETED rather than reconciled, in the past tense, four lines above a section headed WHY IT IS STILL HERE explaining that the scan is live. RECOGNITION RULE, extending the one above rather than replacing it: THE CODE PATH IS THE FACT, and every sentence around it -- in a note, in a doc, or in the producer's own comment -- is commentary that may be stale or may be wrong about WHY. And having reached the producer, do not stop at the sentence that confirms your framing: this amendment exists because a reader quoted IT IS NO WALL from such a comment and dropped `and it is a partial classifier, not an enforcement` from four lines below, inside the same citation.)", evidence: [] }

data identity_absent_graph_traversal: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "identity_absent_graph_traversal" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "identity-absent graph traversal (a walk over a graph the COMPILER built re-enters shared nodes because it cannot carry a `visited` or memo key — the nodes have no identity the model is allowed to name — so the only two arms available locally are to PAY the re-entry, or to key on a substitute the substrate forbids. THE TRAP IS THAT THE ARMS DIFFER IN KIND AND THE CHEAP-LOOKING ONE IS THE UNSAFE ONE: paying is a cost, visible and bounded; keying on a substitute silently skips a DISTINCT node believed already visited, drops whatever that node contributed, and reports nothing. THE MECHANISM, structural and checkable by reading rather than by measurement: `v1.compiler.infer_emit_info` `collect_type_node_import_surface_names` recurses on BOTH `children` AND the `inferred` resolved node, so a shared type DAG is traversed as a tree and a node reachable by k paths is walked k times. The key does not exist. `std.occurrence_identity` `occurrence_identity_scope_law` names filename, SourceSpan, authored name, structural Node equality and content hash as FORBIDDEN identity inputs, and `NodeOccurrenceIdentity` `OccurrenceSynthetic` — which is what the compiler mints for a node no author wrote — carries no id at all, so every synthesised node compares equal to every other and a visited set built on it would skip the wrong one. The remaining candidate is host allocation identity, which exists only in the realization and not in the model. RUNG: OUTSIDE THE LADDER, and the earlier revision of this row said `mitigatable`, which was inflation of exactly the kind section 4b(1) names. The invalid state is writable, nothing refuses it, and its failure is a silent skip — section 4b puts silent wrongness outside the ladder rather than low on it. What that revision offered as the mitigation was that no author has yet needed such a traversal and that review might catch one; neither is containment by a total operation, a typed outcome, a bound, a rollback or an isolation, and no discriminating RED exists on any acceptance path, so no rung above the floor is claimable by executed evidence. ONE PARTIAL CONTAINMENT IS REAL AND DOES NOT LIFT THE CLASS: at the measured seam a dropped name reaches an emitted Rust crate, where rustc refuses it as E0422/E0425/E0433 far from the cause, and the regen byte-identity gate would show the drift. That is a property of THAT seam's consumer being a compiled artifact, not of the class — a traversal whose consumer is a verdict rather than a compilation has no such backstop — and section 4b sets a class's rung at the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths. CEILING: structural impossibility, and per section 4b(3) the trigger names the CAPABILITY rather than an artifact — an identity for synthesised occurrences, sufficient for a `visited` set over inferred type nodes to be authorable in `.dag` at all. Nothing less retires it: a faster traversal, a memo at one seam, or a counter measuring the amplification all leave the key absent and the unsafe arm equally reachable. An intermediate rung is available and is NOT claimed here because nothing implements it: a typed refusal at the traversal seam would make the class mechanically preventable while leaving the invalid state writable. THE ESCAPES THAT LOOK AVAILABLE AND ARE NOT, listed because this class is mostly discovered by trying them, and each was closed by EXECUTION rather than by argument — deleting the producer, replacing it with the cheaper sub-producers beside it, reading `TypeSummary.field_import_surface_names` instead (which is CIRCULAR, being produced BY this walk in `build_field_type_map`, and answers a different relation), and hoisting the work earlier (there is nothing to hoist: each item belongs to one module and each module is emitted once). Two further hypotheses about the COST were falsified the same way and are worth not repeating: the list-copy lowering, and the match-scrutinee deep clone. The measured populations, the amplification, the per-escape figures and the two falsifications are recorded once, dated, with their method and their non-enrollment stated, in the plan document `emit-type-surface-traversal-cost`, which is bound to this traversal and its two consumers in `gunbc.doc_graph_roots` and retires when they move; they are deliberately not transcribed here, because a number copied into a roster row is the positional-citation failure one entry up wearing different clothes. RECOGNITION RULE: when you reach for a visited or memo key over a graph the compiler built rather than the author wrote, enumerate the keys available to you; if every candidate is one the identity authority forbids, the deficit is upstream in the identity algebra and NEITHER local arm is a repair — the amplification is the symptom and the missing identity is the class.)", evidence: [] }

data generated_binding_shadows_bare_render: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "generated_binding_shadows_bare_render" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "generated binding shadows a bare render (an emitter that renders a name by SPELLING while a different generator in the same emission adds a binding for that spelling — a use line, an alias, a prelude — composes into a silent rebinding: each generator is locally correct and the artifact realizes the wrong declaration, with the diagnostic landing at the CONSUMER of the emitted file, far from either producer. SPECIMEN (XL-0T, PR #9720): modules carrying kernel-String data rows plus transitively referenced structural v2.std.text signatures got a generated v2_std_text String use line; the six type renderers' is_host_text_carrier_type short-circuit rendered those kernel rows as the bare spelling String, which the use line then bound to the structural carrier — 160 E0308 rows in one closure, none of them at a line either generator wrote. FIX SHAPE, and the reason this is a class rather than a bug: render by DECLARATION IDENTITY, and give the non-local realization the GROUNDING spelling no local binding can shadow (std::string::String), keeping the bare reference spelling only for the declaration the module's own binding names — the same two-spelling split std.coercion TypeCheckpoint already carries as reference_base vs grounding_base. RECOGNITION RULE: whenever one generator emits a binding for a spelling and any other render site emits that spelling bare, ask which declaration each intends; if they can differ, the bare render needs the grounding spelling or the identity key, because 'correct at every generator' does not compose to 'correct in the artifact'.)", evidence: [] }

data resolved_reference_outside_execution_closure: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "resolved_reference_outside_execution_closure" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "resolved reference outside the execution closure (an Accepted program contains a resolved call edge whose target declaration's OWNER MODULE is absent from the module closure loaded for that execution, so resolve and typecheck both report success and the program dies at run time. MECHANISM: bare-reference resolution consults a declaration population BROADER than the explicit-import closure from which the runtime index is built, so the two phases answer to two different denominators and nothing joins them. THE SPECIMEN, found by execution rather than by reading, and recorded here because a class whose only evidence is an argument is not a class: three witness files -- test.claim.spark_serving_observe_witness_test, test.claim.spark_serving_model_store_witness_test and test.claim.spark.spark_cell_role_retirement_witness_test -- CALLED hermetic_fixture_provenance with no import of the module declaring it. Resolve accepted them, typecheck accepted them, and every claim reaching the call refused at run time with `no declaration named hermetic_fixture_provenance in this execution's loaded index (searched the modules loaded for this run; the name may be declared in a module this run did not load)`. The positive control is exact and cheap: adding the one import admits and executes the UNCHANGED call. WHY IT IS NOT ONE OF THE ROWS BESIDE IT, checked rather than assumed. It is not `reachability_read_as_occupancy`: nothing here mistook reachability for occupancy, and the declaration is genuinely reachable AND genuinely resolved. It is not `identity_absent_graph_traversal`: the declaration exists, has an identity, and that identity is found -- what is absent is the RELATION from the resolved target to the modules the execution loader materializes. This is the missing agreement between two denominators, not the occupancy of either one. RUNG, SCOPED AND NOT INFLATED: mitigatable at the source-to-witness-execution grain the specimen demonstrates, where the runtime refusal is typed, located and loud. THE LANGUAGE-WIDE RUNG IS NOT CLAIMED and the reason is a control that has not been run: place an observable EFFECT before the unloaded call and see whether it executes before the refusal. If it does, the class is not mitigatable at that grain without preflight or rollback, because the failure arrives after the program has already acted. Until that control answers, this row's rung is a statement about witness execution and nothing wider. CEILING: structurally guaranteed rather than structurally impossible -- source can still omit an import, so the state stays writable, but no Accepted program should contain the edge. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the CAPABILITY: acceptance joins every resolved declaration identity's owner module to the exact local/import/prelude closure used to construct the execution index. DISCRIMINATING RED: a bare call with no explicit import is refused BEFORE Accepted, not after. POSITIVE CONTROL: adding the exact import admits and executes the unchanged call. REPAIR DIRECTION, and the wrong arm is the tempting one: constrain RESOLUTION and ADMISSION. Do NOT widen the runtime loader to chase bare-reference edges -- that converts undeclared dependencies into implicit imports and dissolves the direct-import law to make a symptom go away, which is the absorbing-fallback shape applied to a language rule. Both phases must consume ONE admitted dependency closure. RECOGNITION RULE: a green typecheck is not evidence that a call can execute unless the phase that accepted it and the phase that will run it were answering to the same module set; when a name resolves but its module is not imported, ask which denominator each phase used before concluding the reference is sound.)", evidence: [] }

data surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**surface shorthand preempts resolved identity** (a semantic consumer dispatches on a raw lexeme after resolution has already named its declaration, so a declared constructor is reinterpreted as a host sentinel or primitive. Recognition rule: once a node carries a binding/declaration identity, value construction must be total over that identity; spelling may be interpreted only on an explicitly unresolved shorthand arm. Specimen gunbc#9741: bare and imported `None` became host `Null` while qualified `Diagnostics.None {}` became a `Variant`; a single-frame comparison hid the fork. This is not hollow alias: the binding is grounded and present, then discarded downstream. It is also separate from the per-frame symbol-ordinal defect: that defect corrupted lexeme identity while crossing frames, whereas this one ignores an identity already supplied at one construction site. Next-rung trigger: host literals and intentional primitive representations are typed parser/resolver constructions, and evaluator value construction is total over every resolved binding with no raw-spelling arm able to override it.)", evidence: [] }

data meaning_fork: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "meaning_fork" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**meaning fork** (one scoped name carries more than one material semantic referent under hidden state; accuracy of meaning applies to terms in every layer, and for a contract-bearing name, differences in obligations, quality floor, refusal behavior, billing consequence, or remedy establish different referents. The subject is scoped: the key is the naming surface, the visible name, and the declared effective version or epoch — the same spelling in two explicitly distinct scopes or across a declared version transition is legitimate reuse, not a fork. Recognition rule: hold that key constant and vary the hidden state; if the material semantic referent changes without a distinct variant name, the name has forked — for a contract-bearing name, a change in obligations, quality floor, refusal behavior, billing consequence, or remedy is sufficient evidence of that change. This is the one-name/two-meanings dual of nicknaming.)", evidence: [] }

data externalized_degradation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "externalized_degradation" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**externalized degradation** (an actor that accepted an obligation or risk, or caused a cost, silently shifts the resulting burden to another principal while preserving the apparent name, price, or contract. Recognition rule: identify the accepted obligation or causal responsibility, trigger the adverse state, and follow who bears the marginal burden; if another principal's burden rises while the responsible actor neither absorbs it through its reserve, refusal, or remedy path nor exposes a separately named, priced, and refusable transfer, the burden was externalized. A disclosed, refusable allocation agreed before contract formation is the transfer arm; an undisclosed or unilateral later shift is refused. The honest arms are absorb-and-reserve or separately name-and-price the transfer.)", evidence: [] }

data mistyped_body_radiates_nonlocal_diagnostics: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "mistyped_body_radiates_nonlocal_diagnostics" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "mistyped body radiates nonlocal phantom diagnostics (LAYER, stated first because carrying this finding across it inverts its meaning: the producer is the .dag COMPILER diagnosing .dag SOURCE -- the interpreter/type-check path behind gunbc compile and the --required-regen self-compile -- NOT rustc diagnosing emitted Rust; nothing here supports discounting any rustc-diagnostic census. THE FAILURE: a type error confined to ONE module-scope fn body does not refuse at that body with a located diagnostic; it radiates as a fabricated population of field-access diagnostics at UNRELATED modules, so the line stops pointing at the wrong factories. SPECIMEN (XL-0T, PR #9720): one fn added to v1.compiler.infer_env whose body held NonEmptyStr-as-String casts in comparison/argument position plus a FilePath-vs-String if-arm mismatch produced ~700 advisory `no field 'source_indices' on type 'TypeEnv'` rows across compile.dag, 05_emit_rust.dag and 04_resolve.dag -- modules that were fine -- and blocked required-regen, which printed 12 of them and never named the defective body. A reader begins repairing the wrong files; that misdirection, not the volume, is the harm (section 5: every refusal typed AND located). FOUR-POINT DISCRIMINATOR, one instrument (entry-scoped compile of src/v1/compile.dag, counting the diagnostic): full mistyped body 774; same signature with trivial body 0; casts hoisted into let bindings with structure kept 0 phantoms plus ONE real correctly-located error at the fn's own line; that real error fixed rc=0. The series also refuted the name-capture hypothesis for this specimen, since the fn name was held constant across all four points. RUNG: outside the ladder at the diagnosed-population grain -- the fabricated rows ARE silent wrongness about the modules they name -- while the run-level verdict stayed mitigatable (the compile did refuse; it refused about the wrong subject). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- an expression-position type failure inside a body refuses AT that body before any cross-module field-access checking consumes the poisoned inference state. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: body-local type-error containment, sufficient that no diagnostic about module B can be produced by a type defect whose every construction site is inside module A. RECOGNITION RULE: when N same-shaped field/type diagnostics appear at unrelated sites immediately after adding or editing ONE declaration, suspect that declaration's body typing before believing any named site; trivial-body the new declaration as the two-minute discriminator, and hoist casts out of comparison/argument position into let bindings to recover the located refusal.)", evidence: [] }

data mitigation_injected_where_judgment_declined: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "mitigation_injected_where_judgment_declined" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**mitigation injected where the judgment declined** (a downstream stage injects a RUNTIME mitigation at exactly the seam where an upstream judgment returned Undecidable, so a 4b rung-1 fallback comes to occupy the place the wall belongs and the declined seam stops looking empty. **THE LOAD-BEARING HALF IS WHAT THE COINCIDENCE PROVES ABOUT THE DECLINE**: an Undecidable verdict is normally read as benign conservatism — the facts did not settle it, nothing is claimed, no harm asserted — and a mitigation landing on the SAME LINE is the first evidence that a real defect was sitting under that silence. The decline is therefore load-bearing AT THIS SITE, which refutes reading an Undecidable verdict as evidence of ABSENCE. **IT DOES NOT MAKE THE DECLINE CENSUS PREDICTIVE, and this row carries that limit because the author first wrote the stronger claim and then measured it FALSE** on the same board that produced the specimen: 259 of 272 declines sit in modules with ZERO blocking errors, only 6 of 28 decline-bearing modules carry any error at all, and the module holding 42 of the 63 errors carries ZERO declines and 105 ACCEPTS. Declines and defects are ANTI-CORRELATED at module grain, so this specimen is ONE co-location out of 272 and a walk of the decline census would be walking sites that are ~95% empty. The class is about a mitigation landing on a declined seam; it is NOT a claim that declines predict defects. Distinct from `absorbing_fallback`, whose arm WIDENS to a superset and destroys the precise mechanism s signal; here the arm NARROWS to a panic and destroys nothing except the evidence that a judgment was owed. Distinct from `reflection_evidence_structural_proof`, which mistakes an observation for a proof; here nothing is proven or observed — a decision was declined and then papered. Specimen with a receipt, measured 2026-09-01 on gunbc 0e8c49d and unrepaired at authoring: `v2.std.diagnostic outcome_accepted` is `fn outcome_accepted<T>(value: T) -> Outcome<T>` with T FREE; `v2.compiler.07_target_carriers target_fidelity_quotient_optional` declares `-> Outcome<Optional<Node>>` and calls `outcome_accepted(Present \{ value: child \})`, so T instantiates to `Optional<Node>` and THE SOURCE IS CORRECT. The Rust emitter nonetheless rendered `Some(child).expect(\"fail-closed: an optional value flowed into non-optional parameter 0 of outcome_accepted (empty Optional at runtime)\")`. FOUR DEFECTS IN ONE LINE: it fires on a GENERIC formal where `Optional<Node>` is a legitimate instantiation rather than a cardinality escape, so the check does not know T is free; it substitutes a runtime panic for a compile-time judgment; the emitted code does NOT typecheck anyway (rustc E0308 expected `Option<Rc<Node>>` found `Rc<Node>`), so the mitigation buys nothing while standing where the wall belongs; and its own panic string calls itself `fail-closed`, which is 4b rung inflation inside a string literal — a diagnostic naming the discipline it violates is worse than a silent one because it will be cited as evidence the discipline holds. The coincidence that makes this a class and not a bug: `v1.compiler.infer declared_type_inhabitance` returned InhabitanceUndecidable\{UndecidableOptionalCarrier\} at that module s ONLY optional-carrier decline, 07_target_carriers.dag:128:24 parameter `value` — the same line the emitter mitigated. RUNG FOUND AT: 1 (mitigatable) on a seam whose CEILING is 3 (structurally guaranteed), since generic-formal instantiation is decidable from modeled structure. CONSEQUENCE WITH ITS OWN TRIGGER, deliberately NOT folded into this row: wiring the optional-carrier judgment is argued by this specimen but is a separate change, and its trigger is a producer at that seam that can distinguish a FREE type variable from a declared non-optional formal — until that exists the judgment would decline for the same reason it declines today.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }

data instrument_output_read_as_subject_content: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "instrument_output_read_as_subject_content" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**instrument output read as subject content** (a consumer derives a SET from a report whose completeness is a property of the REPORTING TOOL rather than of the subject. **The boundary against `execution_provenance_loss` is the whole justification for a separate row, because the two look identical at the call site and have opposite repairs**: there a value is consumed as though an observation produced it while nothing proves the observation path RAN, and the fix is to bind an execution receipt; here the observation ran and reported FAITHFULLY — the instrument answered its own question correctly — and what is wrong is that its output was complete for the REPORTER s purpose and was read as complete for the CONSUMER s. Provenance is intact; the SUBJECT is substituted, so no receipt binding can detect it and the repair is instead to derive the set from the subject itself. Distinct from `total_at_the_level_examined_blind`, which is a judgment shape (a match total over the type it examines, blind inside an arm), and from `reachability_read_as_occupancy`, which asks whether a quiet guard should exist; this is neither a match nor a guard. Specimen with a receipt, repaired on main by gunbc#9829: the required floor asked `extdeps.git` `git.Core.DiffUnified0` (`git diff -U0 <range>`) which lines a change touched, and `floor_diff_edits_from_line_ranges` attributed those lines to enclosing declarations to decide which witness identities the change established. Git prints only the hunks that DIFFER, so on a rename it prints the module line and whatever else moved — while every identity at the destination is a newly qualified `module.function` that has never executed under that spelling, because the authored module name moved with the file. **THE REASON IT SURVIVED IS THAT THE TWO ANSWERS COINCIDE BY ACCIDENT IN THE COMMON CASE**: for a wholly-added file every line is a `+` line, so line attribution reaches every declaration and the defect is invisible; it appears only when the instrument gets TERSE, which rename detection is. Measured over the window reachable in a shallow session clone — a floor on the population, not the population, since older renames are unmeasured — 8 of 8 rename-destination `.dag` files carrying test decls were under-enrolled and at least 87 of their 103 identities were never selected; a PURE MOVE with no content edit enrolled NOTHING. It was not merely a reporting gap: changed-witness membership is what OVERRIDES the cost-debt withhold and the outside-gate suppression, so the same miss on a rostered identity is a silent decline of a witness whose author is present, which is the state `v2.workflow.floor_changed_witness` `changed_witness_execution_standing` exists to red. The repair derives the set from the subject: a path `parse_unified_diff_added_paths` already rules new-at-path contributes the declarations THE FILE ITSELF PARSES TO, bounded to that file s own decl list and never the corpus, so it is the precise answer rather than an absorbing widen. Its discriminating red is `rename_destination_enrolls_every_test_decl_not_only_the_diff_touched_one`, which feeds the specimen s verbatim diff and FAILS when the rule is disabled, paired with `in_place_modify_enrolls_only_the_touched_test_decl`, which passes under both states so the first cannot be satisfied by widening. **Recognition rule, and it predicts well beyond git**: whenever a set is read out of a tool s output, ask whether that tool promised completeness over YOUR question or over its own — `--stat`, any de-duplicating or truncating reporter, and any porcelain that elides for human brevity all report faithfully and none of them promise the consumer s set. **Its near twin is `executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing`, approached from the other side**: there the satisfied signal is EXECUTION -- the conjunct genuinely runs and is genuinely gated on -- while here it is COMPLETENESS RELATIVE TO THE REPORTER, which is why this class is not a reachability problem and looking for an unexecuted path finds everything healthy. In both, the axis the diligent reader checks already reads green, and checking it harder returns the same green.)**THREE RECEIPTS FROM ONE SESSION (2026-09-01, XL-0T), ALL READ AS A GREEN OR A ZERO, AND THE THIRD IS THE ONE THIS ROW DID NOT ALREADY COVER.** (1) A remote build read as `ctrl-build --remote -- cargo check ... | tail -8`: the pipeline exits with TAIL's status, so it is zero whatever the compiler said, and the eight-line window it keeps is executor cleanup chatter carrying no line capable of holding an error. Absence of an error read as success AFTER every line that could contradict it had been discarded. (2) A regeneration wrapped in `/usr/bin/time -v` in a container where that binary does not exist: bash died at the wrapper, exited ZERO, the program never ran, and the subsequent `git diff` was EMPTY -- which reads exactly as `no drift`, the answer that would have RETRACTED a correct finding already registered as a prediction. (3) The floor's `[over-cost]` listing, from which order statistics were computed and reported as a distribution -- `median 390ms, p95 418ms, a dense band at 78-84% of the 500ms ceiling`. The listing is not the population and SAYS SO IN ITS OWN LAST LINE: `and 260 further row(s) over the 100ms line, not printed ... this list is the 25 most expensive, ranked on the declared cost basis`, against `over_cost_line_diagnostic=285`. The true shape was the OPPOSITE: one outlier 73ms clear of the field (501 refused, runner-up 428, the remaining 260 all at or below 337ms), and the gap claimed to be empty had a row sitting in it. **WHY THE THIRD IS THE SEVERE ONE AND WHY IT NEEDED THIS ROW RATHER THAN A NEW ONE.** The first two were filters the CONSUMER wrote, and the standing guard -- select on the result pattern, never on position -- catches both. The third was truncation the PRODUCER performed, for its own readability, and DECLARED IN BAND; there was no consumer-authored `head -N` to notice, so the guard does not fire and diligence along it returns green. That is this class exactly: the report was complete for the REPORTER's purpose and read as complete for the CONSUMER's, with provenance intact and the subject substituted. **GENERAL FORM, which extends the recognition rule above from completeness to ORDER: a ranked list is a VIEW, and a view's order statistics are not the population's.** A median or a percentile computed over a top-K is an order statistic of a truncated tail; it carries no trace of the truncation, it has the same shape and units as the real thing, and it is therefore strictly more dangerous than a wrong count, which at least invites the question `out of how many`. So: before computing ANY statistic over a tool's lines, find the producer's own statement of what it printed -- a `N further rows`, a `top K`, a `ranked by`, a total beside the listing -- and where the producer names a fuller artifact, THAT is the population and the log is a preview. **THE HARM WAS NOT TO THE AUTHOR'S OWN CONCLUSIONS**, which is what separates this receipt from the two beside it: the wrong distribution had already been relayed to a lane authoring a DECLARED RUNG DROP whose population is stated as a function of headroom against observed inflation. At the measured 8-11% a row tips only from a baseline near 450ms, so the true at-risk population was ONE row -- the 501 itself -- and the relayed number would have made it twenty-five, inside the one artifact whose entire value is that its population is honest, and in the direction that makes a class look larger, which is the direction nobody audits.)**FOURTH RECEIPT, AND IT WAS FOUND INSIDE THE INSTRUMENT BEING USED TO WRITE THE REPORT ABOUT THIS CLASS (2026-09-01, same session).** `v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census`, run over 1320 `.dag` files, prints `subjects=1320` -- and 1320 is the count of FILES INGESTED, not modules CENSUSED. Only 845 modules produce rows; 475, or 36 percent, are silently omitted. The omissions are not obscure: `v2.compiler.parse` is absent, and `v2.std.compilers.lexing` is absent while its siblings `body_lowering`, `cli_surface`, `sugar` and `semantic_decl_emission` are all present, so it is neither a test-module filter nor obvious unreachability. A consumer reads `subjects=` as coverage, which is this class exactly: the count is complete for the REPORTER's purpose -- files it accepted -- and was read as complete for the CONSUMER's, which is modules it examined. **THE SELECTION RULE IS DELIBERATELY NOT STATED HERE**: it was not determined, and guessing it would put a fabricated mechanism in a ledger row, which is worse than an incomplete one. **WHAT IT COST, MEASURED RATHER THAN IMAGINED.** A fixture authored specifically to settle an unrelated question landed in the omitted 475 and produced ZERO rows -- including its own positive control. Its emptiness was exactly what the hypothesis under test predicted, so without the control it would have been reported as confirmation of a hypothesis on evidence containing none. The absence-versus-zero distinction this class names reproduced itself INSIDE the test built to settle it, which is the practical lesson: catching a pattern does not inoculate you against it, and the exposure is highest immediately after being careful. **THE RESOLUTION-AXIS FORM, MEASURED 2026-09-02 (bold-stag-665 specimen i, bold-carp-449 specimen ii): THE INSTRUMENT RESOLVED THE REFERENCE TO SOMETHING ADJACENT TO THE INTENDED SUBJECT AND REPORTED FAITHFULLY ABOUT WHAT IT RESOLVED TO.** The adjacency is a different VERSION or a different SPELLING; and NEITHER specimen here is temporal, which is the clearest statement of where the boundary against `stable_citation_mutable_referent` falls: the time axis went there with the attempt case. Specimen (i) reads one fixed branch against one fixed main, specimen (ii) one fixed tree against one fixed staged copy at one instant; both would answer identically tomorrow, and their adjacency is ANCESTRY and NAMING rather than time.** The forms above substitute WHAT the instrument covered for what the subject contains. Here the instrument resolves to a DIFFERENT VERSION or a DIFFERENT NAME for the same subject, and its answer carries no mark of having done so. **THE TEETH: EVERY RUNG RETURNS A WELL-FORMED PLAUSIBLE ANSWER RATHER THAN AN ERROR, SO THE WRONG ANSWER DOES NOT LOOK LIKE A FAILURE, IT LOOKS LIKE DATA.** `+76/-31` reads as a change; `five functions missing` reads as a deletion. Each arrives with a mechanism ready to explain it, which is what makes it persuasive rather than merely wrong. **THE LADDER, WHICH IS THE TRANSFERABLE PART -- EVERY RUNG BUT THE LAST IS POSITIONAL, AND EACH GOES RED FOR A DIFFERENT IRRELEVANT REASON:** line-diff is red on a REWRITE; identifier-diff is red on a RENAME; concept-mapping is the only test that decides. Identifier-absence is not the cure for line-absence, it is the SAME positional test one level up -- **absence of a NAME is not absence of a CAPABILITY, and only the second is a loss.** **SPECIMEN (i), the line rung -- an ancestry the merge destroyed.** Under SQUASH merge the squashed commit is not an ancestor of the branch, so `git diff --stat origin/main...origin/session/<branch>` re-renders ALREADY-LANDED work as unlanded: gunbc#10100 rendered 3 files, +76/-31, for content wholly present on main. The deciding test is content -- `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main <branch>` against `git rev-parse origin/main^\{tree\}`, identical shas meaning the merge is a no-op. A peer hit the same rendering on gunbc#9995 and reported a no-op as a 5313-line partial revert. **SPECIMEN (ii), the identifier rung -- a rename read as a deletion (bold-carp-449, whose session is archived, so this row is the specimen's only durable form).** A worktree held staged residue: `prose_citation_census.dag` staged at 576 lines against main's 802, with 56 lines staged-only; its witness test 245 against 461, 23 staged-only. The first read reasoned from SIZE to CONTENT -- main is 226 lines further along, so these must be earlier phrasings -- which is unsound because a file can grow 226 lines while independently dropping 56. The token test that replaced it pulled distinctive identifiers from each staged-only line and grepped main: 25 of 56 and 15 of 23 were ABSENT, INCLUDING FIVE WHOLE FUNCTIONS AND FOUR WHOLE TEST FNS, which reads as a substantial deletion. IT WAS ENTIRELY RENAMES. Every construct exists in main under different wording -- staged `cross_file: Bool` became main's `ProseCitationLocality = InRetiringFile | InAnotherFile | RetiringFileAmbiguous`; `prose_citation_baseline_row` became `prose_citation_baseline_reading`; `a_citation_in_the_retiring_file_is_not_cross_file` became `a_citation_in_the_retiring_file_is_local_to_it`. **TWO WERE STRICTLY STRONGER IN MAIN** -- the `Bool` became a three-arm coproduct expressing the several-paths case a `Bool` cannot, and main carried an entire second axis the staged copy lacked -- so the instrument reported a LOSS where the truth was a GAIN. What settled it was reading main's type and function definitions and asking which CONCEPT each staged construct maps onto. **RECOGNITION RULE, COVERING BOTH, AND IT MUST FIRE AT READING TIME RATHER THAN AT RETRACTION TIME:** before reading an ABSENCE or a DIFFERENCE as a fact about the subject, establish that the instrument resolved to the subject you meant -- the same version, the same concept -- because every cheap test available resolves to something adjacent and says nothing about having done so. **THE NEAR-MISSES ARE PART OF THE RECEIPT AND ARE WHY THIS IS FILED AT ALL.** Neither reached a wrong decision and each halted one step short: the no-op diffstat was settled by tree sha before anyone acted on reopening; the deletion was settled by concept-mapping before anything was restored. A class whose specimens each halt one step from harm names exactly what the recognition rule has to beat. **BOUNDED AGAINST THE FOUR NEAREST ROWS, and these boundaries are the justification for a form here rather than a fourth authority.** `receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of` is a RECEIPT that was valid and EXPIRED when its base moved, repaired by re-deriving against the new base; here nothing expires -- every reading is live and true of its own subject, and the defect is manufactured by JOINING two of them. `positional_citation` is an authored HANDLE that decays and fails by matching zero; here the handle keeps matching perfectly and returns a confident answer about something else -- and note the sharper relation, that specimen (ii) shows an identifier GREP is itself a positional test, so `positional_citation` names the decaying-pointer half while this row names the unsound-absence half. `execution_provenance_loss` asks whether the observation ran; here it ran and reported faithfully. `stable_citation_mutable_referent` is the boundary that decides what this form does NOT carry, and it is the sharpest of the four because the two look identical at the call site -- both are a confident well-formed answer about a subject the reader did not mean. **THE TEST THAT SEPARATES THEM IS NOT WHETHER THEY FEEL DIFFERENT BUT WHETHER THE REPAIRS TRANSFER: does a reader who correctly diagnoses one perform the RIGHT FIX for the other? No -- and each fix is actively wrong applied to the other, which is why this is a boundary rather than a framing.** There the identifier resolves to its own correct subject and the WORLD replaces the content served underneath it, so the reader's test was right and re-reading CONFIRMS the wrong answer; the repair is to pin the citation to something that cannot be replaced -- an attempt number, a sha, an immutable artifact. Here nothing is replaced and nothing moves: every reading is live and would be identical tomorrow, the reader's TEST is what resolved to the neighbouring question, and the repair is to change the test rather than the citation -- line-diff to identifier-diff to concept-mapping. Crossed over, both fixes fail: PIN a squash-merge two-dot and you have pinned a merge base that was always the wrong one, and CONCEPT-MAP two attempts and you conclude a migration is real without ever establishing the two readings share a subject. That is why the ATTEMPT axis is not in the list above and why the job-id receipt is filed there rather than here: an attempt genuinely was replaced, which is that class and not this one. All of them share provenance-intact subject substitution, which is why this is a FORM of this row and not a new one.) **RECEIPT (1) IS NOW MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSERTED, AND A NAMED TOOL IS CLEARED BY THE SAME CONTROL (2026-09-03, vivid-ibex-751).** Receipt (1) above states that a `| tail` pipeline exits with tail's status; it was true and it was prose. The discriminating pair, one line apart on one command: `ctrl-build --local -- cargo check -Z definitely-not-a-real-flag 2>&1 | tail -2` reports rc=0 with PIPESTATUS[0]=101, and the same command unpiped reports rc=101. A positive control and a red on a fixed subject, so the mechanism is now established by execution rather than by description. THE EXONERATION IS THE PART THIS ROW DID NOT CARRY. On the strength of the piped reading, `ctrl-build` was reported to a manager as a fleet-wide false-green generator -- a build wrapper whose exit status did not reflect its compile -- and was one message from being filed as a defect against a shared tool. THE UNPIPED CONTROL CLEARS IT: the wrapper reports the compile's status correctly and always did. The 0 was tail succeeding at printing the failure. That is the first receipt here where a named component was ACCUSED and then CLEARED, and it is recorded beside the accusation deliberately: fabricated debt against a blameless component costs more than the misreading that produced it, because it sends every other lane hunting in the wrong place, and a clearing that lives only in a chat thread does not reach them. The three remedies are not interchangeable: `set -o pipefail` and reading PIPESTATUS[0] both work and both require the author to remember at the exact moment they are not thinking about it; NOT PIPING THE THING WHOSE STATUS YOU NEED is the only unconditionally safe one. AND THE MISATTRIBUTION SURVIVED A WRITTEN NOTE OF THIS EXACT FACT. What stopped it was being asked to file the row: a failure-mode row must name its DISTINGUISHING FACT, and that is the one field that cannot be filled without measuring. **FIFTH RECEIPT, AND IT IS THE SECOND HIT ON THE SAME ARTIFACT (2026-09-03, calm-boar-314).** The required-floor log prints, for a witness interrupted by the cpu deadline, both `cpu_at_least=503ms/500ms` and the sentence `interrupt_point=503ms is where the poll observed the ceiling; every interrupted row reports approximately whatever ceiling interrupted it, so that figure is a property of the BUDGET and not of this row -- do not compare it with the budget or with another row's`, together with `ABOVE 500ms with NO UPPER BOUND (a bound, not a near miss: it is wrong as a cost by an unbounded amount, always low)`. A 926KB log was downloaded, grepped for the blocking populations, and three figures transcribed into margins of 0.6, 0.8 and 5.4 percent against a 500ms ceiling -- percentages computed against a sentence forbidding that comparison, printed on the same line as the figures. Only one of the three was a margin at all; the other two were interrupt points, and a cost unbounded above is INDISTINGUISHABLE THROUGH THIS INSTRUMENT from the step change the reading was offered to rule out, so the conclusion was not merely unsupported but unfalsifiable from the evidence held. **What makes it the second hit rather than a first: the same log's `[over-cost]` listing had already produced the truncated-order-statistics receipt above, so this artifact had already taught this lesson once, to the same reader, on the same file.** The structural argument the margins were decorating -- that a prose string in a ledger row has no path to the CPU cost of an emit test -- was sound alone, which is the harm: the numbers added the appearance of a measured claim to an argument that was already better without them. **WHAT THE TWO 2026-09-03 RECEIPTS SAY TOGETHER, co-signed by both lanes and stated in the form that survives the difference between them.** Two lanes, one hour, unrelated subjects, both reading a STATUS or a FIGURE as a fact about a subject the instrument was not reporting on -- and in the one case where a guard rail WAS printed in band, it did not hold. The narrowing is deliberate and was calm-boar-314's: the strong form -- that both read past an in-band guard rail -- is true of the margin receipt, whose forbidding sentence sat on the line the figures were extracted from, and FALSE of the status receipt, where the `tail` window had already DISCARDED every contradicting line. Nothing was there to read past; the guard rail was absent, not ignored. This row already keeps those apart as consumer-authored versus producer-declared truncation, and the co-signed claim is written so it does not need the weaker case to be stronger than it was. **SECOND SPECIMEN, AND IT MOVES THE REPORTER PROPERTY FROM SCOPE TO VINTAGE** (eager-pike-541, 2026-09-03). The instrument was the locally built `claim_executor`; it ran and answered its own question correctly, and its question was asked under the semantics of an OLDER corpus than the tree under test. After merging a main that had added new compiler seed files, the floor refused with `function parsed_import_statements not found in scope` before any claim executed and reported zero passing claims, whose surface reading is that the branch broke the corpus. It had not; the binary predated the function. THE COMPLETENESS AXIS IS THE SAME AND THE REPORTER PROPERTY IS DIFFERENT -- above, the report was complete for the reporter's SCOPE rather than the subject's; here it was correct for the reporter's VERSION rather than the subject's, which is why this is a specimen of this row rather than a new one. **THE RECEIPT IS THE DESTRUCTIVE ARM**: the same stale binary, asked to regenerate projections, DELETED three live rows from DESIGN.md -- a merged rung drop and two failure modes belonging to other lanes -- while the .dag authorities still declared all three, because a projection generated by an instrument that cannot see a row renders its absence as authoritative. THE GENERATED-ARTIFACT GATE CANNOT CATCH THIS: it compares the projection to its authority and reports clean once both sides agree on the loss, so only the instrument's vintage separates a projection from a deletion. The operative rule is that a local refusal measured against a MOVED main is not evidence about the branch until the instrument is rebuilt against that main.", evidence: [] }
data one_refusal_two_destinations: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "one_refusal_two_destinations" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**one refusal, two destinations, remedy misdirected** (a single refusal at a single source column emits two rows naming DIFFERENT expected types, because two producers resolve the same declared spelling in different environments. The reader repairs from the row that names the parameter -- and that is the row the checker did NOT refuse on. **THE SYMPTOM IS THE RECOGNITION RULE, NOT THE CAUSE**: what a debugging author encounters is one column, two rows, two expected types; the instruction that saves them is DO NOT REPAIR FROM THE INHABITANCE ROW -- the compat row is what refused. Specimen, measured 2026-09-01 on gunbc c0a378c07be by calm-boar-314 and bold-carp-449 independently, on two binaries and two phases (`gunbc compile` emit-stage refusal and `gunbc run` entry-resolve), unrepaired at authoring. A module declaring `type String = FreeMonoid<Char>` and `fn takes_bare(s: String) -> Int`, called from a foreign module that IMPORTS the function, with a deliberately wrong `Int` actual so the diagnostic must name its destination, refuses with: `type mismatch: expected 'Primitive(String)', got 'Primitive(Int)'` AND `value does not inhabit its declared type at the direct call argument for parameter 's': declared 'Node(String<Product(Char)>)', produced 'Primitive(Int)'`. THE TWO PRODUCERS, read from source rather than inferred from message shape: `v1.compiler.infer direct_call_arg_mismatch_diags` renders the compat row from the formal as the CALLER environment resolves it, and `v1.compiler.infer declared_type_obligation_diags` renders the inhabitance row from `obligation.declared` through `declared_type_inhabitance`. Both reach `type_mismatch_error` and `DeclaredTypeNotInhabited` in `v1.compiler.core`, so the rendering is shared and the DIVERGENCE IS UPSTREAM OF IT -- which is why the two rows look like one mechanism disagreeing with itself. **THE TRIGGER IS TWO COMPETING BINDINGS LIVE IN ONE RESOLVING SCOPE, NOT THE IMPORT AS SUCH**, and this row states the narrower claim deliberately: the with/without-import pair is measured, but the two AGREEING cells agree for OPPOSITE reasons -- an un-imported foreign caller agrees at `Primitive(String)` because only the kernel binding is available, and an in-module caller agrees at `Node(String<Product(Char)>)` because only the local declaration is. Phrasing the trigger as the import would make a reader conclude the class does not reproduce when some other construct puts a second binding in scope. An explicit `import <module> \{ <fn> \}` is the ONLY construct measured to create the competition; whether any other does is UNMEASURED. Crossed arm, pre-registered before its log was read: removing the import moves ONLY the inhabitance row, from `Node(String<Product(Char)>)` to `Primitive(String)`, while the compat row is `Primitive(String)` under both -- so one producer follows the import binding and the other does not, rather than the whole reading shifting. RUNG FOUND AT: 1 (mitigatable) -- the line DOES stop, and stops located, so this is not silent wrongness; what fails is that the refusal MISDIRECTS the remedy, which is DESIGN section 5's requirement that a refusal be typed AND located read one layer deeper: located at the right column while naming the wrong destination. CEILING: 3 (structurally guaranteed) -- one resolution of a callee's declared type per call site, consumed by both producers, makes two destinations unconstructible. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability rather than an artifact: a single resolved-formal authority at the call site that both the compat check and the inhabitance obligation READ, sufficient that no call-site refusal can render two different expected types for one parameter. Distinct from `meaning_fork`, which is one NAME carrying two meanings across scopes -- that is the underlying condition here and is separately rostered; this row is about two PRODUCERS disagreeing inside a single refusal, which is what makes the remedy wrong rather than merely the meaning ambiguous. Distinct from `diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent`: there the diagnostic names a mechanism that never ran; here both mechanisms ran and both reported faithfully about different environments. WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED, by either measurer: which producer is correct, and why they read the binding differently. No arm on either rig touches it, and the source reading above identifies the producers without settling which environment a call-argument formal SHOULD be resolved in.)" as NonEmptyStr,
  evidence: [],
}


data join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a join answers with ONE of its inputs, so the inputs it did not answer with are judged nowhere** (a reduction over several producers -- match arms, branch arms, any fold that collapses N types to one -- picks its answer by a tie-break and every downstream check then reads only that answer. An input the fold did not select is compared with NOTHING: not with the join's answer, not with the consumer's declared type. **THE TELL IS THAT THE VERDICT IS A FUNCTION OF INPUT ORDER**, and that is also the falsifier: permute the arms and re-run. SPECIMEN, measured 2026-09-02 on gunbc, two modules identical except for arm order: v1.compiler.infer folded match arm body types through v1.compiler.infer_types prefer_specific_type, whose tie-break for two disjoint coproducts is the LEFT operand, so `match fl \{ FYes => FResA  FNo => FOthA \}` passed to a formal declared FRes was ACCEPTED, while the same module with those two arms swapped was REFUSED at the direct-call argument seam with `declared 'Coproduct(FRes)', produced 'Coproduct(FOth)'`. One of those is wrong and it is the ACCEPTED one -- values inhabit their declared types is the ordinary compiler floor, which DESIGN section 4b puts BELOW the ladder rather than on a rung of it. **RECOGNITION RULE: wherever a reduction answers with one of its inputs rather than with a judgment ABOUT them, ask what judges the inputs it discarded -- and if the answer is 'the consumer, which sees only the winner', the discarded inputs are unjudged by construction.** The shape hides because the seam that WOULD refuse demonstrably works: it refuses the other order, so every probe that happens to order the arms unluckily reports the compiler healthy. BOUNDED AGAINST TWO NEIGHBOURS. It is not `absorbing_fallback`: nothing failed and nothing widened, the fold answered confidently and correctly for its own purpose -- selecting the more specific of two types is what it is for. It is not `selection_view_read_as_population` either, though it is that class's compiler-internal cousin: there a measured subset is read as the population, here a SELECTED REPRESENTATIVE is read as a judgment about the whole set. RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent wrongness). RUNG AFTER THE REPAIR: mechanically preventable -- v1.compiler.infer match_arm_join_diagnostics asks match_arm_types_are_disjoint_coproducts once per arm, with the RED and its three controls enrolled at test.claim.match_arm_join_disjoint_coproduct_witness_test; the invalid state stays writable and safety depends on that check executing. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- a join that produces a JUDGED type carrying every arm's verdict, rather than a representative selected from the arms, makes an unjudged arm unconstructible. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: one join relation that every N-ary join in the stage consumes, sufficient that no arm can reach a consumer without having been compared to the join's answer -- the ExprIf and ExprMatch joins in v1.compiler.infer are today two carriers asking two different questions of the same fold, which is what let one of them judge nothing at all.)\n\n**TWO FURTHER SPECIMENS, 2026-09-02 (quick-crab-396), BOTH FOUND WHILE MEASURING SOMETHING ELSE.** (1) v1.compiler.emit_rust `module_name_from_filename` reads `map_get(module_index.by_filename, mod_filename)` and resolves the resulting `List<TypedModule>` with `|> first`. What makes it this class rather than an unlucky lookup is that the BUILDER KNOWS: `build_module_index` explicitly `list_push`es on collision, so the multiplicity is constructed deliberately and discarded silently by the reader, and the verdict is a function of fold order exactly as this row's recognition rule states. The map compounds it by being keyed on `module_to_filename(module_NAME)` -- a filename DERIVED from the module name rather than the source path a declaration sits in -- so it answers the inverse question to the one its name suggests. (2) v1.compiler.coercion `type_realization_decision` selects its checkpoint with `target_checkpoints(target) |> filter(cp => cp.dag_name == dag_name) |> first` -- a BARE-NAME filter resolved by first, standing inside the very function whose exact-identity rows (gunbc.rust_source_type_bindings) exist to remove that ambiguity. The second specimen is the more valuable of the pair because it sits in the mechanism under repair rather than beside it.", evidence: [] }

data executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a conjunct that executes, is reached, is gated on, and still discriminates nothing** (a predicate wired into a live check runs on every call, sits inside a gate that really blocks, and yet deletes cleanly: remove it and every witness stays green, because no fixture ever constructs the population that would make it false. **It is invisible precisely BECAUSE reachability is satisfied.** The usual signature of an unenforced mechanism -- nothing calls it -- is absent, so every reachability-based tell reports health, and review reads the conjunct as a wall because it genuinely is evaluated. Executed and enforcing are different properties, and no amount of coverage over the calling path distinguishes them. **It is bounded against three neighbours and none of their recognition rules will find it.** `reachability_read_as_occupancy` asks whether to DELETE a guard that is quiet, and warns that mechanism-yes / join-yes / occupancy-zero is a healthy guard; this class is not about deletion and not about occupancy -- the conjunct here should stay, and the defect is that it was believed to be doing work it was not. Section 6's inert-lens tell is machinery that nothing GATES on; this is gated on. Section 4b's decoration case is a check whose RED cannot be authored ANYWHERE; this RED can be authored -- it simply never was, which is the whole difference, and it is the difference between a permanent ceiling and one missing fixture. **THE REMEDY HAS TWO HALVES AND THE SECOND IS WHAT MAKES THE FIRST SOUND.** First: for each wall, run the DELETE arm and confirm EXACTLY ONE witness reddens -- not that a witness reddens. Second: the subject that isolates the conjunct must be chosen with care, because a red for the wrong reason is how this class survives its own test. **SPECIMEN, with both halves executed** (gunbc#9838, `gunbc.self_host_compile_phase_frontier`): `census_population_is_duplicate_free` was added as a conjunct of `receipt_population_coherent`, evaluated on every coherence check and reachable from the live path; deleting it left the whole witness module green. The fixture that isolates it is a receipt whose `refused_files` REPEATS A PATH -- enrolled as `a_receipt_whose_refused_population_repeats_a_path_is_refused_by_coherence` in `test.claim.self_host_compile_phase_frontier_witness`, with `the_same_receipt_without_the_repeat_is_coherent` as its positive control. The subject that looks equally good and is not: a repeated ERROR DIAGNOSTIC IDENTITY also reddens the module, but it breaks a count invariant one line over rather than this conjunct, so it would have scored the DEAD conjunct as LIVE and closed the investigation with the wall still inert. **RUNG: mechanically preventable, and the honest ceiling is the same rung rather than higher.** The unenforcing conjunct stays writable; what exists is an executed falsifier per wall, not a construction that forbids authoring one. The next-rung trigger is a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: a mechanism that derives, from the check itself, the population its removal would change -- so that a conjunct with an empty such population fails to compile rather than waiting for an author to think of the delete arm. Enumerating delete arms by hand does not retire it; it only executes this row's recognition rule once per wall. **Its near twin is `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content`, and they meet from opposite sides**: there a report is complete for the REPORTER and read as complete for the SUBJECT; here a conjunct is genuinely executed and read as genuinely discriminating. Both are the shape where the health signal the reader actually checks -- completeness there, execution here -- is fully satisfied while the property they believe it establishes does not hold. **Neither is found by checking harder along the axis that already reads green.** **SECOND SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, the same shape one layer down and found by a different tell.** `v1.stage0.required_regen_host` `admit_stage_execution_from_model` built ONE identity list from the stage plan and passed it as BOTH the `planned` and the `executed` field of `RegenStageExecutionObservation`, so `v2.workflow.regen_convergence_transaction` `regen_identity_population_eq` evaluated x == x.clone() on every install of the self-host convergence transaction. The conjunct ran, the install boundary really blocked, and `StagePlannedExecutedMismatch` stayed authorable in `v2.test.claim.regen_convergence_transaction_witness_test` while being unreachable from the real acceptance path -- the exact split section 4b's authorable-RED rule exists to catch. **THE DELETE ARM IS NOT WHAT FOUND IT; THE PRODUCER COUNT IS**, and that is this specimen's addition to the row: reading the two sides of one population equality back to their PRODUCERS and finding a single producer is cheaper than removing the conjunct and re-running, and it needs no experiment -- any equality whose two arguments trace to one value is this class already. **THE REPAIR IS A SECOND PRODUCER, NEVER A SECOND READ OF THE FIRST**: a digest delta over the journalled generated roster, taken before the copy loop and again after the build, carried in its own Rust newtype `ObservedEffectPopulation` with no conversion from the plan, so a later refactor cannot re-collapse the two sides without deleting a type. Its discriminating red `stage_execution_joins_the_plan_to_independently_observed_effects` carries TWO arms because one-directional identity checking is how the loss survived: an effect on a path OUTSIDE the plan, which was green before because `allowed_after` blanket-permits every already-dirty stage0 path for the rest of the transaction; and a planned surface the stage left byte-identical, which did refuse before but as `InstalledDigestMismatch` -- a CONTENT verdict standing in for a POPULATION one, so the arm asserts the cause and not that it refused.)", evidence: [] }

data unbacked_execution_claim: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "unbacked_execution_claim" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**unbacked execution claim** (prose asserts a live executing relation — this runs on X, X reads these fields, Y already resolves Z — that no authority backs, and a reader forms the premise and plans against it. §4b's CI rung drop names the harm PREMISE CONTAMINATION in its own words; this row is that harm as a general class, since the drop is about one paragraph in the canonical authority and the class is about every carrier. **THE ORIGINS ARE A FIELD OF THIS ONE ROW RATHER THAN SEPARATE ROWS, because the recognition rule is identical across them** — resolve the claim against the authority that owns the relation — **but the REMEDY BRANCHES ON THE ORIGIN, and a remedy applied without reading the origin manufactures new false statements.** Three origins are ATTESTED here and a fourth is conceivable but was NOT found. ORIGIN 1, EXECUTOR DELETED: the claim was true and its executor was removed. Specimen: `gunbc.floor_component_receipt_document` recited that an alert downloads an artifact named `floor-component-receipt` from a run id it is given and reads four named fields; that alert was `falsifier-alert.yml`, deleted 2026-08-15, and a lane read the module, believed the transport live, planned against it, and was corrected by its reviewing authority — the cost is measured, not hypothetical. Second specimen, same origin: `gunbc.ci_failure_class` stated its dissolution trigger as calling `classify_failure_reason` *the way claim_executor already resolves* `gunbc.floor_component_receipt`; `write_floor_component_receipt_at` did exactly that from 2026-07-30 (gunbc#7467) until gunbc#9228 deleted it on 2026-08-25. ORIGIN 2, THE CITED SYMBOL DIED WHILE ITS CONTENT SURVIVED AS AN ANNOTATION, and this one has a corpus-wide producer: `v1_compiler.cli_run` twice cited `floor_component_resource_checkpoint_note` and `floor_component_phase_journal_scaffold_note`, which were real `data …: String` declarations in `gunbc.floor_component_receipt` until the 2026-08-30 prose-bankruptcy sweep (gunbc#9752) converted module-scope commentary rows into §4c annotations corpus-wide. §4c makes an annotation uncitable by construction — `v1_compiler.cli_run` `annotation_erased_scan_text` feeds the semantic passes, so annotation text is not present in the tree the citation harvester walks. **THE CONSEQUENCE IS THE OPPOSITE OF THE ONE THIS ROW FIRST DREW, AND THE CORRECTION IS THE INSTRUCTIVE PART.** The first revision reasoned that the sweep therefore broke every citation of a converted row, making the population the sweep's own diff. Measured by a separate lane (gunbc XL-0-CITE, 2026-09-01) against `v1_compiler.declaration_index`, whose only citation producers are `citation_from_record_literal` and `citation_from_constructor_call`: the typed-citation breakage is **ZERO**, computed both today and as of the sweep commit, on a control that discriminates in both directions. A plain name in annotation prose was never a citation, so the sweep could not break one. What that leaves is a REAL class with an honest ceiling rather than a defect population: these citations bind READERS and no mechanism, so they sit in §4b's *outside the modeled guarantee* column — observed and repaired by reading, never gated — and calling them a dangling-citation population would have been rung inflation about a check that by construction cannot see them. The two `cli_run` sites are genuine instances of the harm and there is no mechanical census that would have found them. ORIGIN 3, WRONG AUTHORITY FOR SOMETHING THAT STILL EXECUTES: `dag/test/claim/instrument_sandbox_witness_test` says its live half `runs on the falsifier lane`; that half sits on `FalsifierSubstrateLongLane`, which `std.witness_admission` `witness_cadence_has_scheduled_route` reports routeless — but it also carries a local recipe, and `OfflineLocalRecipe` HAS a route, so the relation is live and only the named authority is wrong. THE FOURTH, NEVER BACKED AT ALL, IS NOT ATTESTED IN THIS CORPUS and is recorded as unmeasured rather than as a population. **THIS ROW IS NOT THE AUTHORITY ON ANY POPULATION, and saying so is the point:** `gunbc.deleted_cadence_reference_census` already owns the falsifier-cadence instance of origin 1 — twelve sites, a `DeletedCadenceReferenceStanding` vocabulary whose `PremiseInvalidated` arm is exactly this class, and one `GuaranteeRungDrop` filed once for the shared executor rather than per site. A pattern row that restated its population would be a second authority for a fact that already has one, which is the §3 violation this row's own remedy is meant to prevent; so the census is cited here and nothing about its contents is copied. What belongs HERE is only the recognition rule and the remedy arms, which generalize past the falsifier. **THE MECHANICAL TEST for finding one is sharper than asking whether the verb is runs or is enrolled: resolve the claim against the authority that owns the relation, and ask whether the prose implies a live route for something that authority says has none.** The naive runs/enrolled discriminator loses one arm and it is the common one — `Enrolled on falsifier_rehomed_bin_wet_entries (nightly batch 5)` is nominally an enrollment claim, which is TRUE, but `nightly` asserts a cadence that executes and `FalsifierRehomedBinWet` is routeless, so the reader forms the false premise anyway. Three outcomes per line: asserts execution (contaminating), asserts enrollment only (true, leave it), asserts enrollment while implying a live cadence (contaminating). **THE REMEDY HAS THREE ARMS, KEYED TO WHAT THE AUTHORITY SAYS NOW, and picking the wrong one is itself an instance of this class.** Origin 1 → PAST TENSE WITH THE DATE, keeping the reasoning, because the reasoning usually outlives its executor and a reader who finds a dangling claim silently deleted learns nothing. Origin 2 → name the module and the FACT rather than the dead symbol, since §4c left no symbol to cite; past-tensing here would wrongly report the content as gone when only its citability is. Origin 3 → CORRECT IT to the authority that does back it, NOT past tense: past-tensing a live relation records it as dead and is a new contamination in the opposite direction, produced by the remedy itself. Origin 4 → say it was never backed, or delete the assertion while keeping any surviving reasoning; NEVER past tense, because there is no past to record, and `X USED TO resolve Y` asserts an execution that also never happened. **The default against deletion is a default and not an absolute: a sentence whose entire content is a false execution claim has no reasoning to preserve.** **THE SELF-RECEIPT, and it is the most useful thing in this row (2026-09-01):** the first revision of this entry asserted the `ci_failure_class` clause and the two `cli_run` notes as never-true, on the strength of a grep showing they resolve nowhere TODAY. **Both were true when written**, and the row about unbacked claims therefore contained two of them. It was caught by a reviewing authority asking for verification rather than inheritance, not by any check. **RECOGNITION RULE EARNED: `resolves nowhere now` is not `never resolved`, the distinction is decided by history and not by the working tree, and the instrument is `git log --all -S` over the DECLARATION FORM** — which also separates origin 1 from origin 2 by showing WHAT deleted the referent. The neighbouring rule is `positional_citation`'s: a citation left naming a deleted symbol fakes a grep hit, so every arm above records the change rather than quietly removing the name.)", evidence: [] }

data transport_close_read_as_completion: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "transport_close_read_as_completion" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a transport close is read as protocol completion** (a consumer of a streamed response decides the response is FINISHED because the connection ENDED, rather than because the protocol's own terminator arrived. Every partial answer then presents as a complete one, and the consumer reports success while holding a fragment. This is state-space conflation on the completion axis specifically -- `the bytes stopped` and `the sender said it was done` are two facts, and a stream has a third state, SEVERED, that a two-state reading cannot express. **SPECIMEN, measured 2026-09-01 by a peer session on its own routing layer.** A streaming SSE client accumulated `message_start`, then a long run of `content_block_delta`, and registered completion in `res.on('end')` UNCONDITIONALLY -- never checking that `content_block_stop`, `message_delta` carrying `stop_reason`, and `message_stop` had arrived. A stream severed after 364 thinking deltas therefore produced a well-formed response object containing an intro line and a heading, which the transcript recorded with a tidy `stop_reason` and the UI rendered faithfully as the model's answer. **EVERY LAYER DOWNSTREAM OF THE READING LAYER BEHAVED CORRECTLY, AND THAT IS WHY THE TRUNCATION PROPAGATED SILENTLY.** The reading layer did NOT behave correctly -- it is the defect, converting a transport termination into a protocol completion and minting a `stop_reason` no sender had emitted. What every layer BELOW it then did was faithful: the transcript recorded the object it was handed, and the UI rendered that object exactly. The distinction is the whole diagnostic value of the row -- a defect that hands its consumers a WELL-FORMED artifact recruits every correct layer beneath it into carrying the wrong answer, so correctness downstream is not evidence of correctness upstream. It is also why the class survived a full evening of investigation that cleared the UI, the parser, the token budget, and the serving stack in turn: each of those really was innocent, and each exoneration made the true location look less likely rather than more. **THE DIAGNOSIS WAS INVERTED FOR HOURS BY THE ARTIFACT THE DEFECT ITSELF PRODUCED.** The fabricated `stop_reason: end_turn` was read at face value as `the model chose to stop`, so the investigation was pointed at the model and at long-context serving -- a lead reinforced by a genuinely large KV allocation -- while the defect sat in the layer doing the reading. **RECOGNITION RULE: find the completion predicate and ask whether it names a PROTOCOL EVENT or a TRANSPORT EVENT.** `on('end')`, `on('close')`, process exit, EOF, a read returning zero, and `the socket closed` are transport; a terminator frame, a `done` member, a declared length satisfied, and a trailer are protocol. A consumer whose completion predicate is transport-shaped cannot distinguish a finished answer from a severed one, no matter what it does downstream. **THE SECOND HALF OF THE RULE IS ABOUT RECOVERY, AND IT IS WHY THE CLASS IS NOT MERELY A MISSING CHECK.** Neither the Messages API nor Ollama's compatibility layer carries a resumption protocol -- no sequence numbers, no cursor, no reattachable session -- so a severed stream cannot be resumed and the only recovery is re-issuing the whole request. A client that cannot DETECT truncation therefore cannot retry either, and the missing predicate silently removes the entire recovery arm rather than one diagnostic. **THE REMEDY IS ORDERED AND THE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING**: make truncation a typed refusal FIRST, because until it is detectable a retry cannot be triggered and a fix cannot be verified; only then add re-issue. Adding retry first produces a client that retries the errors it can already see and silently accepts the ones it cannot. **GUNBC'S OWN EQUIVALENT PATH IS STRUCTURALLY IMMUNE, and the contrast is the useful part rather than a boast.** `gunbc.spark.serving_readback_parse` `spark_serving_parse_generate_done` reads completion from the response's OWN `done` member, and `spark_serving_parse_version_json` refuses a body it cannot parse with `SparkServingReadbackRefused` carrying a typed cause instead of collapsing to an absent reading. A severed body there produces a refusal, not a short answer -- the protocol terminator is the predicate, which is exactly the repair the specimen needs. **BOUNDED AGAINST NEIGHBOURS.** Against `empty_observation_narrow`: there an observation that could not express what changed renders as `nothing is affected`; here a PARTIAL observation renders as a COMPLETE one, so the count is plausible rather than empty and no zero draws attention. Against `absorbing_fallback`: that arm WIDENS on ignorance and is merely expensive; this arm reports a fragment as an answer and is silently wrong, which is below the ladder rather than on it. Against `unbacked_execution_claim`: there prose asserts a relation no authority backs; here a machine-generated artifact asserts a completion no protocol event backs, and it is more dangerous precisely because a `stop_reason` field reads as evidence.)",
  evidence: [],
}

data merge_region_excludes_shared_tail: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "merge_region_excludes_shared_tail" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**merge region excludes the shared tail** (a roster carrier whose rows are multi-line blocks ending in an identical suffix makes every two-lane append resolve WRONG BY DEFAULT. The three-way merge factors the shared suffix out of the conflict region, so the region holds two half-blocks above the markers and one tail below them, and the purely additive resolution -- delete the markers, keep both sides, which is the CORRECT resolution when the two appended rows are independent -- leaves the first row's closing lines belonging to the second. Specimen: this carrier, which conflicted on every integration of main across four merge bases in one session (2026-09-01) with a shared tail of `evidence: [],` and `}`; `gunbc.rung_drop` had the same shape with `}` alone. **THE CLASS IS LOUD, AND THAT IS THE HALF A REPORT OF IT WILL GET WRONG.** The first reading was that the severed row survives as a structurally broken declaration under which the natural check -- declared names against rostered names -- still passes, because both lists stay complete. Measured against a gunbc built at d0009ca531 on the resolved shape: it is a PARSE REFUSAL at the module index, `expected expression, found Eq`, because a `data` keyword cannot stand in record-field position. Nothing reaches the checks that reading worried about, so the cost is toil and not silent wrongness -- a load-bearing authority whose every integration lands a conflict whose natural resolution does not compile, hand-repaired each time. **RECOGNITION RULE: for a carrier two lanes append to, ask what suffix the appended units SHARE, because a conflict region never contains it -- whatever semantics live in that suffix are exactly what a resolution can drop.** THE REPAIR IS THE UNIT AND NOT A CHECK: make the appended unit one line, and the shared suffix is a blank separator carrying nothing.  **SECOND, INDEPENDENT INSTANCE, AND IT RE-RAN THE MISREPORT THIS ROW WARNS ABOUT** (vivid-boar-481, 2026-09-01, integrating main on a later base than the one above): the severed identity was `sealing_property_erases_structure` and the recipient of its donated tail was `accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target`, over the same `evidence: [],` and `}` suffix. The finder produced the naive both-sides resolution, spotted the fusion by AUDITING THE RESULTING DECLARATIONS rather than by any marker, repaired it -- and then reported that the fused file STILL PARSED and that nothing went red. That report was an inference from reading the text, never an execution, and compiling the reconstructed fused shape refused at `expected expression, found Eq`, the same diagnostic recorded above. So the row's corrected reading survived contact with a second lane, and the reading it corrects -- silent survival -- is what the second reporter independently reinvented before measuring. THE TRANSFERABLE PART IS THAT THE MISREPORT IS THE DEFAULT AND NOT A LAPSE: a reader who resolves the conflict, sees both rows present and no markers, and does not compile, will conclude 'parses fine' every time, because every visible signal available WITHOUT executing agrees with that conclusion. The audit that finds the fusion and the execution that establishes its cost are two different steps, and doing only the first is what produces a confident wrong report about severity.)", evidence: [] }

data disagreement_census_blind_to_agreed_wrong: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "disagreement_census_blind_to_agreed_wrong" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a two-reader disagreement census is blind to the case where BOTH readers are wrong together** (an instrument whose subject is DISAGREEMENT between two producers of one answer reports AGREEMENT as healthy, so the population where both answer the same WRONG thing is scored green and is invisible to it by construction. The trap is that such an instrument is commissioned precisely to adjudicate a known-defective population, and it can be structurally incapable of seeing that population while looking perfectly well-formed and producing rows. **SPECIMEN, measured 2026-09-01.** `v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census` records, per type-reference occurrence, the legacy short-circuit key and the strict authority answer, and reports where they diverge. Its calibration control -- stated in docs/plans/carrier-realization-arbiter-repair-design.md -- requires the diagnostic-producing `DivergesWithExactIdentity` subset to reproduce arm A 25 sites, joined by source declaration and enclosing declaration, never by line. Run over the transitive import closure of `src/v2/compiler/01_tokenize.dag`, the module that emits the file where every arm-A site lives contributed 76 rows: 74 Agrees, 2 IdentityUnavailable, ZERO divergences, and all 26 of its `String`-named rows Agree. Every divergence row in the closure sat in `v2.std.text`, the DECLARING module, in the opposite direction. Empty intersection with the population the control exists to find. **THE SHAPE OF THE ABSENCE IS THE DIAGNOSIS, and it is what distinguishes this class from an over-broad walk.** `gunbc#9900` predicted the walk might visit occurrences the emitter never renders; that defect shows the target population PLUS extras. This showed the target population NOT AT ALL. Same instrument, same rows, opposite conclusions -- and only the shape separates them. **WHY BOTH READERS AGREE THERE**, read off `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `checkpoint_table_bypasses_identity_note` REACHABILITY CORRECTION rather than executed here: the short-circuit returns the host spelling before consulting any authority, and the authority answers from `type_reference_decl_file`, whose fallback returns the file containing the REFERENCE. Two readers, one wrong answer, perfect agreement. **RECOGNITION RULE: any two-reader comparison cited as CORRECTNESS coverage.** A differential oracle, a twin fixture, a cross-check, a self-hosted-versus-seed comparison, an A/B over two emitters -- each answers `do these two concur`, and none answers `is the answer right`. Ask what a SHARED error would look like in its output; if the answer is `indistinguishable from health`, the instrument cannot be the correctness evidence, whatever else it is good for. **THE REMEDY IS A DIFFERENT ORACLE, NOT A REPAIR OF THIS ONE.** The adjudicating instrument has to reach OUTSIDE the pair of readers for its ground truth -- for this specimen, a census of agreement-at-a-wrong-answer joined against emitted-crate diagnostics. Widening the occurrence set, fixing the walk, or adding a third reader that shares the same defective input do not help, and the first two are what a reader who diagnosed this as an over-broad walk would have spent. **Bounded against `executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing`**: there a live gated conjunct never meets a population that would falsify it, and one authored fixture retires it; here the instrument meets its population on every run and reports it as healthy, so no fixture over this instrument can retire it. **Bounded against `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content`**: there the instrument answers its own question faithfully and a consumer substitutes the subject; here the instrument answers ITS OWN question faithfully too, and the defect is that its question -- do the readers concur -- was never the question that was asked.)",
  evidence: [],
}

data undecided_fraction_read_as_denominator: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "undecided_fraction_read_as_denominator" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a census with an unresolvable fraction of its population reports a denominator it does not have** (an occurrence census that emits a third disposition for `could not determine` is honest at the row grain and misleading at the total grain: rows scored `identity unavailable` are neither agreements nor divergences, so any ratio taken over the reported total silently treats them as decided. **SPECIMEN, unowned and unexplained at filing (2026-09-01).** The `v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census` run over the `src/v2/compiler/01_tokenize.dag` closure produced 121 `IdentityUnavailable` rows -- roughly a tenth of its population. The earlier run recorded in docs/plans/carrier-realization-arbiter-repair-design.md, over the same subject module at the FRONT-END phase on 2026-08-21, reported `1142 rows: 1134 Agrees, 8 DivergesWithExactIdentity, 0 IdentityUnavailable`. Zero to a tenth, across a phase change nobody predicted it for. **BOTH RUNS ARE NAMED RATHER THAN THEIR NUMBERS INHERITED**: the earlier is the front-end-phase run the design itself later withdraws as measuring the wrong phase, and the later is the typed-graph census landed by `gunbc#9900`. They are not the same instrument and the pair is recorded to locate the question, not to compute a delta from. **RECOGNITION RULE: an instrument with a `cannot answer` disposition, whose consumers aggregate over the reported total.** Ask what fraction is undecided before reading any ratio, and treat the undecided fraction as a separate finding rather than as noise. **WHY IT IS FILED WITHOUT INVESTIGATION**: identity being unavailable is a different defect from the readers disagreeing, it has no owner, and it was found while running a control for an unrelated question. A row that records it with both runs named is what stops the next reader taking the census denominator at face value.)",
  evidence: [],
}

data sealing_property_erases_structure: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "sealing_property_erases_structure" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a construction-restricting property read as a structure-erasing one** (a declaration is annotated to RESTRICT how its inhabitants may be built, and a consumer that asks about the declaration's SHAPE treats the annotation as a reason to stop looking -- so the deliberate climb on the construction axis silently drops a rung on every axis decided by shape, with no declaration, because the two axes are read by different consumers. **THE INVERSION IS THE CLASS**: the annotation exists to make the carrier MORE distinct from its payload, and the consumer's response is to make it INDISTINGUISHABLE from everything. Recognition rule, keyed on the SHAPE and not on any one keyword: whenever a declaration-level marker is stored in a general side-channel -- a properties list, an attribute bag, a modifier set -- find every consumer that BRANCHES ON THAT CHANNEL BEING NON-EMPTY rather than on the specific marker, and ask what each of them would have answered had the marker been absent; a consumer that answers 'opaque', 'unknown', or 'skip' for the whole channel has conflated 'this declaration carries a marker I do not model' with 'this declaration has no structure', and every future marker inherits the same silence on arrival. **SPECIMEN, with the discriminating pair** (gunbc XL-0-FLOOR, 2026-09-01): `v2.compiler.normalized_tree` `NormalizedTree` was sealed by BL-1 from an alias for `Node` into a `sole_constructor` record so that a wrapper-retention drop would be unwritable. `sole_constructor` is carried as a PROPERTY on the declaration node (`v1.compiler.parse` `parsed_sole_constructor_properties`), and `v1.compiler.infer` `exposure_view_for_node` answered `OpaqueTypeHead` for any node whose properties list was non-empty -- so `nominal_product_head_name` answered the empty string for every sealed carrier, `nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal` short-circuited on the empty head, and `declared_type_inhabitance` fell through to `Inhabits`. `v2.compiler.source_authority` `normalized_source_ast_equal_witness` then bound a `NormalizedTree` at a formal declared `Node` and the compiler ACCEPTED it: the ordinary-floor violation DESIGN section 4b names as exact application bijection, below baseline. The discriminating pair is two record declarations identical to the token except for the word `sole_constructor` -- the sealed one compiled with zero diagnostics where the plain one refused. **WHY A CENSUS MISSED IT, which is the part that generalizes**: gunbc#8886 measured 285 sites behind the `v2.*` direct-call argument-type exemption, of which 148 were `Node` against `ResolvedTree`/`ParseTree` and siblings -- every one a transparent-ALIAS false positive. This shape never appears in that roster and could not have, because it is a TRUE positive the comparison relation cannot reach: the census enumerates what the relation REFUSES, so a defect the relation is blind to is invisible to the census by construction, and a large census reads as thorough coverage of exactly the region it cannot see. **THE MISDIAGNOSIS THIS CLASS INVITES, recorded because this lane was dispatched with it**: the silence sat inside a module the exemption covers, so the exemption was the obvious cause; refuting it took running the identical program in an ordinary module and on a tree with the exemption deleted, both of which stayed silent, while the same run showed the exemption's effect on a kernel red so the arms were provably live. A plausible nearby mechanism that is genuinely broken is the most expensive wrong answer available, because repairing it changes nothing and the repair reads as coverage. **Rung: mechanically preventable, and the ceiling for this class as a class is the same rung.** The repair makes one marker structure-preserving by positive establishment -- the parser builds the identical declaration node and only the properties list differs -- and every OTHER marker in that channel stays opaque and unmeasured, which is a named residue rather than a covered class. The next-rung trigger is a CAPABILITY: markers carried in the declaration's own type rather than in an untyped side-channel, so that a consumer branching on the channel cannot compile.)",
  evidence: [],
}
data censored_estimator_drops_its_own_tail: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "censored_estimator_drops_its_own_tail" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**censored estimator drops its own tail** (an estimate of a variable is computed over the observations that SURVIVED a threshold on that same variable, so the sample structurally excludes its own extreme and the estimate is biased low with no bound. It is the neighbour of `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content` moved one step earlier: there a REPORT is complete for the reporter and read as complete for the consumer; here the truncation is in the ESTIMATOR'S OWN DOMAIN, and no amount of reading the instrument's output correctly recovers what the filter removed. SPECIMEN, both directions, 2026-09-01: the required floor's per-run cost inflation was estimated by pairing every claim that reported a cost in BOTH attempts of one tree -- median 1.053, p90 1.107. A claim that exceeds the cpu ceiling goes INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT AND REPORTS NO COST, so the pairing dropped exactly the two most inflated observations; recovered from the ceiling itself, their inflation was at least 500/418 = 1.196, censored from above. THE SECOND HALF IS WHY THE ROW EXISTS: a peer lane, correcting a DIFFERENT defect in the same measurement, took the biased p90 by relay and derived an at-risk population of ONE -- an understatement arriving with the credibility of a retraction, which is the artifact nobody re-audits. Both counts were lower bounds and neither was labelled as one. RECOGNITION RULE: whenever an estimate is computed over rows that COMPLETED, RETURNED, PASSED, or were OBSERVED, ask what the incomplete rows would have contributed -- and if the incompleteness is caused by the very variable being estimated, the statistic is a floor and must be reported as one. The tell is a filter and an estimand naming the same quantity: cost estimated over rows that finished, latency over requests that did not time out, size over responses that were not truncated. REMEDY: report the censored bound rather than the sample statistic, and recover the excluded observations from the THRESHOLD they crossed, which is a real datum -- a row killed at 500ms is not missing, it is known to be above 500.)", evidence: [] }

data restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a restoration promise names a route that does not exist** (a mechanism withholds, defers or dormant-marks a population and tells the reader it becomes observable again under some named condition — and that condition names a RUN, LANE, CADENCE OR SWEEP the tree does not contain. Nothing refuses, because the promise is a string in a diagnostic rather than a citation anything resolves; the population is not silently dropped, which is what makes the class survive review — it is dropped WITH A RECEIPT, and the receipt is what stops anyone looking. **THE BOUNDARY AGAINST `unbacked_execution_claim` IS THE TENSE AND IT DECIDES THE REMEDY.** That class is prose asserting a relation that RUNS NOW; this is prose asserting a relation that WILL run — a future condition, so `git log --all -S` over the declaration form finds nothing to past-tense and the origin arms there do not apply. It is also not `absorbing_fallback`: nothing widens, the withhold is precise and correctly counted. It is 4b(3)'s trigger trap with the polarity inverted — there a trigger names LESS than the capability it restores and gets satisfied while the capability stays dead; here the trigger names a capability whose PRECONDITION IS ALREADY FALSE, so it can never be satisfied at all and the row waits forever in a state that reads as temporary. **SPECIMEN WITH A RECEIPT, measured 2026-09-01 on head 4c6c509e and unrepaired at authoring.** `v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner` `suppress_withheld` removes enrolled expected-red identities whose module sits outside the required gate, printing that their enrolment `becomes observable again when the gate roster admits the module or in the whole-corpus receipts run`. THAT RUN DOES NOT EXIST: the phrase occurs exactly once in the tree, inside the message that promises it, and the repository carries three workflows of which none is it. 39 identities across 23 modules sit under that promise. Each is enrolled on `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red`, whose own header states what an enrolment asserts — that the identity REACHES ITS SUBJECT AND ANSWERS, and that a row belongs there only while someone is fixing it — so every one of the 39 asserts `runs, fails, someone is fixing it` about a row no run reaches. The only surviving route by which one executes is the changed-witness override, i.e. somebody editing it. **THE POPULATION IS DERIVABLE AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT TRANSCRIBED HERE**: it is `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` `floor_expected_red_roster` minus the identities whose module matches `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` — two authorities and a set difference, so it re-derives instead of rotting. **THE SAME ROSTER'S HEADER ALREADY RECORDS THE ANCESTOR OF THIS MISTAKE**, which is why it is a class: 101 rows were held there as agreement while never reaching their subject, and were reclassified into `v2.workflow.floor_route_gap` on 2026-08-20 once `ExpectedRedArm` was taught to refuse `HostEffectRefused`, `HostToolUnresolved` and an interrupted budget. That repair closed the arm where a NON-VERDICT was read as agreement; this class is the same harm one step earlier, where a row never reaches an arm at all and a sentence promises it will. **RECOGNITION RULE: whenever a diagnostic says a withheld thing becomes observable again `in`/`under`/`by` some named run, grep the tree for that name and require an executing consumer — a workflow job, a scheduled entry point, an actuator argv. If the only occurrence is the promise itself, the population is dormant forever and the honest states are two: admit the row cannot be observed on any cadence, or delete the enrolment. **RUNG: 1 (mitigatable) — the withhold is counted and located, which is the whole of what holds. CEILING: 3, since `whether a named route exists` is decidable from the workflow and entry-point authorities the tree already carries. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: restoration conditions expressed as a resolvable citation to an executing consumer rather than as prose, so a promise naming no route fails to compile — writing this particular sentence better retires nothing.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }
data unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**an unhandled state falls to the NOT-YET arm, so a settled answer is reported as a pending one** (a fold reduces a producer's conclusion set to a verdict with an arm per state it knows and a default for the rest, and the default it falls to is NOT-YET-TERMINAL. A state the producer really can emit, but the fold has no arm for, is therefore rendered as STILL WAITING -- and waiting is the one disposition that never resolves, because nothing further is coming. THE DISGUISE IS THE WHOLE DEFECT: an unhandled state normally announces itself by producing a wrong answer, and this one produces NO answer, which is indistinguishable from the fold working correctly over a subject that has not finished. SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, gunbc PR 10086: `dashboard-ops reviews` reported ready:false with requirement `checks` failing and checks_state `pending`, AT THE SAME INSTANT that GitHub reported the head CLEAN and mergeStateStatus admitted a merge -- and the merge was then taken on GitHub's word, with no override, and was correct. Every job in the run had a terminal conclusion: five `pass` and one `skipping`. The skip is the unhandled state -- a GitHub NEUTRAL, which is a THIRD conclusion beside success and failure -- and the readiness fold, carrying arms for the first two, dropped it into not-yet-terminal. THE MECHANISM IS NOT LAG AND THAT IS THE POINT: the two are the same field with the same value, and only one of them is discharged by waiting. RECOGNITION RULE, and it is the load-bearing part because the status field cannot answer it: when a readiness or aggregate verdict says NOT YET, do not wait on the verdict -- NAME THE SPECIFIC ROW THAT IS NON-TERMINAL AND ASK WHETHER IT CAN EVER BECOME TERMINAL. A row already sitting in a terminal state the fold does not recognise never will, so patience is not a remedy for it and no amount of it produces new information. The falsifier is cheap and available at every such moment: read the producer's own per-row conclusions beside the fold's summary. If every row is terminal and the summary is not, the summary has an arm missing. WHY THIS LOCATION IS WORSE THAN A LOG READER, which is the reason it is ranked rather than merely filed: this is the instrument that decides whether WORK IS DONE. A log reader that under-reports costs a diagnosis and the next reader recovers it; a readiness fold that under-reports costs the MERGE, and it fails in the direction that LOOKS LIKE CAUTION, so nobody overrides it and nobody is embarrassed by it. THE COUNTERFACTUAL IS WHAT MAKES THE ROW ACTIONABLE: a reader following the dashboard alone would still be waiting on a pull request that had been mergeable for an hour -- and would read their own patience as diligence, which is the one failure mode that generates no complaint from the person suffering it. WHY THIS IS NOT `empty_capture_read_as_clean_result`, its nearest neighbour and the class the same session had just extended: that class is about a CAPTURE that is empty, where the reader holds no observation and believes they hold one. Here the observation is complete and correct at every input -- five passes and a skip, all present, all read -- and the loss is in the REDUCTION over them. Merging the two would repeat exactly the defect that produced this row's neighbour, a recognition rule too broad to catch a second instance of its own subject: `size the artifact before grepping it` is the surviving rule there and it is silent here, because the artifact is the right size and says the right thing. WHY THIS IS NOT `state_space_conflation`, the honest neighbour on the other side: all three of that class's forms are defects in a domain THIS TREE MODELS -- an `Option` overloaded past two meanings, a prose dichotomy over three states, a real state carried as an ad-hoc spelling -- and each of their recognition rules ends in ADD THE CONSTRUCTOR OR THE ARM. That repair is unavailable here: the conclusion set is GitHub's and the fold is the dashboard's, neither of which this repository owns, so the actionable rule has to be one a READER can execute against an instrument they cannot edit. That is why the rule above is a discriminator rather than a modelling instruction, and it is the whole reason this is its own row. RUNG FOUND AT: silent wrongness for any consumer of the summary field alone, since the fold reports a value that is not merely imprecise but WRONG about whether the subject can still change, and offers no signal that an input was unrecognised. It is mitigatable for a reader who applies the rule above, which is diligence rather than a mechanism. CEILING: outside the modeled guarantee for the dashboard's own fold, which this repository does not own and can only observe; for the equivalent folds gunbc DOES own, structurally impossible, because a reduction over a CLOSED conclusion set is exactly the case DESIGN section 4's exhaustive match makes unwritable -- a state with no arm fails to compile rather than defaulting. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER for the part we own: every gunbc fold over a third-party status or conclusion set ingesting that set as a closed coproduct in `extdeps/` with a variant per documented state, so an unmodeled state is a typed, located refusal at the boundary rather than a silent fall-through -- and NOT a default arm that maps the unknown to pending, which is this row's defect re-authored one layer down.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }

data salience_instrument_blind_to_the_record_it_sizes: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "salience_instrument_blind_to_the_record_it_sizes" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a salience instrument blind to the record it sizes** (a change's SIZE IN THE DIFF is read to decide how much attention it deserves, and for one class of artifact that number is wrong by orders of magnitude, so a substantive edit is allocated a trivial edit's scrutiny. The instrument is not merely inaccurate, it is a SALIENCE instrument -- read FIRST, to decide where to look -- which is why the error does damage a plainly wrong number would not: nobody checks a figure they have already used to decide the thing is not worth checking. SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, gunbc#10044: `git diff --stat -- dag/gunbc/rung_drop.dag` reported `1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)` for an edit adding 15,286 bytes, because every `RungDrop` in that corpus is ONE VERY LONG LINE. Three consecutive independent reviews described that hunk as a small wording tweak; a fourth, earlier one attributed it to `direct_call_arg_seam_v2_exemption`, A ROW THE DIFF DOES NOT TOUCH, because git's `@@` header names the declaration PRECEDING the hunk and the edited record is a single line. So one representation produced two distinct review failures -- under-sizing and misattribution -- and n=3 on the first within one pull request. THE APPROVALS WERE NOT WRONG ON WHAT THEY READ: each verdict is defensible over the prose rows the same diff carries, which render normally. What the count concealed is that the PR had three approvals and NO review coverage of the half that carried the receipt. A review tally is a claim about attention, and this instrument silently redirects attention before any reviewer forms a judgment. RUNG FOUND AT: silent wrongness, which is not a rung -- the misallocation leaves no trace, produces a green, and is indistinguishable from a reviewer who looked and found nothing. CEILING: mechanically preventable. The size of a record's diff can be made to track the size of its content, which is a representation question and decidable; it does not reach structural impossibility because nothing stops a future record from being authored as one long line again. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT 'REVIEWERS SHOULD LOOK HARDER': a representation in which a record's diff size tracks its content size -- the long-line record broken across lines so a diff has hunks proportional to the change, or a review surface that reads the generated projection (`docs/design-failure-modes.md` renders the same content as prose and diffs legibly) rather than the `.dag` line. 'Look harder' is advice, and advice is what a class gets when nobody wants to pay for the fix; it also cannot be discharged, since every reviewer meets the same instrument. RECOGNITION RULE: when a review's description of a hunk is smaller than the hunk, check whether the artifact's line structure and the change's content structure agree. Where one record is one line, EVERY size signal derived from lines -- the diffstat, the hunk header, a line-count budget, a review-effort heuristic -- is answering about the file's shape rather than the change's. The tell is a reviewer citing the enclosing declaration rather than the edited one.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }

data non_verdict_disposition_surfaces_as_refusal: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "non_verdict_disposition_surfaces_as_refusal" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a non-verdict disposition surfaced as a refusal** (a gate COMPUTES the difference between THIS SUBJECT IS WRONG and I DID NOT FINISH LOOKING AT THIS SUBJECT, and then DISCARDS it at its aggregate boundary. THE NARROW CLAIM IS THE TRUE ONE AND AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW OVERSTATED IT: the floor does NOT conflate the two at the diagnostic grain, and saying so was falsifiable from the very log this row cites. It prints INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT and COMPLETED-OVER-COST-REQUIREMENT as distinct typed diagnostics, and its summary carries `interrupted_before_verdict` and `completed_over_cost_requirement` as separate counters beside `failed`. A reader of the log can tell them apart perfectly. What cannot tell them apart is everything DOWNSTREAM of the fold -- the FloorRefused verdict, the red check, the dashboard cell, the merge gate -- each of which receives one bit and offers one affordance, which is to run it again. So the defect is not a missing distinction; it is a computed distinction erased on the way out, which is the worse shape of the two because the information exists and is thrown away. Its neighbour is `state_space_conflation` and its dual is `absorbing_fallback`: absorption widens an answer it could not compute, while this reports a computation it never completed AS an answer. The harm is specific and it is not the red itself: a refusal that names no wrong subject cannot be acted on, so the only available response is to run it again -- and a wall that is discharged by rerunning is not a wall. It teaches every consumer that its refusals are weather. SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, gunbc.witness_floor_workflow required floor: the same commit, 9b00e24f592 on gunbc PR 9984, was run twice with no intervening edit -- ONE run id retried, Actions run 33604337589 attempts 1 and 2 -- and every counter below is addressed by ATTEMPT AND JOB rather than by the ordinals FIRST and RERUN, which name no instrument and do not distinguish this pair from run 33628404336, a different run on a later head. ATTEMPT 1, required-witnesses-floor job 100172868685, conclusion failure: planned=3486 executed=3486 passed=3404 failed=0 interrupted_before_verdict=4 completed_over_cost_requirement=3, verdict FloorRefused. ATTEMPT 2, required-witnesses-floor job 100189043027, conclusion success: planned=3486 executed=3486 passed=3411 failed=0 interrupted_before_verdict=0 completed_over_cost_requirement=0, verdict green. RE-DERIVE EACH SIDE FROM ITS OWN JOB with `gh api repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/actions/jobs/<job>/logs --allow-escape-sequences`, and NEVER with `gh run view --job <job> --log`: measured on this very pair, the latter ANSWERS THE ATTEMPT-1 JOB ID WITH ATTEMPT 2's CONTENT -- its runner banner reads 09:03 where that job's own log begins 08:05, and it reports interrupted_before_verdict=0 completed_over_cost_requirement=0, which are attempt 2's counters. A reader trusting it would record 0 and 0 for BOTH attempts, see no disagreement, and destroy the specimen this row is built on. It is the sibling of `empty_capture_read_as_clean_result` arriving through a WRONG-CONTENT channel rather than an empty one, and it is the more dangerous direction because the answer is ~600 kB of well-formed, plausible log for the wrong subject rather than a zero-byte file anyone would question. Identical planned and executed populations, zero failures in BOTH runs, and the cost-arm rows simply absent the second time. THE SUBJECT OF THIS CLASS IS THE FOUR INTERRUPTED ROWS AND NOT ALL SEVEN, corrected after review: `completed_over_cost_requirement` names claims that REACHED A VERDICT and were then reclassified on cost -- the floor's own text says \"reached its verdict and then exceeded its budget ... cost=501ms EXACT ... This is a cost debt only -- it is not a defect\", and the rows carry outcome=completed_over_budget, which is to say they PASSED. Those three are a cost-debt fact about a gate that did judge, and folding them into a class about gates that did NOT judge would inflate the specimen by more than half while contradicting the model's own deliberate distinction. They are retained above only as the second half of the nondeterminism observation, where they belong: both arms of the cost machinery vary run to run on fixed bytes. THE SAME-HEAD PAIR IS THE POINT: a cross-head comparison would have required arguing that the intervening commit could not have touched cost accounting, and an argument about what a diff cannot do is exactly what gets overturned; holding the bytes fixed by construction leaves nothing to argue. The disposition at issue is named non-verdict by the floor itself: INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT says the deadline preempted the witness so whether it passes is UNKNOWN, and the row's cost is reported as above the ceiling with NO UPPER BOUND -- a bound, not a near miss. So on those four rows the gate is not reversing a judgment between runs; it is failing to REACH one and rendering that as a refusal. That is the whole class: FOUR rows in this specimen, and the arithmetic of the refusal is that four undecided rows were sufficient to refuse a run in which zero claims failed. THE COST HALF OF THIS STORY IS NOT THIS ROW'S AND IS NOT RE-DERIVED HERE. That a claim's measured cpu-ms is unstable on a shared runner -- and therefore that `completed_over_cost_requirement` varies run to run on fixed bytes -- is the declared standing drop `gunbc.rung_drop` `floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable`, whose restoration trigger is a claim-owned cost basis invariant or bounded by construction across the admitted envelopes. That row also settles what happens at the boundary: both terminal arms STAY required reds and are distinct. This row takes no position on whether a cost verdict qualifies a claim; it says only that the aggregate discards which arm fired. Filing the cost instability separately would be a second authority over one fact. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the dispositions are typed, located and counted at the fold, and the floor's own diagnostic text states plainly that the verdict is unknown rather than claiming a failure. What it does not do is carry that distinction past its own summary line. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a claim reached a verdict is decidable and already decided -- the floor holds the disposition -- so this is DESIGN section 5's wall after grounding, not a decidability limit. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, two conjuncts because either alone leaves the class where it is: (i) a required-gate verdict in which non-verdict dispositions are a THIRD outcome distinct from pass and fail -- DISTINCT IN DIAGNOSIS, NEVER IN WHETHER THE LINE STOPS. The third outcome must still block the gate: a run that did not finish looking has established nothing, and letting it through would be a widening arm of exactly the kind DESIGN section 5 forbids, trading a refusal that names no subject for no refusal at all. What must change is what the refusal SAYS -- an undecided row is reported as undecided and is discharged by making the claim reach a verdict, never by a rerun that happens to land under the ceiling. The defect is the conflation, not the stopping; AND (ii) a cost admission whose budget is a property of the CLAIM rather than of the run's host speed, sufficient that the same bytes yield the same disposition across runs -- without it, arm (i) merely relabels an intermittent outcome and the population that must be resolved keeps changing underneath its own roster. RECOGNITION RULE: ask what the gate reports when it could not measure, and compare it with what it reports when it measured and found the subject wrong. If those two are the same value, the gate's refusals do not name a subject, and the tell is behavioural: people begin rerunning it rather than reading it.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }

data empty_capture_read_as_clean_result: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "empty_capture_read_as_clean_result" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**an empty capture read as a clean result** (an instrument refuses on one stream while the reader keeps the other, so the capture is EMPTY and the empty capture is consumed as a finding of nothing. It is a specialization of `blank is not evidence` narrowed to a mechanism that recurs: the refusal is well-formed and honest, it simply travels on a channel nobody kept. SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, reading a failing CI job during gunbc PR 9984: `gh run view --job <id> --log > f` writes ZERO BYTES and puts `run is still in progress; logs will be available when it is complete` on stderr, so the redirect captures nothing while the job is already recorded as completed failure. A grep for `panicked` or `FAILED` over that file then reports no failures for a job that failed. Two adjacent instances in the same call: `gh api .../actions/jobs/<id>/logs` writes zero bytes without --allow-escape-sequences, again refusing on stderr; and the same subcommand takes a JOB id rather than a run id, where the wrong id also yields nothing useful. THE ASYMMETRY IS WHAT MAKES IT RECUR: the failure direction is always benign. An empty capture never manufactures a false alarm, only a false all-clear, so nothing in the reader's experience trains them to check it. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable at the reading site -- measuring the capture's size before consuming it converts the silent case into a loud one -- and silent wrongness wherever that check is absent, which is the default. CEILING: mechanically preventable for instruments this repository owns, since a reader that must consume a typed outcome cannot consume a byte count of zero as a verdict; it stays mitigatable for third-party command-line tools, whose stream discipline is outside the modeled guarantee and is observed rather than proven. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a repository instrument-reading surface whose result type distinguishes READ SUCCESSFULLY AND FOUND NOTHING from DID NOT READ, sufficient that a zero-byte capture cannot inhabit the first -- at which point the diligence rule below is subsumed for every call routed through it, and remains diligence for calls that are not. RECOGNITION RULE: before believing a quiet result, ask which stream the instrument refuses on and which stream you kept. If a refusal and a clean result produce the same bytes in the channel you read, you have no observation. The mechanical form, and it is a two-step rather than a byte-count rule, because inferring failure from size alone fabricates a refusal for the query that legitimately returned nothing: a zero-byte capture is NOT A VERDICT IN EITHER DIRECTION, so consult the instrument's typed status -- its exit code, and the stream its refusal travels on -- before consuming the emptiness. Where the status says the instrument ran and the capture is empty, that is FOUND NOTHING and is a real observation; where the status says it refused, or the status is unavailable, the capture is DID NOT READ and no conclusion may be drawn from it. The failure of the original habit is not that it read zero as one of those two, it is that it read zero WITHOUT ASKING which. FOURTH INSTANCE, 2026-09-02, gunbc PR 10078, AND IT DEFEATS BOTH RULES ABOVE AS WRITTEN: reading the newly promoted aggregate's receipt line via `gh api .../actions/jobs/<id>/logs` produced NINETY-NINE BYTES ON STDOUT -- the refusal string `the response contains terminal escape sequences; pass --allow-escape-sequences to output it anyway` written into the PAYLOAD channel rather than onto stderr. Both steps of the mechanical rule miss it: the capture is not zero-length, and the stream question -- which stream does the refusal travel on -- answers THE ONE YOU KEPT. A grep for the receipt line over that file finds nothing and exits non-zero, which is indistinguishable from THE RECEIPT LINE IS ABSENT -- and absent would have meant the freshly promoted lane was consuming nothing and the promotion was cosmetic. THE SHARPENING THIS INSTANCE ADDS is to the asymmetry claimed above: an empty capture never manufactures a false alarm is true of the CAPTURE and false of the CONSUMER, because a grep that searches for a symptom's ABSENCE converts the benign direction into a confident positive finding -- and a finding gets acted on where a green gets ignored, so the harm here is the greater one, not the lesser. The rule that actually caught it is a THIRD beside the two above and is independent of both: size the artifact against what the subject plausibly weighs before reading a grep over it as a result. Ninety-nine bytes is not a job log, whatever the exit code says. FIFTH INSTANCE, 2026-09-02, gunbc PR 10086, AND IT IS A THIRD SHAPE RATHER THAN A REPEAT: A COMPLETED JOB WHOSE LOG READS ZERO BYTES WITH NO REFUSAL ON EITHER STREAM. `gh run view --job 100322901366 --log` returned zero bytes and printed nothing on stderr -- not the documented in-progress refusal, no refusal at all -- while `gh api repos/gunb-ai/gunbc/actions/jobs/100322901366/logs --allow-escape-sequences` returned 442,248 bytes carrying the cause. A grep over the empty capture finds nothing and exits non-zero, which reads as THE JOB LOG CONTAINS NO FAILURE for the very job that failed. WHAT THIS INSTANCE BREAKS IS THE ROW ITSELF, and that is why it is filed rather than counted: the fallback advice accumulated above is CIRCULAR. The fourth instance names `gh run view` as the escape from a refusing `gh api`; this instance names `gh api` as the escape from a silent `gh run view`. The two routes are each other's documented remedy and both failed on 2026-09-02, in OPPOSITE directions -- ninety-nine bytes of refusal on the PAYLOAD channel from the api route, zero bytes and NO refusal from run view -- so a reader following this row lands on whichever route happens to be broken that day. The two mechanical steps written above are route-dependent for one shared reason: each interrogates HOW THE INSTRUMENT REFUSED -- which stream the refusal travels on, what the exit status says -- and an instrument that emits no refusal at all answers neither question. Consulting the typed status here yields SUCCESS over an empty capture, which is precisely the DID NOT READ case wearing the FOUND NOTHING answer. ONLY THE SUBJECT-WEIGHT CHECK SURVIVES, and it survives because it interrogates the ARTIFACT rather than the instrument, so it is indifferent to which route broke. COROLLARY, and it is the operative addition: when the weight is implausible, RE-READ BY THE OTHER ROUTE -- not because the other route is trustworthy, it demonstrably is not, but because 442,248 bytes against zero for one subject is a DISCRIMINATING COMPARISON, where either number read alone is not a measurement of anything.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }

data liveness_probe_read_as_currency: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "liveness_probe_read_as_currency" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a liveness probe read as currency** (a probe answers whether a thing is RUNNING and its answer is consumed as whether it is running the CURRENT definition. The two questions differ only for a process that outlived the definition it was started from, which is the one state a converge is supposed to repair, so the conflation is invisible on every host that has never drifted and load-bearing on exactly the hosts that have. Its neighbour is `state_space_conflation`, and what separates it is that NOTHING HERE IS OVERLOADED: each probe answers its own subject correctly and the loss happens in the JOIN, where a reader picks the observation nearest the question instead of the one that answers it. SPECIMEN, 2026-09-02, gunbc.spark.serving_membership: serving convergence carries an activity member observed through `systemctl --user is-active`, whose four states are running, stopped, no-such-unit and unobserved, and a registration member whose digest is the unit content ON DISK. A host whose unit file was rewritten and whose manager was reloaded converges at BOTH addresses -- the disk holds the desired bytes, the manager has consumed them, the unit is active -- while the process still serves the definition it was started from. No member disagrees, so no remedy is planned, and the drift is reported as convergence. THE HARM IS NOT THE STALE PROCESS, IT IS THAT NOTHING CAN EVER SELECT ITS REMEDY: a restart has no observation to be conditioned on, which is why gunbc.spark.serving_realization carried its only restart as an unconditional third command welded into EnableSystemUnit, restarting every host on every converge because it could not tell which host needed it. RUNG FOUND AT: silent wrongness, which is not a rung -- a stale server and a converged one produced the same verdict with no diagnostic. THE STATE PREDATES THE CHANGE THAT FILED THIS ROW, stated because an honest declaration of a pre-existing gap is indistinguishable, to a reader scanning a diff for regressions, from a confession of a new one -- and it has now been read that way twice. The convergence path acquired this class when activity was modeled on `systemctl --user is-active` in gunbc.spark.serving_observed_members, whose four states name whether a unit runs and never which definition it runs. The PR that split the fused restart neither introduced this state nor closed it; it named it. IT IS STILL THERE ON THE CONVERGENCE PATH, and an earlier revision of this row said MITIGATABLE, which was rung inflation caught in review: `spark_serving_reactivation_remedy` refuses with a typed located cause, but it has NO PRODUCTION CALLER, so nothing routes a convergence through it and the operational path still reports convergence without the refusal. A rung is the minimum across a class's in-scope paths, and a selector nothing calls moves none of them. WHAT THIS CHANGE DID ESTABLISH is the vocabulary and a selector whose refusal is executed against FIXTURE inputs -- a declared boundary, not a rung, and named as one so it cannot be cited as coverage. THE ABSENCE OF THE CALLER IS A DECISION, NOT AN OMISSION: a production caller is a path that can emit a restart, and until an admission fence, a drain protocol and a lease population exist, a restart emitted on a live host is the destructive convergence the gate exists to prevent -- so wiring it early would trade an honest gap for an unguarded one. CEILING: structurally guaranteed. The question is decidable -- a running invocation either carries the definition identity it was started from or does not -- so this is DESIGN section 5's wall AFTER GROUNDING, waiting on its single authority rather than on a decidability argument. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, AND IT IS TWO THINGS RATHER THAN ONE, because either alone leaves the class exactly where it is: (i) an observation that joins a unit's RUNNING INVOCATION to the definition it was started from, sufficient to mint `RunningDefinitionObserved` for a live Spark -- nothing smaller counts, since a probe that reads the file, the manager's loaded definition, or liveness answers a different subject and would leave the capability dead while looking like its trigger; AND (ii) a guarded producer that routes `ReactivationUndecidable` into the convergence verdict, so a host whose running definition cannot be established stops instead of reporting converged. Naming only (i) would be the grain mismatch section 4b(3) warns about: the trigger would be satisfied by a probe landing while the convergence path stayed silent, which is the whole defect. THE OBSERVED-VERSUS-DESIRED DRIFT ON BOTH SPARKS IS A CANDIDATE CONSEQUENCE OF THIS CLASS AND NOT A FINDING: nobody has read a host back, and candidate is the correct word until someone does. RECOGNITION RULE: when a converge concludes from an observation, ask what the observation would say about a subject that is CORRECT BUT STALE -- if the probe answers the same for a current and an outdated instance, it is a liveness reading standing where a currency reading was needed. The tell is a remedy with no condition: an operation that is issued every time, or never, because no observation can distinguish the state it repairs.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }

data compensating_errors_cancel_in_the_aggregate: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "compensating_errors_cancel_in_the_aggregate" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**compensating errors cancel in the aggregate** (a completeness check compares a COUNT on each side instead of joining the two populations by IDENTITY, so a member missing from one side and a phantom member on the other cancel exactly, and the check reports the coverage it was written to refuse. The green is not a near miss: it is the check confirming a roster that covers nothing of the sort, and it is louder the longer both defects stand, because each new member added to either side keeps the totals in step. Distinct from `executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing`, where the conjunct can never go red: this one goes red readily on a SINGLE defect and is blind only to defects in opposing directions -- which is precisely the pair a long-lived roster accumulates, since the same neglect that leaves a new member unrostered leaves a deleted member rostered. Receipt (2026-09-01): `test.claim.language_source_scaffold_index_test.compiler_tests_rust_blobs_are_all_rostered` asserted `declared_fn_count(ct_) == rostered_count_for(v1.compiler.compiler_tests_rust)`. The tree carried 44 `ct_` blobs and 40 roster rows, so it was RED and enrolled in `v2.workflow.floor_expected_red` -- but the residues were not 4 of one kind. FIVE live blobs were unrostered and ONE row, `ct_caret_parse_smoke_native_witness_tests`, had outlived the blob #8532 deleted from the carrier. Rostering four of the five would have balanced the counts at 44 and greened the witness with one blob still unmarked and one row still naming a declaration that does not exist. The count was never the claim; it was a NECESSARY CONDITION of the claim being read as the claim. **Recognition rule: for any check whose sentence contains \"every\", \"all\" or \"covers\", ask what it would report if one member were missing from one side AND one phantom stood on the other. If the answer is \"green\", the check measures a cardinality and reports a coverage, and the two are joined by an assumption nothing enforces.** The remedy is the join: name the two residues separately -- present-not-covered and covered-not-present -- and assert each is empty, so the two directions red with distinct meanings and neither can pay for the other. Cardinality then survives as a third conjunct answering the one question containment cannot, a DUPLICATE within one side, and it is no longer the assertion. The evidence must not stop at the repaired tree, since a repaired population makes both live arms permanently green and the join indistinguishable from the count it replaced: the discriminating REDs belong over authored fixtures, with the equal-counts-different-identities case enrolled explicitly, because that is the one case the previous form accepted. NO SWEEP FOR SIBLINGS WAS PERFORMED, and that is a declared boundary rather than coverage: the recognition rule above is cheap enough to apply to any check whose sentence contains every, all or covers, and this repository certainly holds others, but the receipt below establishes the class at ONE subject and says nothing about the population. Reading this row as a census of aggregate-cardinality checks would be the same substitution it names.", evidence: [] }

data incidental_denominator_as_wall: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "incidental_denominator_as_wall" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**incidental denominator as a wall** (a destructive operation is safe only because an upstream filter written to answer a DIFFERENT question happens never to hand it the dangerous input. Nothing is wrong today and nothing declares why, so the safety is a coincidence with no authority, no diagnostic and no test — and it dissolves silently the moment the upstream question changes, which is a change nobody reads as touching safety. Distinct from `authority_substitution`, where PROSE invents an A-to-B arrow: here the CODE leans on an arrow that genuinely holds and that neither carrier claims, so grepping the guarded operation finds no guard to have gotten wrong. Receipt (2026-09-01): `v1_compiler.required_regen_host` `install_convergence_stage_with_backend` copies `candidate_src/<basename>` over `stage0_src/<basename>` for whatever roster it is handed, asking nothing about the artifact. The emitter really produces a bare `Cargo.toml` (`v1.compiler.emit_rust`); `write_emitted_tree` writes it into the candidate tree verbatim because it is not rustfmt-normalizable; `produce_candidate_manifest` rows it as a `GeneratedSurface` declared by that emitter. Every stage between the emitter and the copy admits it. The sole reason it never became an install target was `is_compared_generated_basename`, whose job is to denominate the DRIFT COMPARISON. **THE HARM CLAIM IS THE PART THIS ROW GOT WRONG FIRST, and the correction is the instructive half.** The finding was briefed, amplified through a manager and written into a work-item title as a destructive overwrite of the 172-line hand-maintained `src/v1/stage0/Cargo.toml`. It is not: the installer joins destinations under `stage0_src = workspace/src/v1/stage0/src`, so a bare `Cargo.toml` basename resolves one directory BELOW the manifest, to a path that does not exist. Widening the population alone writes debris rather than destruction ONLY IF the join is the whole story, and THAT CLAIM WAS ITSELF AN UNDER-ENUMERATION, caught in review of the repair: `fs::copy` follows the DESTINATION link, git tracks symlinks, so a committed stage0 entry that is a symlink reaches any path in the tree with the join untouched. The lesson generalizes past this row: a harm correction that names ONE mechanism and treats it as the requirement is the same coincidence-as-wall shape turned on the analysis -- the honest form enumerates the ROUTES to the destination and says which are closed, since `resolves outside X` is a property of the filesystem and not of the path expression. Two readers reached the destructive reading independently and agreement read as confirmation, which is why the deciding observation is a JOIN EXPRESSION and not a semantic comparison of the two files — the artifacts genuinely differ, and that true fact was fused with a destination claim it never established. **The surviving harm is exemption, not destruction, and it is the one worth naming:** a declared `GeneratedSurface` that the comparison filter hides is invisible to the fixed point (`first_generation_equal`, `changed_paths`) and unreachable by the one authority that would force its gap to be counted — `v2.compiler.self_host.stage0_crate_layout` `emitter_produced_divergent_registrations`, which already enforces in three directions and holds `main.rs` for exactly this relation. So the filter did not accidentally PROTECT the artifact; it accidentally EXEMPTED it. Beside it sat a second, CALLER-LESS installer, `install_candidate_paths`, equally unguarded and invisible to review because a crate-wide dead-code allow kept it compiling: an unguarded operation with no consumer still reads as sanctioned precedent for the next author. **Recognition rule: for every operation that mutates authoritative bytes, ask what it would do if handed the worst member of the population its input is DRAWN FROM — not the population it is called with today — then name the function that forbids that member and the question that function was written to answer. If those two questions differ, the wall is incidental and the operation has none.** The remedy is an admission at the mutation boundary itself, over the whole roster before the first byte moves and refusing rather than skipping, since a per-item skip re-exports the same silence one layer in; and it is honestly a mechanically-preventable rung, whose ceiling is structural impossibility once the plan projects a typed surface identity instead of a `List<String>`. **THE REMEDY HAS ITS OWN TRAP, AND THIS ROW WALKED INTO IT BEFORE CATCHING IT: restating the incidental denominator as the guard's own rule.** The first repair refused every non-`.rs` install target, which reads as a wall and is the SAME defect dualised — the accidental denominator promoted from coincidence to policy, in a second location, now refusing the correct end state by construction, since the emitted manifest is stage0's own and is supposed to converge. **Recognition rule for the repair: state the arm's reason, and check whether it forbids the state the system is trying to REACH.** If it does, the guard has ratified the coincidence instead of replacing it, and the honest arms are the ones the boundary can answer from its own facts — here a path that cannot address its own destination, and a hand-authored mirror — while the artifact-kind question goes back to the authority that owns dispositions. **SECOND RECEIPT, AND IT IS FILED HERE RATHER THAN AS A NEW CLASS BECAUSE THE MECHANISM IS IDENTICAL WHILE THE POLARITY IS INVERTED (measured 2026-09-02 at dc878756107b).** The receipt above is an upstream filter that accidentally KEEPS a destructive operation safe. This one is an upstream filter that accidentally KILLS a declared wall. gunbc#9824 moved the namespace transition-admission roster's cleanup bill off bystanders by making a provably consumed row an inert typed receipt, and put the deletion obligation in one arm: a consumed row refuses on the first change whose diff touches the roster's own source file. v1_compiler.cli_run.namespace_wave_admission.run_required_wave_admission computes that arm's predicate as roster_touched over the head side returned by diff_sides -- whose final act retains only paths satisfying in_sweep_scope, a predicate that opens by requiring a .dag suffix, while ADMISSION_ROSTER_REL_PATH names a .rs file. A .rs path cannot survive a .dag filter, so roster_touched is false on every production run and consumed_due in claim_executor.report_wave_admission_outcome can never be true. in_sweep_scope was written to answer WHICH FILES THE PARSER RE-READS to reconstruct the baseline; nothing joins it to the deletion obligation it silently decides, and that is this row's mechanism unchanged. **THE RECOGNITION RULE ABOVE CATCHES BOTH POLARITIES WITHOUT AMENDMENT and this receipt exists so the next holder of a dead arm recognises themselves in a row whose other specimen is accidentally safe:** naming the function that decides the operation and the question that function was written to answer is polarity-free, and the two questions differ here exactly as they differ there. **WHAT THE INVERTED POLARITY COSTS THAT THE SAFE ONE DOES NOT, and it is the reason the inversion is worth carrying:** an accidentally-safe operation still behaves correctly today, so the debt is latent. An accidentally-dead wall is cited as coverage while it is dead -- in a merged pull-request body, in the arm's own doc comment, and to every reader who greps for the arm and finds it present, gated on, and reached. Every reachability-based tell reports health, because the arm IS reached; what never happens is that its predicate is true. The declared window it guarded (roster-use bounded) is therefore unbounded in execution, which gunbc.rung_drop namespace_admission_consumed_row_deletion now declares.)", evidence: [] }

data restored_bytes_reviewed_as_authorship: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "restored_bytes_reviewed_as_authorship" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**restored bytes reviewed as authorship** (a clobber repair returns content a prior PR already merged and a prior reviewer already accepted, but a diff has no way to say so: the restored lines are ADDED LINES, so a reviewer attributes them to the repairing PR and reviews them as new work. Specimen: gunbc#9937 restored two rows that gunbc#9868 had reverted off a stale base, and review 58203 filed REQUEST_CHANGES against a DESIGN section 6 transcribed-count defect in bytes that are character-for-character gunbc#9888's merged row -- a finding correct on its merits and misaddressed by one PR. **THE SECOND-ORDER EFFECT IS WHY THIS IS A CLASS AND NOT AN ANECDOTE: it makes clobber repairs EXPENSIVE TO LAND, which biases the fleet toward leaving clobbers standing.** The repairing lane inherits review debt for content it did not write, and the only way to discharge it inside the repair is to edit another lane's cells from a base lacking their context -- which is precisely the failure the repair exists to undo, committed a second time with better manners. RECOGNITION RULE: a diff whose added lines are byte-identical to a prior merged blob. It is DECIDABLE rather than a judgement call -- `cmp` against `git show <sha>:<path>` answers it, and provenance for the whole region comes from `git log -S` naming the commit that added the text and the commit that removed it. THE REMEDY IS THE AUTHOR'S AND IT IS CHEAP: state the restoration ahead of the diff and carry the byte-identity receipt, so a reviewer meets provenance before content; without it the same finding is re-filed against the same bytes on every re-review, and the loop is paid for twice. A finding against restored bytes is well-formed and BINDS THE DESTINATION: provenance decides who answers it and in which diff, and never whether it is answered. **THE WRONG READING OF THIS ROW WAS AUTHORED AND REFUSED IN ITS OWN FILING** (review 58220): an earlier revision said such a finding 'belongs in its own diff', which reads as licence to merge a known defect behind an authorship argument -- DESIGN section 5's hard reject, and inverted, since a restoration is exactly the motion that puts the bytes back on main. What actually happened on the specimen is the rule: the reviewer's section 6 finding was correct, the repairing lane argued for routing it elsewhere, the owning manager OVERRULED that, and the defect was repaired inside the restoration under a ruling -- which is what made the edit a decision rather than one lane rewriting another's cells. Routing is a question about AUTHORITY and context, decided by whoever owns both lanes; the bytes are reviewed at their destination either way. **Rung: mitigatable** -- the author states the restoration and carries a byte-identity receipt, and a reviewer may still miss it. **Ceiling: mechanically preventable**, because the recognition rule is decidable: a tool that joins each added line against the merged blobs of the commits git log -S names can annotate a diff as restored before a human reads it. It is not structural -- nothing can make a restoration unwritable, nor should it. **Next-rung trigger, at capability grain: the review surface distinguishes restored bytes from authored bytes without the author asserting it**, since an author-supplied notice is exactly the evidence a tired or adversarial diff will omit. **THE RECEIPT MUST BE TAKEN AT THE DESTINATION AND NOT AT THE SOURCE, and that is the transferable half.** `cmp` decides the git case because it reads the bytes where they LANDED, not the bytes an author meant to send; the general shape is ANY step between assertion and delivery altering content while the delivery reports success -- and the step is not always the one a reader would blame first. Measured the same day in three places, and the THIRD one is a caution about naming the culprit too early: git's merge region dropped a row outside the conflict markers; a review read merged bytes as authored ones; and two sessions' messages arrived with a backticked identifier deleted and a dollar-variable replaced by a plausible shell path, which BOTH of them first attributed to the message transport. That attribution was wrong, and it was settled by measurement rather than by reasoning: a third session kept the local source of a sent message, read the delivered body back out of the store, and diffed them -- identical but for a trailing newline, with backticks, a backslash continuation and a dollar-brace token all intact. The corruption was in the SENDER'S OWN SHELL, expanding an inline double-quoted argument before the tool ever saw it, and the proposed remedy of banning backticks would have cost a real notation to avoid a hazard that lives in a construction nobody has to use. A deletion leaves a gap a reader might notice; a substitution leaves a syntactically fine claim that is simply false, which is why source-side confidence is not evidence at all.)", evidence: [] }

data review_summary_inverts_roles_and_affirms_the_join: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "review_summary_inverts_roles_and_affirms_the_join" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a review summary that inverts real roles and then affirms the join** (a review names files that all exist, assigns each the wrong role, and closes by asserting the one property it was uniquely positioned to test. Specimen: review 58215 approved gunbc#9937 at `fafd2adc7e1` with *'restoration of two ledger rows to recurring_failure_mode.dag ... plus an accompanying prose update in the gap-analysis doc ... Diff is narrow and matches the PR title.'* The carrier held ONE added row, not two; that row was a NEW class row, not a restoration of anything; the actual restoration was the docs file it demoted to 'accompanying'; and the diff did NOT match the title, because the `.dag` file had been swept in by a staged-change leak the PR body never declared. **DISTINGUISH IT FROM A HALLUCINATED SUBJECT, which is the neighbouring failure and a much easier one:** review 58070 described a `match` arm that appeared nowhere in its diff, and an invention is refutable by grep. Here EVERY NOUN IS PRESENT IN THE TREE and only the relations between them are wrong, so the usual defence -- check that the cited things exist -- returns all-clear. **THE AFFIRMATION IS THE HARM AND NOT THE MISDESCRIPTION.** A lane cannot audit its own title-versus-diff agreement with fresh eyes; a reviewer can, and this one asserted that agreement in the exact PR where it failed. A review that stays silent on a property leaves the check undone; a review that affirms it wrongly marks the check DONE, which is worse and is why this is not merely a low-quality summary. RECOGNITION RULE, and it is decidable rather than a matter of reading care: join the changed-FILE set against what the title and body claim to change, at file grain, and refuse any file the body does not account for. That join is mechanical, needs no understanding of the diff, and would have fired here. **THE BACKSTOP QUESTION IS THE SECOND HALF OF THE ROW, and its answer is honest rather than comforting:** the leaked roster row carried no regenerated `DESIGN.md` or `docs/design-ledgers.md`, and by construction the required build lane's generated-artifact phase compares every `CommitRequired` projection against its authority, so it WOULD have refused. It did not get the chance -- that lane was CANCELLED on the leaked sha when the next push superseded it, and the leak was caught by the author re-reading the diff. So the backstop is real and was not what caught it, and a row claiming the gate held here would be asserting an execution that never ran. **Rung: mitigatable** -- the harm is contained only by a second reader noticing, and on the specimen the second reader was the author. **Ceiling: mechanically preventable**, and no higher: whether a summary DESCRIBES a diff correctly is not decidable, so no construction forbids the bad summary -- but the one clause that did the damage is decidable, because a changed-file set and a body are both machine-readable. **Next-rung trigger, at capability grain: no review verdict is admissible unless a changed-FILE-set join against the declared scope has executed and passed** -- not a reviewer instructed to check it, which is the same assertion that failed here, and not a lint on summary wording, which would ratchet the prose while leaving the join undone.)", evidence: [] }
data admitted_module_without_judged_standing: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "admitted_module_without_judged_standing" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a source-ingested module has no judged standing** (the required gates adjudicate entry-derived closures, while source-root ingest admits a larger identity population; a module outside every required closure can carry a structurally checkable defect while every gate stays green. This is NOT an import-edge class: globally unique names can resolve without a direct import, so authored inbound imports neither prove nor disprove judgment. It is also NOT a claim that every identity outside the closures is defective or should be gated. The severity is unknown, and that unknowability is the finding. **SPECIMEN AND DISCRIMINATING CONTROL** (node://adhoc-2d3c27b7-660, PR #9899): gunbc.annotation_parse_instrument_agreement constructed Terminal { reason, authority } although Terminal declares only reason; a clean required run left both build and witnesses green and both in-run judgment receipts omitted the module. The matched visible control placed the same undeclared-field construction in ordinary production module gunbc.clock_read: both required lanes refused with `field 'authority' not found in type 'LaneVisibilityControl'`; removing only the plant returned both lanes to green. Thus visibility, with defect class held constant, discriminates the arms. The witnesses prediction was weaker than its result: only submitted-closure membership was known beforehand, yet execution established strict judgment by refusing. **MEASUREMENT, EXPLICITLY NOT COVERAGE OR ENFORCEMENT:** the producer joins every first-party identity admitted by the exact source-root ingest against the union of module identities for which build or witnesses produced a strict typecheck verdict. On clean run 33484666539 it derived 4,419 admitted, 947 build-judged, 2,158 witnesses-judged, 2,319 in the judgment union, and 2,100 with no required-lane judgment. Build contributes only 161 identities beyond witnesses, so the two required closures are far from independent and their union remains close to one lane's reach. Exactly one of the 2,100 is confirmed orphaned by the executed control; the other 2,099 are Undecided because no typed authority currently says whether each is an executing standalone entry, fixture/generated/excluded, retired, or orphaned. Those identities are deliberately re-derived and NOT committed as a baseline or roster: a hand-carried 2,099-row exemption set would be a ratchet wearing a wall's name. The instrument reports; it does not refuse, and citing it as a gate is rung inflation. **PROVENANCE LIMIT:** in-run strict judgments and cross-process content-addressed cache judgments are separate columns. Required CI does not arm GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR, so the cross-process column was empty beside nonempty in-run columns in both planted and reverted runs. That empty column is a control for the unarmed premise, NOT evidence that the provenance split is exercised by required CI. **CEILING: decidable but waiting on a single standing authority.** A wall now would either false-red legitimate importer-free subjects or grandfather opaque debt. The next rung requires four capabilities together: (1) one typed standing registry exhaustively binds every first-party ingest identity to required judgment, a verified executing consumer, typed fixture/generated/exclusion, retirement, or orphan standing; (2) each executing-consumer binding is checked against the named consumer's actual roster and execution receipt, so a hollow alias cannot admit it; (3) a changed retained identity resolves only through its named consumer from materialized facts within the required floor's 8-second wall and 500-millisecond CPU envelopes, never by whole-corpus compilation; and (4) the two-direction matched undeclared-field control remains executable. At that rung admission makes the invalid state unwritable; until then this remains measurement and an Undecided population, not a defect backlog.)",
  evidence: [],
}

data fabricated_debt: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "fabricated_debt" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**fabricated debt** (a declaration is authored for an exposure that does not exist, or that is already declared elsewhere, so the ledger grows a row whose trigger CANNOT FIRE because there is nothing to restore. It is the exact inverse of the unfiled gap and it is the more comfortable mistake: filing reads as diligence, the row survives review because every reviewer checks whether a declared drop is HONEST about its loss and none checks whether the loss is REAL, and the cost lands on whoever later tries to retire it. **THE HARM IS NOT MERELY CLUTTER, WHICH IS WHY IT IS A CLASS.** A drop is retired BY ITS TRIGGER AND BY NOTHING ELSE, so a row for a non-existent exposure is permanent by construction; it inflates the standing-drops list that DESIGN projects on every turn of every session, and the next reader plans against an exposure nobody has. A row DUPLICATING an existing declaration is worse still: it forks the single authority for one safety fact, so the two can be retired independently and the tree ends up asserting both that the class is dropped and that it is restored. **THE ORIGIN IS ALWAYS THE SAME, and naming it is the recognition rule: the population was read from a PARAGRAPH rather than measured from the tree.** A loss clause enumerates what was unguarded on the day it was written; capabilities return, get re-homed, or acquire their own declarations, and the sentence does not move. So the rule is: before authoring a drop, resolve every named item against the tree -- is this exposure live NOW, and does it already have a row? **TWO RECEIPTS, both caught before authoring, 2026-09-01, while splitting `gunbc.rung_drop` `floor_cut`'s six-capability loss into capability-grain rows.** (1) GENERATED-ARTIFACT DRIFT was on the loss clause's list and is RESTORED -- gunbc#9415 enrolled a required `generated-artifact` phase adjudicating every member of `committed_generated_artifacts`; the same paragraph elsewhere admits the phase took it off the list, so the row contradicted itself and a reader following the enumeration would have declared a drop for a live gate. It is now stated as a FRACTION, 1 of 7 discharged and 6 outstanding, because a population that shrinks silently cannot be checked. (2) THE PER-WITNESS EVAL DEADLINE was on the same list and ALREADY CARRIES ITS OWN DROP at `gunbc.witness_row_cost` `gunbc_ci_fast_lane_rule_note`; a second row would have been the section 3 fork, and it is cited from the sibling rows rather than re-declared. Six items on the paragraph, five real rows. **NEIGHBOURS, and the boundaries are what keep this from absorbing them.** Distinct from `unbacked_execution_claim`: there prose asserts a live relation that no authority backs, and the subject EXISTS while the claim about it is false; here the subject itself is absent and the claim of loss is the fabrication. Distinct from `rung inflation`, which reports a class as SAFER than its evidence supports -- this reports the tree as MORE EXPOSED than it is, and both mislead the same reader in opposite directions. Distinct from `restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist`, which is a REAL exposure with an unsatisfiable trigger; this is an unreal exposure, and the two are found by the same question asked at different ends -- does the trigger name something that exists, and does the LOSS name something that exists. **RUNG: 1 (mitigatable) -- caught by a reader resolving the population, which is exactly what happened here and is not a mechanism. CEILING: 3, since `does this exposure exist` is decidable for any loss expressed as a citation to a mechanism rather than as prose. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY: a drop row whose lost capability is carried as a resolvable citation to the mechanism that provided it, so a row declaring the loss of something the tree still has -- or something another row already declares -- fails to compile. Enumerating populations more carefully by hand does not retire it; it only executes this row's recognition rule once more.)" as NonEmptyStr, evidence: [] }
data alias_resolution_collides_with_kernel_spelling: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "alias_resolution_collides_with_kernel_spelling" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**an instrument resolves an alias, lands on a name that COLLIDES with a kernel spelling, and attributes the result to the kernel** (the reference under measurement is authored QUALIFIED and points at a type alias; the reader resolves the alias, arrives at the alias declaration's own name, and that name is also a kernel name -- so the row is attributed to the kernel identity, naming THE EXACT CARRIER THE QUALIFICATION WAS WRITTEN TO MOVE AWAY FROM. **IT DOES NOT FAIL TO ANSWER; IT ANSWERS CONFIDENTLY AND WRONGLY**, and that is the whole severity: a missing answer is visible to its consumer and an inverted one is not, so the two rank completely differently and only the second can be cited as evidence for the opposite of what holds. **Distinct from `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content`, and the boundary is worth stating because they were found in the same instrument in the same hour**: there a report is COMPLETE for the reporter and read as complete for the consumer, so the defect is in the READING; here the report is wrong on a specific row it does examine, so the defect is in the INSTRUMENT and no amount of careful reading recovers it. Also distinct from `hollow_alias`, which is about a second name minted for one concept: the alias here is legitimate modelling, and what fails is a reader of it. **SPECIMEN, with a discriminating probe executed on covered ground (2026-09-01, gunbc#9907 follow-up).** `v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census` reports, for two functions appended to `v2.compiler.tokenize` on adjacent lines with identical position kind, differing only in alias-versus-concrete: a param authored `std.determinism.Determinism` keeps its dotted name, while a param authored `v2.std.text.String` comes back as bare `String` attributed to `<kernel:String>`. `v2.std.text` declares `type String = FreeMonoid<Char>`, so the alias name collides with the kernel spelling. Both probes produced rows (17661 -> 17663), which is what makes the negative half evidence rather than absence -- the positive control is the whole discriminator, and the same census had already produced a null result on an uncovered fixture whose emptiness was indistinguishable from confirmation. **CONSEQUENCE MEASURED, NOT IMAGINED**: read naively, the census contradicted the namespace wall about nine function declarations and would have been read as nine admission rows asserting a binding the carrier lacks, on a merged PR. The wall was right; the contradiction was this bug. **RUNG: MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE AT BEST TODAY AND CURRENTLY UNENROLLED** -- the wrong answer is produced silently and nothing executes over it. The next-rung trigger is that two-line probe being ENROLLED as a discriminating RED in any covered module, which is cheap; a class whose RED is two lines and still does not execute has no excuse, and naming the cheapness is what makes it rank rather than sit. **Recognition rule**: wherever a reader resolves through an alias, ask whether the resolved name could collide with a name in a DIFFERENT namespace the reader also knows -- kernel, prelude, or ambient -- because at that point the reader cannot tell them apart and will pick one silently.)", evidence: [] }
data yaml_inline_comment_ingested_as_scalar_content: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "yaml_inline_comment_ingested_as_scalar_content" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a YAML inline comment is ingested as scalar content** (a bounded YAML reader that does not model comment separation accepts `key: value # comment` and stores `value # comment` as the value, so a syntactically valid document is silently assigned the wrong tree. Measured 2026-09-01 against `extdeps.languages.yaml.ingest` `ingest_yaml_source`: a column-zero full-line comment and an indented full-line comment both refused loudly as malformed mapping entries; an inline trailing comment was accepted and reserialized as a quoted scalar containing the comment; a hash-leading line inside a block literal was accepted and preserved as content. The last arm is the discriminating control because generated workflow run blocks contain shell comments and issue references such as `#5828`; a line-wide hash filter would reject or delete real scalar content. Repair: full-line comments are skipped only at parser block boundaries, never in literal collection, while recognizable unquoted inline comments now produce `YamlIngestRejected` until lexical inline separation is modeled. **APPROXIMATION DIRECTION:** the temporary predicate intentionally over-refuses richer unquoted scalar forms containing separation-whitespace (space or tab) followed by hash that this bounded parser does not model, excludes double-quoted scalars, and never examines block-literal content; it does not claim full YAML comment lexing. Rung: mitigatable -- the silent wrong tree becomes a typed refusal. Ceiling: structurally guaranteed once comment separation is a lexical production in the YAML grammar, so comment bytes cannot enter scalar content except through quoted or block scalar productions. Next-rung trigger: inline YAML 1.2.2 comment separation modeled lexically rather than recognized by the temporary value-text refusal.",
  evidence: [],
}

data accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**accepted source emits uncompilable target** (INVALID STATE: a .dag construction the front end accepts with zero blocking diagnostics, whose emission is a target program the target compiler refuses. The instance filed here is a coproduct's UNIT VARIANT standing in a NON-APPLIED TYPE POSITION -- a field, parameter or return type spelled with a constructor rather than a type. HARM: section 5 silent wrongness on the source-to-target path. gunbc says Accepted and hands over a program that cannot build, so the only wall that fires belongs to the target's compiler; where a target has no such wall, or where the emitted artifact is never compiled, nothing fires at all. Section 7 makes this the seed's floor and not the target's problem: the .dag graph is the authority and Rust is one realization, so 'rustc catches it' is exactly the outsourcing this project exists to end. THE SPECIMEN IS CARRIED IN THIS ROW RATHER THAN CITED, because the fixture that produced it was never committed to this repository (neat-otter-332, 2026-09-01). Its emitted artifacts are held by that lane's own receipts; no path is given here, since a path outside this repository is not a citation a later reader can resolve. Authored source, two modules: `scope.provider` declares `type Quantity = Time | Memory`; `scope.consumer` does `import scope.provider \{ Quantity, Time \}`, `type NonApplied \{ value: Time \}`, `fn field_as_quantity(subject: NonApplied) -> Quantity \{ subject.value \}`. gunbc accepts it. DISTINGUISHING FACT, and the reason this class must not be read off the target's error code: WHAT rustc says is decided by what else the emitter minted, not by the source defect. Under the NARROW emitter classifier the consumer emits `pub use crate::scope_provider::\{Quantity\};` then `use crate::scope_provider::Quantity::\{Time\};` with no marker binding, and `pub struct NonApplied \{ pub value: Time \}` refuses `error[E0573]: expected type, found variant Time` at `src/scope_consumer.rs:15:16` on `pub value: Time,`, label `not a type`, help `consider importing this struct instead`. Under the BROAD classifier the consumer instead emits `pub use crate::scope_provider::\{Time\};` beside `\{Quantity\}` -- the provider having emitted `pub enum Quantity \{ Time, Memory \}` AND `pub struct Time;` -- so the field declaration COMPILES, and the refusal moves to the function: `error[E0308]: mismatched types` at `src/scope_consumer.rs:20:5` on `subject.value.clone()`, `expected Quantity, found Time`, against `expected Quantity because of return type`. INDEPENDENTLY REPRODUCED AT PARAMETER POSITION on this branch, 2026-09-01 on gunbc baeabbbf80, by a single-file source handed to the compiler: `type StampMode = StampClass | StampOther` with `fn take(stamp: StampClass) -> StampMode \{ stamp \}`. `gunbc compile --target rust` exits 0 with 0 blocking errors, emits `pub fn take(stamp: StampClass) -> StampMode` beside `pub struct StampClass;`, and `cargo check` on the emitted crate refuses `E0308 expected StampMode, found StampClass`. One source defect; E0573, E0308-at-the-parent, and E0308-at-the-body depending on emission. THE MASK IS THE SHARP HALF, and it is fabricated plausible output rather than a lucky green: the broad classifier's marker import made the FIELD-ONLY source compile by substituting a distinct struct for a variant. It never preserved the modelled meaning, and extending the SAME accepted source across its declared parent boundary -- the function returning `Quantity` -- is what exposes it. So the narrow classifier's E0573 is this class becoming VISIBLE, not a regression the narrowing introduced. GENERAL FORM: a green obtained because the emitter manufactured a target-only entity for a source name is not evidence the source is well-typed, and the discriminator is to extend the source past the boundary the manufactured entity does not model. THE ONE .dag-SIDE SIGNAL IS ABOUT THE WRONG QUESTION: on the parameter reproduction the compile printed the ADVISORY `unlisted import use 'StampClass' (referenced but not in any import's name list)`. It fires because the name was not found among types -- the front end reached the exact fact that decides this case and reported it as import hygiene. It is not a partial wall: it is advisory, it names listing rather than type position, and the field specimen above IMPORTS `Time` explicitly, so it does not fire there at all (see `diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent`). RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder, established by execution at the emission boundary -- the compile accepts and the emitted crate refuses. Section 4b's rung-1 mitigations are absent: nothing at the .dag boundary is typed, located or countable about this construction. CEILING: 4, structurally impossible, and the reason is that constructor identity and type identity are two distinct modelled facts whose membership is decidable from the coproduct declaration -- a variant name is reachable from that declaration as an ARM and never as a type, so the type-position slot has no constructor that admits it. No undecidable predicate is involved, so this is a wall now and not a ratchet. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, PHRASED AT CLASS GRAIN, phrased as the capability that retires the row rather than an artifact that would contribute to one: FRONT-END TYPE AGREEMENT for every construction whose emission carries a type obligation, sufficient that NO Accepted program emits a target program its compiler refuses on a type ground. That capability has one component per mechanism this row carries, and the row retires only when ALL of them hold: (i) type-position name resolution that consults the TYPE namespace alone and refuses a name resolving to a constructor with a located diagnostic, sufficient that no Accepted program contains a variant name in any non-applied type position -- field, parameter or return; (ii) arm-type agreement across a match, sufficient that no Accepted program mixes a coproduct constructor with a kernel literal across the arms of one match; (iii) agreement between the two renderings of an arrow at a call argument, sufficient that no Accepted program passes a function VALUE where the emitted parameter's rendering cannot accept it. Repairing any specimen, narrowing the emitter classifier, or adding a fixture satisfies less than any one component and retires no part of this row. WHY THE TRIGGER IS STATED THIS WAY, recorded because the row previously said otherwise and a reviewer was right to refuse it: the trigger read as (i) ALONE while the row's population had grown to three mechanisms, so satisfying it would have RETIRED THE ROW WHILE TWO OF ITS OWN DOCUMENTED FAILURES REMAINED AUTHORABLE -- DESIGN section 4b(3)'s grain mismatch exactly, a plural loss under a singular trigger. Noting the mismatch inside the row, which is what the function-value paragraph originally did, DOCUMENTS the defect rather than repairing it: a trigger that a row's own prose admits is too narrow is still the trigger the row will be retired by, since a drop is retired BY ITS TRIGGER AND BY NOTHING ELSE. RECOGNITION RULE: when the target compiler names a symbol at a type position, check whether that symbol is declared as an ARM of a coproduct in the source; if it is, the defect is in accepted .dag and the target compiler is the only wall that fired. SCOPE STATED RATHER THAN GENERALISED: executed for a unit arm at a field type and at a parameter type, Rust target only. Record-shaped arms, applied positions such as `List<Time>`, and other targets were not measured and are not claimed.) **SECOND SPECIMEN, AND ITS SUBJECT IS THE CHANGE THAT WAS CONSTRUCTING THE DISTINCTION IT VIOLATED** (quick-crab-396, 2026-09-02, the type_reference_decl_file state-space split). v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census identity_query_provenance declares a return type of std.coercion TypeDeclarationProvenance and answers it in five arms: three return the bound provenance and two -- IdentitiesDisagree and IdentityUnavailableBoth -- returned the empty string. The front end ACCEPTED it with zero blocking diagnostics, emit produced the mirror, and rustc refused the mirror at E0308 `match arms have incompatible types`, expected Rc<TypeDeclarationProvenance>, found String. THE SPECIMEN IS WORTH MORE THAN THE FIX because of what the two bad arms were: this change exists to replace `decl_file: String` with a coproduct precisely so that ABSENT declaration identity is a constructor (DeclarationIdentityAbsent) instead of an empty string -- so the uncompilable arms were the exact conflation the change was built to make unwritable, surviving inside the change that makes it unwritable. RECOGNITION RULE, and it is narrower than 'run the emitter': a match whose arms MIX a coproduct constructor with a kernel literal is the shape, and it is invisible to a reader who checks that every arm is present, because exhaustiveness holds and only the arm TYPES disagree. WHAT THE ROW ESTABLISHES ABOUT THE RUNG: the class is still mechanically preventable and not structural -- the refusal fired in the TARGET compiler, one phase and one language too late, and the .dag front end that had every fact needed to refuse it did not. The next-rung trigger is unchanged and this instance sharpens rather than moves it. (AMENDED WHEN THE FUNCTION-VALUE INSTANCE LANDED, and the amendment is to the trigger's GRAIN rather than to this specimen's reading: the trigger has since been restated at class grain with one component per mechanism, and THIS specimen is component (ii). The sentence above stays because it was right about what the specimen does -- it sharpens rather than moves -- and what changed is that the row stopped stating one mechanism's trigger as though it were the class's.) **A FURTHER INSTANCE, AND IT MASKS BY A DIFFERENT MECHANISM FROM THE FIELD AND PARAMETER SPECIMENS -- CANDIDATE EVIDENCE, NOT A RUNG.** (Deliberately not numbered: this row gained a specimen from another lane while this one was in flight, and an ordinal written at authoring time is wrong the moment a second lane appends. The specimens are named by their shape.) Executed by snappy-koi-286, 2026-09-02, and carried in gunbc#9989 (`The function-value adapter, judged by rustc`), which is OPEN at this writing -- so this points at the PR carrying the fixtures rather than asserting paths that resolve on main today. SUBJECT: the function-value adapter at the call position in `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `rust_call_arg_function_value_adapt`. An arrow type has TWO Rust renderings -- a function VALUE renders through `callable_type_template` as a reference-counted dyn Fn, a function-typed PARAMETER renders through `emit_rust_param_type` as `impl Fn(..) -> .. + Clone` -- and the reference-counted form carries no blanket Fn impl the way a boxed one does. The adapter closes that seam, and it fires ONLY when the argument is spelled as a CALL EXPRESSION. SOURCE HANDED TO THE COMPILER, three declarations in one import-free module: `fn let_add(k: Int) -> fn(Int) -> Int` returning a closure over `k`; `fn let_apply(f: fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int) -> Int` applying it; and a probe that binds `let_add(k: 1)` TO A LET AND THEN PASSES THE BINDING to `let_apply`. GUNBC'S VERDICT: ACCEPTED, zero blocking diagnostics -- and that is established BY THE ROUTE REFUSING TO REPORT IT OTHERWISE, not by reading a success line: `v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host` `FixtureClosureOutcome` separates `SourceRefused` from `Measured`, a `SourceRefused` fails the pair rather than producing a rustc verdict, and this arm reports Measured. RUSTC'S VERDICT ON THE EMITTED CRATE: cargo completes non-zero with error[E0277], expected a `Fn(i64)` closure, found `Rc<dyn Fn(i64) -> i64>`, attributed to the FIXTURE'S OWN emitted module at the call rather than to some other member of the closure, and the note reads required by a bound in `let_apply` -- THE BOUND IS ON THE CONSUMER, `pub fn let_apply(f: impl Fn(i64) -> i64 + Clone, x: i64)`, which is the half that makes this the two-renderings SEAM and not a random type error. THE POSITIVE CONTROL IS WHAT MAKES THIS AN INSTANCE OF THE CLASS RATHER THAN A BROKEN FIXTURE, and it is the sharp half: a sibling fixture is THE SAME PROGRAM WITH ONE AUTHORED DIFFERENCE -- the producer's result passed directly as a call expression instead of through the let binding -- and it emits and compiles clean. Same producer, same consumer, same call; the only variable is whether the adapter fired. INSTRUMENT NAMED RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED, per DESIGN section 6: the opt-in pair authored in that same OPEN PR as an ignored `v1-compiler` lib test naming the function-value adapter fixture-closure discrimination -- described rather than spelled, because an identity under review may be renamed before it lands, and a bare name that no longer resolves reads as correct; three runs on three bases agree, the latest on that PR's integrated head. WHAT IT ADDS TO THE CLASS, and it is why it is filed rather than folded into the field and parameter specimens: those mask through a MANUFACTURED TARGET ENTITY -- the emitter minting a target-only struct for a source name -- so their discriminator is to extend the source past the boundary that entity does not model. This one masks through a CALL-SITE SPELLING: one source meaning emits compilable or uncompilable target depending on whether an INTERMEDIATE BINDING WAS AUTHORED, with no manufactured entity anywhere. So the class has a second discriminator, and it is cheap: RE-SPELL AN ACCEPTED CALL THROUGH A LET AND RE-EMIT. WHAT THIS INSTANCE DOES NOT ESTABLISH, stated because the consumer's standing makes it easy to overclaim: the pair is ignored by default and `rust-unit-tests` is not a `needs` of the required aggregate, so nothing executes over it on the required path. It is CANDIDATE EVIDENCE. It establishes no rung and it discharges no component of the next-rung trigger above -- including component (iii), which is the component this instance's own mechanism names: exhibiting a failure is not building the wall against it. SCOPE THIS INSTANCE ADDS, stated locally so the row keeps ONE scope sentence rather than two that could drift: a function-typed argument passed through a let binding, Rust target only. It widens the scope sentence above by that one position and claims nothing beyond it.",
  evidence: [],
}
data selection_view_read_as_population: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "selection_view_read_as_population" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a selection view read as the population** (a decidable predicate is written over MEASURED values -- cost at or above N, latency under N, rows a report printed -- and its output is then treated as the population of the class under study. Membership in that set is a property of THE MEASUREMENT, not of the subject: it moves when the instrument moves, when load moves, when the reporter truncates, while the subject is unchanged. The set and the population are two objects joined by an assumption nobody states, and the assumption is false exactly when the measured quantity carries an unbounded term the threshold cannot see beneath. **WHAT MAKES THIS DIFFERENT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS IS THE ROUTE IT ARRIVES BY, AND THAT IS ALSO THE WHOLE DIFFICULTY: IT ARRIVES AS THE FIX FOR A REAL OBJECTION.** `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content` is a report read past its own promise, and its closest unnamed relative here is a statistic computed over the observations that SURVIVED a threshold on the very variable being estimated -- filed separately as `censored_estimator_drops_its_own_tail`, and cited here by identity because that row now resolves in this tree; it was carried descriptively while it was unlanded, since a boundary drawn against a symbol that does not resolve is worse than a boundary drawn descriptively. Both of those are errors in the READING. This one is produced BY diligence. The predicate is decidable, it is honestly derived, and it is very often the correct answer to a legitimate refusal -- which is precisely why the next question does not get asked. **BEING CAREFUL IS WHAT MAKES IT INVISIBLE: the diligence is spent on the repair, and the repair's correctness is what stops anyone asking whether it answers the question that was posed.** A defect arriving inside a correct fix is not caught by the diligence that produced the fix. SPECIMEN, WITH BOTH ENDS BELONGING TO THE SAME AUTHOR THREE HOURS APART, which is why it is filed rather than blamed. (i) A peer lane computed a median and p95 over the rows a required-floor run's `[over-cost]` listing PRINTED -- an instrument that ranks by cost and truncates to a fixed head, and whose own closing line says so and names the per-claim cost artifact the run uploads as the complete population. This author correctly told them an order statistic of a truncated tail describes nothing, because the truncation is a property of the REPORTER. THE TWO PRODUCERS ARE NAMED RATHER THAN THEIR OUTPUTS TRANSCRIBED, per DESIGN section 6: the truncated view is that `[over-cost]` listing, and the population is `required_floor_claim_cost.tsv` as uploaded by the same run -- either is re-derivable from any floor run, and no count here needs to be trusted. (ii) The same author then had a declared drop refused for defining its population as `every required row whose headroom is smaller than the observed inflation` while calling that inflation censored with no upper bound -- an undecidable membership predicate, correctly refused under DESIGN section 4b(3). The fix was a decidable admission rule over each run's own per-claim cost artifact, which was the right repair for the refusal, and its output was then written into the row AS THE POPULATION. With an unbounded contention term, no lower threshold can prove the rows beneath it unaffected, so the set was a view the whole time. REPAIR: name the closed subject universe from the SUBJECT rather than from any measurement -- for the specimen, every required identity for which the cpu deadline is armed while it executes under the uncontrolled shared-runner envelope -- and keep the threshold set, which is genuinely useful, under an honest name: an EXPOSED ATTENTION SUBSET for prioritising work. A COROLLARY WORTH CARRYING SEPARATELY, because conflating the two hides the seam: the evidence floor behind such a threshold may be MONOTONE while the membership set is NOT. An observed floor only rises, so a constant derived from it only falls; individual identities still enter and leave the subset as their measured values vary. Monotonicity of the bound says nothing about stability of the set. **RECOGNITION RULE: when a set is produced by comparing a MEASURED value against a threshold, ask what the set would contain if the measurement were taken again under different conditions -- and ask it hardest when the predicate was just written to satisfy a reviewer, because that is the moment the answer feels settled.**)", evidence: [] }

data unlanded_citation_indistinguishable_at_the_citing_end: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "unlanded_citation_indistinguishable_at_the_citing_end" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a citation to a symbol that has not landed** (a canonical row cites an identity that exists only in an OPEN PR, so on main -- the tree the row lands in -- the citation resolves to nothing. **THE MECHANISM IS THAT THE TWO STATES ARE INDISTINGUISHABLE AT THE CITING END.** A name that resolves and a name that will resolve are the same text in the same position; nothing at the point of authorship separates them, so this is not carelessness and reading more carefully does not find it. The check that discriminates is a LOOKUP AGAINST MAIN; the check an author naturally performs is a lookup against their own context, in which the symbol is vividly present because they or a peer just wrote it. Both receipts below were caught by CI and neither by review, which is what that asymmetry predicts. **A VOCABULARY DEFECT CARRIES IT BETWEEN LANES, AND THAT HALF IS WHAT MAKES THE CLASS PREVENTABLE RATHER THAN MERELY DETECTABLE.** One receipt arrived through a MESSAGE saying a class was `filed`. That word is true the moment a row is authored in a branch and is heard as `the tree carries it`; the two states collapse into one utterance. So the rule has a speech half: never say FILED without saying filed WHERE -- `authored in gunbc#NNNN, open` or `landed on main` -- because a reader cannot recover the distinction the word destroyed. TWO INDEPENDENT RECEIPTS, ONE HOUR APART, DIFFERENT LANES AND DIFFERENT CARRIERS, EACH CAUGHT BY CI. (i) A recurring-failure-mode row drew its load-bearing boundary against a sibling class that lived in the author's own other open PR. (ii) A proof field in a separate lane cited a class living in a third session's open PR, reached through the `filed` message above. Both authors repaired it the same way without knowing of each other: DESCRIBE THE SIBLING BY SHAPE RATHER THAN NAMING IT. THE RULE, and it is stronger than it first sounds: A CANONICAL ROW MAY CITE ONLY WHAT RESOLVES ON MAIN AT THE MOMENT THE ROW LANDS. Not `resolves eventually`. **That formulation FORBIDS STACKING the citing PR behind the cited one**, which is the tempting repair precisely because it feels like it fixes the citation -- it satisfies resolves-eventually and fails resolves-at-landing, so it defers the defect rather than removing it. THREE ADMISSIBLE FORMS, AND THE RANKING BETWEEN THE FIRST TWO IS CONDITIONAL ON WHETHER THE CITED IDENTITY IS STABLE -- an unconditional ranking was proposed, and withdrawn by its own author on the argument below. WHERE THE CITED IDENTITY IS STABLE, name the PR AND ITS OPENNESS -- `authored as <identity> in gunbc#NNNN, which is open at this writing, so this points at the PR carrying the row rather than asserting an identity that does not yet resolve`. It stays TRUE after the cited PR lands and TIGHTENS to the bare identity rather than needing correction. **WHERE THE CITED IDENTITY IS NOT STABLE, BOUNDARY BY DESCRIPTION RANKS FIRST INSTEAD, AND AN IDENTITY IN AN OPEN PR UNDER ACTIVE REVIEW IS PRECISELY THE UNSTABLE CASE.** If the cited PR RENAMES its row before landing -- under review pressure, or because two lanes converge and merge their classes -- the PR-naming form points at a real PR carrying a row that no longer has that name, AND IT FAILS WHILE STILL LOOKING RESOLVABLE: the PR number resolves, the identity does not, and the sentence reads as correct. A description survives that, because it does not name the thing that changed. So: PR-plus-openness when the identity is settled, description when it is in motion. BOUNDARY BY DESCRIPTION -- name the sibling's shape and not its symbol -- is otherwise second: correct, but it must be REWRITTEN once the sibling lands, and a rewrite is where a citation quietly stops matching the row it describes. Never: a bare identity that does not resolve on main today, which is worse than no citation at all because a reader takes the name as established and stops checking. RUNG, CEILING AND TRIGGER, per DESIGN section 4b. RUNG FOUND AT: MITIGATABLE. The repository already runs a required cited-symbol resolution check -- its rung drop `cited_symbol_census` is RETIRED, so the capability is live -- and it did not fire on either receipt, because BOTH CITATIONS WERE PROSE INSIDE AN `authored: String`, not typed references. A prose name is not reachable from the namespace tree the check walks, so the check was not weak here; it was not applicable. What caught both was a review bot reading the text, which is containment after the fact and not prevention. ATTAINABLE CEILING, AND IT IS NOT STRUCTURAL WHILE THE CITATION STAYS PROSE: deciding whether an identity-shaped token inside a paragraph is a CITATION or merely a mention is not decidable, so a scanner over prose would be a heuristic, and DESIGN section 5 forbids dressing one as a wall. This class therefore sits in the *outside the modeled guarantee* column for as long as row-to-row citation is prose -- observed and repaired by reading, never gated -- which is the same standing `unbacked_execution_claim` records for the same reason. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT: A TYPED ROW-TO-ROW CITATION CARRIER -- the ability to express `this row's boundary is drawn against THAT row` as a reference the namespace authority resolves, rather than as a name inside a paragraph. The moment such a citation is typed, the EXISTING required check covers it and the class climbs to structurally guaranteed for every typed citation in one step, with no new gate to build. `RecurringFailureMode` carries an `evidence: List<DeclarationRef>` field, which is the nearest existing carrier and is NOT that capability: it records declarations that witness the class, not the class's boundary against a sibling, and pressing it into service would be a second meaning for one field. WHY THIS ROW'S OWN `evidence` IS EMPTY, stated rather than left to look like an omission: both receipts are PULL REQUESTS AND REVIEW ARTIFACTS, not declarations, so there is no `DeclarationRef` to carry them and the field is honestly empty rather than padded. THE RECEIPTS AT CHECKABLE GRAIN: (i) gunbc#9946, review 58237 -- the boundary clause of `selection_view_read_as_population` named `censored_estimator_drops_its_own_tail`, which at that moment lived only in the same author's other open PR, gunbc#9932. BOTH IDENTITIES RESOLVE IN THIS TREE NOW, which is why they are named here rather than described: the receipt is that they did NOT resolve when the citation was written, and the repair the citing row carries is the descriptive-then-tightened form this row ranks second; (ii) gunbc#9949, review 58260 -- a proof field naming a class living in a third session's open PR, gunbc#9939, reached through the `filed` message. Both reviews are codex, both on the first pushed head of their PR, and each names the unresolvable identity explicitly. **THE TWO RECEIPTS ARE CARRIED IN TWO DIFFERENT ADMISSIBLE FORMS, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE: the first names identities because its two subjects have since landed, the second names a PR and its openness because gunbc#9939 has not. A reader who sees the ranking stated learns the conclusion; a reader who sees one paragraph use both forms because its two cited PRs are in different states learns the DISCRIMINATOR.** A COROLLARY THAT THIS ROW ITSELF DEMONSTRATES, and it is the reason the first receipt does not read as two bare names: WHEN A CITATION TIGHTENS FROM DESCRIPTION TO IDENTITY, THE RECEIPT USUALLY LIVES IN THE STATE THAT JUST ENDED, so tightening SILENTLY DESTROYS IT. This row's first receipt is the historical NON-RESOLUTION of those two names, not the names; tightened to identities alone it would show a reader two symbols that resolve and no evidence the class ever occurred -- a row about unresolvable citations, evidenced by resolvable ones. So a tightening must carry the ended state as a stated fact beside the new name, never merely replace it. THE CAUSE IS A SEPARATE SHAPE AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT FOLDED IN HERE: a correct decomposition -- splitting two classes into two PRs because a rider in a large PR gets skimmed rather than read -- is often what SEVERS the citation path between the pieces. That is a cause held at one receipt and not yet filed; this row is about why the severance is invisible from the citing end, which is a different question with a different repair. If both are ever filed, the causal link is named rather than merged.)", evidence: [] }

data refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "refusal deferred to the emitted runtime (a compiler refusal expressed as a construct IN THE EMITTED PROGRAM rather than as a diagnostic in the COMPILING one, so the compile reports success and the line does not stop). INVALID STATE: an emission path that cannot answer a declared fact writes a panic, an error expression or a stub into the artifact and returns normally, so the compiler emits N files and reports zero diagnostics beside a body that cannot run. HARM: fabricated plausible output at the strongest grain -- an artifact that looks like a compiled program and is not one. The refusal message may be perfectly honest and still fail DESIGN section 5, because nobody reads it until production; the reviewer's three questions are does the line stop, is the stop typed and located, does analysis precede restart, and this arm fails the first. DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the tell is a SUCCESS REPORT beside a refusal construct in the same run -- 'compiled: 7 files emitted, 0 diagnostics' printed by a compile whose emitted body was a panic naming its own refusal. It is NOT the same as a legitimate runtime arm at an honest boundary: the discriminator is whether the compiler KNEW at emit time, from modeled structure, that the artifact could not answer. If it knew and wrote the knowledge into the output instead of the diagnostic stream, the class applies. SPECIMEN AND HOW IT WAS FOUND: gunbc#9886's shell service-emission climb refused an unrealizable output channel by emitting panic!() from emit_shell_channel_expr while emit_artifact returned its files normally. Found by a DIFFERENTIAL READ against an independent implementation of the same repair (calm-boar-314's superseded WIP), then by execution on a probe; five consecutive reviews APPROVED the arm, two of them praising the refusal by name, so review did not catch it and is not the mechanism that will. WHY REVIEW MISSES IT: the refusal is present, typed, located and honestly worded at the point a reader's eye lands, and the missing half is an ABSENCE elsewhere -- no diagnostic in a stream the diff does not show. RECOGNITION RULE: for every arm that emits a refusal construct into a target artifact, ask what the COMPILE reports on the same input. If the answer is success, or any file count above zero, the arm belongs to this class. REPAIR, and it is usually already written next door: pair the refusal expression with a blocking emit-stage diagnostic so the artifact producer returns no files. In the specimen the FILE transport already had that pair and shell had the expression half only, so the repair was building the twin rather than inventing a path -- which is the general shape, since a codebase that emits refusals at all usually has one arm that does it correctly. KEEP THE EXPRESSION as the unreachable second half rather than deleting it, so the two readers cannot disagree if the wall is ever weakened. RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable -- a runtime panic in generated code, established by executing the emitter and reading its own success line, NOT by reading the type. CEILING: structurally guaranteed, and reached in the specimen -- a located compile-time refusal per declared field, derived from modeled structure, with zero files emitted. NEXT TRIGGER for the class as a whole: an emission-stage census that pairs every refusal-construct emitter with its diagnostic twin, since nothing today makes the missing half visible and the specimen was found by accident. POPULATION NOTE THE SPECIMEN CARRIES: the wall converted a SILENT corpus defect into a loud one -- gunbc.WitnessBin.Run declares stderr_truncated, stderr_total_bytes and stderr_retained_bytes, three channels the Rust realization cannot answer because the emitted Command body implements no capture policy, so every entry closure reaching that operation now refuses at field grain. That was always true and the old arm said nothing. Measured OUTSIDE REQUIRED COVERAGE, which is the honest phrasing and not 'affects nothing': claim_executor --required-emit-compile is green on all 8 rostered entries, each with its own mutation-established red, those 8 reaching 47 modules, with ZERO shell-channel diagnostics.)",
  evidence: [],
}

data ambient_process_state_read_by_a_concurrent_reader: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "ambient_process_state_read_by_a_concurrent_reader" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**ambient process state read by a concurrent reader** (a fact that is really a PARAMETER is instead read from a mutable cell the whole process shares -- the working directory, an env var, a global -- while the runtime schedules concurrent readers of it, so the answer a reader gets depends on which writer last ran and the wrong answer is SILENT: the read succeeds, returns a well-formed value, and is simply about a different subject than the reader meant. INVALID STATE: any reader resolving a relative name against ambient state that a concurrent writer may move mid-read. WHY IT SURVIVES REVIEW: each site is locally correct -- it sets the state to the right value before its own work and restores it after -- and the defect exists only in the PRODUCT of sites, which no single diff shows. SPECIMEN (PR #10024, v1_compiler.cli_run): 38 forward set_current_dir sites in one test binary that cargo runs multi-threaded, with the idiom prior = current_dir(); chdir(ws); work; chdir(prior) -- so one test's RESTORE hands the cwd back while a sibling is mid-read. The victim population is not the writers, it is every non-ignored test in the binary that resolves a relative path during the window; the file's own entry_admission_tests note already records the measurement, a DIFFERENT pair of tests failing on each run of identical code (4/1 then 3/2). Seven of the sites were reachable from the required unit lane and in all seven the chdir was DEAD -- every consumer already took an explicit root -- i.e. residue from an unfinished parameterisation, which is the expected shape once the migration is half done. THE CENSUS THAT MATTERS IS REACHABILITY, NOT THE LITERAL AND THE RANGE THAT MATTERS IS THE POPULATION'S, NOT THE FILE'S: the first cut of that gate scanned the one file its author was editing while declaring the whole lane as its subject, which is a selection view read as a population and puts the reported rung above the executed evidence (DESIGN section 4b(1) reads a class's rung as the MINIMUM across in-scope paths). Widening it to every source file of the lane's crate cost a change of input plus a linear-time call extractor -- the per-name matcher is quadratic in lines times declarations and does not survive the wider corpus -- and it surfaced a second trap immediately: resolving cross-file call edges by BARE NAME merges every declaration of a shared spelling, and this crate declares main 18 times, so one production seed bridged into hundreds of unrelated tests. That arm is the absorbing fallback again, in the guard built to catch it. What survives is intra-file edges plus cross-file edges only for names declared exactly once, with the ambiguous remainder pinned by IDENTITY rather than assumed empty. Six forms of the same defect were found in this one guard; they are rostered as their own class at check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim, which this row is a specimen of rather than an authority for: all seven reached the mutation through a helper, so a body-local grep for the call is green over every instance of the class and stays green the moment a writer is moved one call deeper -- the guard must close transitively over call edges. A SECOND, DISTINCT ARM, kept apart because it has a different remedy: memoizing a value DERIVED from the ambient state (workspace_root's OnceLock over a .git-ancestor walk from cwd) freezes whichever writer won the race for the whole process. On this specimen that arm's population is EMPTY -- every forward site targets the checkout root and 37 of 38 force the memo from the pristine cwd one line above their own call -- so it is reported UNSUPPORTED rather than disproven (see a_structural_possibility_is_not_an_occurring_phenomenon); ONE chdir to a non-checkout path arms it, and a fixture that runs git init is such a path. RUNG: found BELOW the ladder, since a redirected read is a silently wrong answer with no typed refusal anywhere. CEILING 4, structurally impossible, and decidable: state passed as a parameter has no shared cell to race on, so the invalid state has no constructor. The intermediate rung is a reachability gate over the guarded population (no_gating_test_reaches_a_process_cwd_mutator), which keeps the state ABSENT but not unwritable; its next-rung trigger is the capability that every reader in the population resolves from an explicitly passed root, after which the ambient write has no consumer and the call can be removed rather than merely counted. REVIEW TELL: a diff that sets shared process state and restores it, in code the runtime may run concurrently -- the restore is the tell, because it is what makes the site look self-contained.",
  evidence: [],
}

data predicate_vacuously_true_on_an_empty_domain: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "predicate_vacuously_true_on_an_empty_domain" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a predicate vacuously true on an empty domain** (a universally-quantified check -- `all`, `every`, `iter().all(..)`, a for-loop that only ever narrows a flag, a SQL NOT EXISTS -- is satisfied by the IDENTITY ELEMENT when its domain is empty, so the check answers TRUE about a population it never examined. INVALID STATE: a guard whose verdict is read as evidence while its domain is empty, with nothing establishing that the domain was non-empty. WHY IT SURVIVES REVIEW, and this is what separates it from an ordinary off-by-one: the code READS as a check, it EXECUTES, it is REACHED, and on every input a reviewer imagines the domain is non-empty and the predicate genuinely discriminates. The vacuous case is not a value in the data -- IT IS PRODUCED BY A BOUNDARY, so it appears only at the end of a line, the end of a buffer, a remainder shorter than the window, an empty selection, the last chunk. Those are exactly the inputs a hand-written fixture omits, and exactly the inputs a real corpus eventually contains. SPECIMEN (PR #10033, measured): a raw-string scanner tested its closing delimiter with `chars[i+1..].iter().take(hashes).all(|h| *h == '#')`. Over a remainder shorter than `hashes` that iterator yields fewer items and `all` is vacuously TRUE, so a quote near end-of-line closes a hash-delimited raw string that is still open, and the rest of the fixture is handed back to the code scanner -- reintroducing the very brace-depth skew the raw-string handling existed to prevent, silently and in the UNDER-approximating direction. The repair is a length bound, not a different predicate: `i + 1 + hashes <= len` conjoined with the same `all`, which leaves the zero-hash case (a raw string with no hashes) trivially satisfied as it must be. RECOGNITION RULE, and it generalises past scanners: A PREDICATE THAT IS TRUE ON THE EMPTY CASE IS NOT A CHECK UNTIL ITS DOMAIN IS PROVEN NON-EMPTY. Ask of every universal: what does this return when the collection is empty, and can the boundary produce empty? If the answer is TRUE and YES, the domain bound is part of the predicate and its absence is the defect. BOUNDED AGAINST THREE NEIGHBOURS, none of whose recognition rules find it. `executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing` is about a CORPUS that never constructs the falsifying population, so its remedy is a fixture; here the falsifying population is unconstructable at the boundary by the shape of the quantifier itself, and the remedy is a bound on the domain. `empty_observation_narrow` is an OBSERVATION that could not express what changed being rendered as a verdict -- one layer up, about evidence rather than about a predicate's truth value. `incidental_denominator_as_wall` is a guard that holds by a coincidence upstream that genuinely holds; here nothing holds at all, the guard simply returns TRUE. RUNG: found OUTSIDE the ladder, because the wrong answer is silent and well-formed -- the check reports satisfaction. CEILING 4 and decidable per-site: a windowed comparison whose window length is carried in its type cannot be asked about a short remainder. The intermediate rung is an executed control that exercises the BOUNDARY case specifically, asserted on a synthetic input rather than on the live corpus, so it keeps discriminating power when the corpus changes.",
  evidence: [],
}

data check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "**a check's subject is narrower than the claim it is cited for** (EVERY DEGREE OF FREEDOM IN A CHECK'S SUBJECT -- which call sites, which spellings, which lexical states, which domain, which files -- is a place its coverage can silently be narrower than the population it is read as covering. INVALID STATE: an executing, reached, green check whose declared subject is a strict superset of the population its implementation actually ranges over. RUNG: outside the ladder, because the gap is invisible from the check's own result -- a wall whose range is too narrow is green for the same reason a wall over a clean corpus is green, and DESIGN section 4b(1) reads a class's rung as the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths, so a check like this INFLATES the rung of everything it is cited for. THE ROUTE IS WHAT MAKES IT INVISIBLE: the narrowing is never a decision, it is the shape of the first implementation -- an author edits one file, so the scanner reads one file; the corpus spells the call one way, so the seed matches one spelling; the fixture has no raw strings, so the projection has no raw-string state; the window is never short, so the universal is never vacuous. Each is locally reasonable and none is written down, which is why the gap survives the review that reads the check's LOGIC and never asks what its INPUT was. SPECIMEN, and the reason this is a class rather than a bug: ONE guard in PR #10033 carried SIX instances -- (1) a body-local grep for the mutator, defeated by moving the call one helper deeper; (2) a seed matching only the fully-qualified path, defeated by `use std::env;`; (3) a lexical projection with no raw-string state, so an unbalanced brace in a fixture silently shifted every containment decision after it; (4) `take(n).all(..)`, vacuously true over a short remainder (rostered as predicate_vacuously_true_on_an_empty_domain); (5) a scan ranging over ONE FILE while the scope declaration claimed every test the required lane runs -- found by review, not by the author; and (6) after widening, cross-file call edges resolved by BARE NAME, which merges every declaration of a shared spelling (18 `main`s in that crate) and bridged one production seed into hundreds of unrelated tests. Four were found by the author, one by review, one by the widening itself, and the sixth is the mirror of the fifth: over-broad and under-broad are the same defect measured in opposite directions, and both are reported as coverage. RECOGNITION RULE: name the check's SUBJECT and the check's RANGE as two separate sentences, then ask what is in the first and not the second. If the answer is anything, the claim is the narrower one until the range is widened. The review-side tell is a scope comment that quantifies (`every test`, `all modules`, `any call site`) beside an implementation that names ONE input. BOUNDED AGAINST TWO NEIGHBOURS. selection_view_read_as_population is a set produced by a MEASUREMENT threshold and read as the population, arriving as the fix for a real objection; here nothing is measured and nothing is filtered -- the range was simply never as wide as the sentence beside it. incidental_denominator_as_wall is a guard that holds by an upstream coincidence that genuinely holds; here the guard holds over a population it never read. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed, and decidable: a check whose subject is a VALUE it receives rather than a scope its implementation re-derives cannot range over less than it claims, because the claim and the range are then one object. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: the guarded population is passed to the check as a constructed value carrying its own extent, sufficient that no check can name a subject its input does not contain. WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: that widening always wins. Narrowing the DECLARATION to match the range is equally honest and is sometimes correct -- what is forbidden is leaving the two different, and the choice between them is a cost measurement, not a preference. On this specimen widening cost one change of input plus one linear-time rewrite of a quadratic edge builder, and the wider check ran FASTER than the narrow one, which is what settled it.) A SEVENTH FORM, AND THE FIRST WHERE THE NARROWING IS AN AXIS OF THE COMPARISON RATHER THAN A RANGE OF INPUTS (2026-09-03). The six above narrow WHICH INPUTS a check sees; this one narrows WHAT IT COMPARES, so it is invisible even over a complete corpus. `v1_compiler.behavioral_receipt_host` `behavioral_differential` is cited as the executing evidence for DESIGN section 7 behavioural equivalence, and its own doc comment cites section 7 by name. What it RANGES OVER is the seed-Rust versus emitted-Rust axis: `generate_receipt_driver` emits a Rust main that prints each planned call, and the differential runs that ONE driver twice -- against the tree as committed, then after the candidate overwrites its mirror and the crate is rebuilt. Both transcripts come from COMPILED RUST BINARIES, so any property the two realizations SHARE is unobservable to it by construction, however clean the corpus. THE DISCRIMINATING INSTANCE IS NOT THIS ROW'S TO STATE, AND CITING IT RATHER THAN RESTATING IT IS THE POINT (amended 2026-09-03). The interpreter-versus-emitted evaluation divergence has an owner with better evidence than prose: `realization_arms_diverge_on_whether_the_program_refuses`, filed by gunbc#10139, which carries the source reading in both directions AND an EXECUTED red -- `fn guarded_division(n: Int) -> Bool { n != 0 && (100 / n) > 1 }`, run and dated, explicitly not asserted. An earlier draft of this receipt described that divergence in its own words. That would have been a second authority for a fact this ledger already owns, committed inside the row about subjects narrower than their claims, which is the specimen writing itself. WHAT IS THIS ROW'S OWN SUBJECT is the other half and a different fact: THE INSTRUMENT CANNOT SEE IT. Both of `behavioral_differential`'s arms are compiled Rust, so they share the target's evaluation semantics and agree with each other -- wrongly, together -- on exactly the inputs where that cited class occurs. The divergence is #10139's; the blindness of the equivalence instrument to it is this row's. THE REVIEW TELL FOR THIS FORM: ask what the two sides of a comparison SHARE, not what the check ranges over -- a differential between two realizations of one target cannot see a property of that target. The ordinary tell, a green over a population nobody checked, is unavailable here: this instrument is green for a reason no input can change. ONE NEIGHBOUR CHECKED AND EXCLUDED, so the next reader does not re-derive it: `v2.compiler.emit_host` `run_test_claim_emit_vs_eval` IS enrolled on the required floor and DOES pair an executed emitted answer with an interpreted one, with a positive control and a discriminating negative. But it evaluates `expected_eval_root` while host-running the emitted `claim_input_root` -- two different roots -- so it is an ORACLE comparison and the interpreter never evaluates the expression the target runs. Its subject excludes same-expression evaluation divergence structurally, not by coverage. THE AUTHOR'S OWN INSTANCE, recorded because it happened while filing this: the first draft claimed NO required phase pairs an interpreted answer with an emitted-and-executed one, derived by enumerating the closed five-variant `RequiredCiPhase` and then asserting what its members execute without reading them. The population was closed; the claim about its members was never checked -- a real enumeration, divided by nothing. It was refuted by the very rows that refused the pull request being worked on.",
  evidence: [],
}
data recurrence_ledger_scoped_below_the_recurrence: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "recurrence_ledger_scoped_below_the_recurrence" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a recurrence ledger scoped below the recurrence it must find** (an instrument counts repetition WITHIN a unit of work and is reset at that unit's boundary, while the repetition that matters happens ACROSS those units. Every unit then reports the same honest answer -- ONE -- and the aggregate nobody computes is the only place the duplication exists. The instrument is not wrong at its own grain and never reads as broken: it runs, it is enabled, it prints, and its output is empty of the thing being looked for, which is indistinguishable from that thing being absent. **The recognition rule is a question about RANGE, not about correctness: name the scope over which the redundancy you are hunting is defined, and check that the ledger's lifetime is at least that scope.** If the ledger is cleared more often than the redundancy recurs, its silence is a property of its reset schedule. **THE KINSHIP THAT MAKES IT LEGIBLE, and it is `censored_estimator_drops_its_own_tail` in a different medium: a cost paid once per unit and attributed to one arbitrary consumer never reaches count>=2 inside that unit, so the ledger that ranks REPETITION cannot observe the population it exists to rank.** The estimator is censored not by a threshold but by a scope. **THE FIELD TELL, and it is the one that identifies this class from the outside before anyone reads the instrument: the repair mechanism ALREADY EXISTS and its coverage is hand-authored, because candidates are discovered when the unrepaired cost causes a failure somewhere unrelated.** A roster that grows one row at a time, each row traceable to an incident on somebody else's change, is a roster whose discovery instrument is blind -- the incidents are doing the ranking, and their cost is paid by whoever was passing. Distinct from `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content`, where a report is complete for the reporter and read past its promise -- here the report IS complete for its declared scope and the CONSUMER'S QUESTION LIVES AT A WIDER ONE -- and distinct from `selection_view_read_as_population`, where a threshold over measured values is mistaken for the class: no selection happens here at all, the population is simply unrepresentable in the ledger's key space. SPECIMEN, WITH THE FULL CAUSAL CHAIN MEASURED (2026-09-02, gunbc#10036 lane). The required floor charges each claim a per-claim CPU ceiling and builds a FRESH EVALUATION FRAME PER CLAIM -- deliberately, so one witness cannot contaminate the next -- so every claim re-derives the pure substrate its import closure reaches. `v1_compiler.v1_interpreter`'s recompute-trace ledger ranks pure calls with count>=2 within ONE `InterpContext`, and `claim_executor` prints and drops it at every claim frame exit; a producer evaluated EXACTLY ONCE per claim, in 3477 claims, has count=1 in every ledger and appears in none. The repair mechanism already existed -- `v2.workflow.floor_pure_producer_share` serves one evaluation of a declared pure producer across frames -- and its roster was six hand-authored rows, because nothing produced its candidates. **SO THE DISCOVERY MECHANISM WAS THE COST: roster coverage was found when a per-claim budget refusal landed on an unrelated lane's pull request, four lanes in one day, every one of those runs reporting failed=0.** THE DISCRIMINATOR THAT PROVED THE CHARGE WAS NOT THE CLAIM'S OWN WORK, and it is reusable: a witness and its DISCRIMINATING RED do materially different work, so when they cost the same to within 2ms while both sit near the ceiling, the cost is not the assertion's -- 296/294, 333/331 and 384/382 on main run 33615659836's `required_floor_claim_cost.tsv`, against a corpus p50 of 2ms; one 34-row module spans 0ms to the ceiling in three bands that track WHICH SHARED PRODUCER a row forces rather than what it asserts. **WHAT THE SPECIMEN REFUTES IS BOTH OF THE OBVIOUS REMEDIES, AND THAT IS WHY THE CLASS IS FILED RATHER THAN THE INSTANCE FIXED.** Raising the ceiling moves a line that the corpus distribution says is correctly placed, to accommodate a charge that is wrong, and it destroys the only signal that anything is slow; quarantining the family converts a cost problem into a coverage problem silently. Both are the absorbing arm DESIGN section 5 forbids, and the second cannot even be reached, because the family is not anomalous -- its own work is among the smallest in the corpus. REPAIR: fold each unit's ledger into a run-scoped census keyed on the DECLARATION identity plus the argument row, so cross-unit demand becomes a run product; the receipt is `v1_compiler.v1_interpreter` `absorb_claim_recompute_demand` and the artifact `gunbc.witness_floor_workflow` `required_floor_cross_claim_demand_path`, whose own discriminating red asserts the per-frame ledger's blindness beside the census's answer so re-scoping it back reds. A SECOND, INDEPENDENT CONSEQUENCE, AND IT RETIRES PART OF A DECLARED DROP RATHER THAN THE DROP: `gunbc.rung_drop` `floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable` names a missing carrier -- the per-claim cost artifact modeled as data a function can read -- and states that its attention subset is a HAND derivation rather than a run product. That is buildable, so what a cross-unit census plus that modeled fold retires is BLIND CANDIDATE DISCOVERY, INCIDENT-AS-DISCOVERY, AND THE MISSING CARRIER. **WHAT IT DOES NOT RETIRE, AND SAYING OTHERWISE WOULD BE THE RUNG INFLATION THIS LEDGER EXISTS TO CATCH: environment-independent claim-cost qualification.** Naming every shared producer does not make a claim's remaining evaluator work invariant across execution envelopes -- host scheduling, contention and cache state still move it -- so the per-claim line stays an ATTEMPT-SAFETY boundary and that drop keeps standing on its own subject. **THE SAME DISCIPLINE APPLIES TO WHAT THE CENSUS ITSELF EXPLAINS.** A per-unit constant is BY CONSTRUCTION identical on two runs of one tree, so it accounts for the LEVEL and not the VARIANCE; a run-to-run delta is separately measured (byte-identical evaluator steps against 1.31-1.80x cpu over a byte-identical payload). The two COMPOSE into the observed shape -- the constant puts a family AT the line and something run-to-run decides which of its rows cross -- and that composition is why the victim WANDERS rather than repeating -- the prediction this account makes and the rival 'fixed set of expensive rows' account does not. **TWO RECEIPTS, NEITHER A CROSS-RUN COMPARISON.** (i) ZERO MARGIN: two rows of one module measured 502ms and EXACTLY 500ms against the 500ms budget. (ii) ONE ROW OBSERVED CROSSING THE TWO POPULATIONS ON ONE TREE -- run 33620893203 attempt 1 records `an_empty_receipt_series_leaves_the_live_tree_unmeasured_rather_than_held` as INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT with `cost=UNMEASURED`, and ATTEMPT 2 OF THE SAME RUN records it as COMPLETED-OVER-COST-REQUIREMENT at cpu_ms=500, reaching its verdict. **THAT PAIR IS A BOUND BESIDE A VALUE, NOT TWO MEASUREMENTS OF ONE QUANTITY, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE WHOLE POINT:** the interrupted arm knows only that the cost exceeded the ceiling by an unknown amount, and its reported figure names where the POLL observed the ceiling -- a property of the budget, which its own diagnostic spends three clauses saying. Writing the pair as two costs would say the row got a couple of milliseconds cheaper and crossed a line, which is a story about the row; what actually changed between the attempts is WHAT THE OBSERVER COULD SAY. Those are the two populations the budget cut separated BECAUSE THEY ARE DIFFERENT FACTS WITH DIFFERENT REMEDIES, and at this margin which one a row lands in is decided by whether the poll fired before or after the work finished: a fact about the poll, not about the row. **THE CITATION DISCIPLINE THAT MADE THAT RECOVERABLE IS PART OF THE CLASS, because the evidence was retracted and then restored on it: CITE THE ATTEMPT, NOT THE RUN OR THE JOB.** A bare run id and a bare job id both resolve to the LATEST attempt, so a rerun silently changes what a stable citation serves -- no error, and nothing visible from the citing end, which is why the first retraction looked sound. `/actions/runs/<id>/attempts/<n>/logs` serves the attempt that was actually read; a figure cited without an attempt should carry `run_attempt` beside it so a reader can tell whether the citation still points at what its author saw. **AND THE STANDING RECOMMENDATION IS UNCHANGED BY EITHER DIRECTION OF THAT CORRECTION: A REMEDY MUST NEVER BE KEYED TO WHICH ROWS TIPPED.** A producer census survived the retraction and the restoration without a word changing in what it reports; a ranking of tipped rows would have been rebuilt twice. Two independent arguments for one conclusion: dispersion shows the charge is not the ASSERTION's, wandering shows it is not the ROW's.)", evidence: [] }
data stable_citation_mutable_referent: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "stable_citation_mutable_referent" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**stable citation, mutable referent** (an identifier that names a thing correctly and forever, while the CONTENT served for it is replaced underneath. Distinct from `positional_citation`, and the difference is what makes it worse: a `file:line` pointer goes stale under an edit above it, and re-reading the file EXPOSES that — the symbol is not there, or a different one is. Here re-reading the citation CONFIRMS the wrong answer, because the identifier still resolves, still returns content of the expected shape, and reports no error. There is no red anywhere. Receipt (2026-09-02, gunbc#10042): a GitHub Actions JOB ID was cited as the source of a floor measurement. A job id names the job; the logs API serves the LATEST ATTEMPT. A rerun replaces the attempt, so job 100217416636 served six budget-refused identities when first read and thirteen when read back, and the second reading was byte-identical to a DIFFERENT job id — two ids, one attempt. A cross-run comparison built on those readings appeared to compare two runs while one side had been replaced underneath, and the damage ran in BOTH directions: a near-disjointness claim that was simply false, and a real bucket migration that was retracted as unfounded because it could no longer be reproduced through the citation that found it. The second is the more expensive error — a true finding withdrawn, downstream prose rewritten in four places to remove it, and a merge rule changed — and it is the one a reader would not think to look for, because a retraction feels like the conservative move. THE DEFAULT CITATION IS THE TRAP AND THE PINNED ONE IS THE REMEDY, and both were measured rather than assumed: `gh run view --job <id> --log` serves the latest attempt, but the attempt-pinned REST path — `/repos/OWNER/REPO/actions/runs/RUNID/attempts/N/logs` still serves attempt 1 in full. Recovering it confirmed the original six-row reading exactly, and confirmed that `an_empty_receipt_series_leaves_the_live_tree_unmeasured_rather_than_held` is INTERRUPTED in attempt 1 and COMPLETED-OVER-COST in attempt 2 — a real migration across the two populations, not the artifact it was briefly retracted as. So the class is not that the earlier subject is destroyed; it is that the ORDINARY way of citing it silently resolves to a different one, and a reader who re-reads the same citation to check gets agreement instead of a contradiction. **Recognition rule: before comparing two readings of one producer, ask whether the producer serves a STABLE SUBJECT for a fixed citation — not whether the citation is well-formed. An identifier that addresses a CONTAINER (a job, a branch, a latest, a mutable tag, a rolling window) serves whatever currently occupies it, so two readings of one citation are two subjects and their DELTA is uninterpretable. Cite the thing that cannot be replaced — the attempt, the commit, the immutable artifact — or capture the content at read time and say when.** The receipt worth keeping is that this survived the diligence that should have caught it: the same author had, that morning, REFUSED to file a transcribed measurement on the §6 grounds that no producer owned the number, and then built a delta out of a producer that mutates what it serves for a fixed id. Naming the instrument is not sufficient if the instrument does not serve a stable subject. One diagnostic tell for the delta itself, preserved here from gunbc#10130 where it was measured against this same receipt: the two readings were differenced into a `3 -> 6 -> 13` upward trend with a memory-pressure mechanism attached, the `3` having additionally come from a different head — and monotone growth is precisely what independent draws at a fixed distance from a budget do NOT produce. The shape that made the artifact persuasive was the evidence against it, so the tell is available BEFORE the referent is re-checked: a delta through a container-addressing citation that arrives already fitting a story is the reading to distrust first.)", evidence: [] }

data hedged_benefit_leaves_the_harm_axis_unexamined: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "hedged_benefit_leaves_the_harm_axis_unexamined" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a carefully hedged BENEFIT claim leaves the HARM axis wholly unexamined** (INVALID STATE: an actor takes an irreversible or side-effecting action, states a calibrated caution about whether it HELPS, and never asks whether it HARMS. The two are different axes, and no amount of hedging on the first reaches the second. HARM: the hedge is what makes it dangerous rather than merely wrong -- it reads as due diligence, so a reviewer or manager sees the epistemic care and endorses, and the endorsement generalises a single act into practice. Section 5 silent wrongness with an amplifier: the honest-sounding sentence is the vector. **SPECIMEN, and the actor is the reporter** (sunny-gull-270, 2026-09-02). A superseded CI run on a two-commit-stale head was cancelled to return a fleet slot during saturation, reported with the explicit caution `the cancel does not make the current run start, and I have no evidence it helps rather than merely stops waste`. The manager verified the reasoning and endorsed it as `the only lever any of us actually has`, generalising it. Both were wrong, and the authority that settles it was one grep away: gunbc.witness_floor_workflow emits cancel-in-progress false with running NeverSupersedeRunning, because the fleet's builds are bounded by a host-persistent GNU jobserver whose permits are returned COOPERATIVELY -- a cancelled run SIGKILLs cargo mid-build, so every borrowed permit is lost for the daemon's lifetime and the pool decays monotonically toward zero. So the act did not merely fail to help; it is the mechanism that produces the exhaustion symptom it was taken to relieve, and the stale runs it reclaimed are that policy's DECLARED cost rather than waste. **RECOGNITION RULE, and it is mechanical: read the hedge and ask which axis it is on.** A caution of the form `I cannot show this helps`, `this may not be enough`, `no evidence it improves things` is a BENEFIT hedge. If the action has any side effect on shared state -- a cancel, a delete, a force-push, a config write, a retry against a non-idempotent endpoint -- the benefit hedge is not the relevant one and its presence is evidence the harm question was never asked. **THE TELL A REVIEWER CAN USE: an actor who has genuinely examined harm names the mechanism by which harm would occur, and then says why it does not apply here.** An actor who has only hedged benefit names no mechanism at all, because there is none to name. **RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable, and by nothing structural** -- the harm was caught after the fact by reading an authority nobody was required to read. **CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable, and not higher.** Whether an action's side effects are harmful is not decidable from the action alone; it depends on a governing policy that may live in any authority. What IS decidable is whether the policy governing a class of action was CONSULTED. **NEXT TRIGGER: a typed standing that binds each fleet-affecting operator action to the authority governing it, so taking the action without consulting that authority refuses rather than relying on the actor to grep.** Until that exists this is a review discipline and citing it as coverage is rung inflation.", evidence: [] }

data receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "receipt_names_a_property_not_the_tree_it_holds_of" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a receipt names a PROPERTY and never names the TREE it holds of, so it expires silently** (INVALID STATE: evidence of the form 'regenerating produces the committed bytes', 'the diff is zero', 'the census matches', 'the fixed point is reached' is a claim about A BASE, but is recorded and cited as a claim about A CHANGE. When the base moves the receipt keeps reading as valid while describing a tree that no longer exists. HARM: section 5 silent wrongness, and this is the WORST-SIGNALLING member of its family rather than merely another one -- a stale citation still shows the reader its text, an incompatible merge still conflicts, an absent observation still reports an absence; AN EXPIRED GREEN PRODUCES NOTHING AT ALL. Nothing goes red, no conflict is raised, and the author's own careful re-verification re-affirms it, because re-running the same command against the same stale working tree reproduces the same true-of-nothing answer. **DISTINCT FROM ITS TWO NEAREST NEIGHBOURS, and the repair law is what separates them.** `execution_provenance_loss` asks whether the observation RAN; here it ran and was valid, and then STOPPED being valid because its subject moved underneath it. `positional_citation` is a decaying HANDLE -- a pointer that no longer names what it named; here the handle is fine and it is the EVIDENCE BINDING that decayed. Different invalid states, different repairs. **SPECIMEN (sunny-gull-270, PR #10036, 2026-09-02).** The PR's entire acceptance test was that the emitted .github/workflows/witnesses.yml is byte-identical after regeneration -- a behaviour-identical refactor whose whole claim is that the bytes do not move. It was re-verified after each of three commits, and ALL THREE measurements were taken against a base main had already left: #10024 had landed and materially rewritten BOTH the authority the PR edits and the artifact under test -- re-derive the magnitudes with `git show --stat 7c310ed74c5 -- dag/gunbc/witness/witness_floor_workflow.dag .github/workflows/witnesses.yml`, which is an immutable commit and so answers the same forever. No signal at any point. The expiry was found by asking what had changed in main, not by any check. **RECOGNITION RULE, mechanical: before citing a zero-diff or byte-identity receipt as merge evidence, ask whether the base moved ON THE FILES THE RECEIPT IS ABOUT** -- `git diff --stat $(git merge-base HEAD origin/main) origin/main -- <those paths>` -- because a receipt about generated bytes is invalidated only by changes to the authorities that produce them, and a whole-repository is-my-branch-behind check is both too coarse to act on and too noisy to keep. **A SECOND, LESS OBVIOUS OBLIGATION: RE-DERIVE THE DISCRIMINATING CONTROL TOO, NOT ONLY THE RECEIPT.** A control taken before the merge proves the zero was readable on a tree that is not the one shipping, so a re-derived green beside a stale control is half a measurement. And rebuild the PRODUCER: the tree and the emitter are two inputs, and a regeneration with one of them stale proves nothing about the pair. **THE UPSIDE IS WORTH STATING BECAUSE IT CHANGES WHETHER PEOPLE DO IT: a receipt re-derived after a FOREIGN change to the same artifact is STRICTLY STRONGER than the original.** The first green only ever asks whether a projection reproduces its own base; the second asks whether it reproduces a base someone else moved -- which is where a projection that disagrees with the hand-kept form it replaced would actually surface. **RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable.** Today the only defence is an author remembering to re-derive before citing, which is exactly the defence that does not survive a tired hour. **CEILING: 2, mechanically preventable, and the reason it is not higher is that a receipt cannot make its subject stop moving -- what it can do is make the movement OBSERVABLE. NEXT TRIGGER, named as the capability and not as an artifact: a receipt CARRIES THE BASE IT WAS MEASURED ON, so a producer can compare that base against HEAD and refuse an expired receipt, rather than a person remembering to. THAT CAPABILITY IS NOT HYPOTHETICAL -- IT ALREADY EXISTS ONE SURFACE OVER, WHICH IS WHY THIS TRIGGER IS REACHABLE RATHER THAN ASPIRATIONAL: the review runner binds each review to the sha it was taken on and REFUSES on mismatch. On this row's own pull request, review 58587 failed with `worktree freshness check failed: HEAD is ad388184ac but PR #10036 head is c80c9d88db -- refusing to review a stale/wrong checkout`, and a refused review is exactly the signal an expired receipt does not produce. So reviews already carry their base and receipts do not; the gap is an UNAPPLIED mechanism rather than a missing one, and the trigger is discharged by giving regeneration receipts the binding reviews already have. **THIS CITATION CARRIES ITS OWN BASE, because a row about receipts that expire must not carry one that has.** What is DURABLE is review 58587 itself: it is retrievable from the reviews API with status=failed, sha c80c9d88db and that error text, and a completed review is a historical fact that does not decay. What is an OBSERVATION AT A TIME is the claim that the runner still behaves this way -- measured 2026-09-02, and NOT re-confirmed since, because the runner's source lives outside this repository and is not visible from a session container, so no gate here can check it and its absence from a local filesystem is not evidence either way. Sampling later pull requests for a freshness failure -- `dashboard-ops reviews <pr>`, reading each review's status and error -- found none, and that is EXPECTED RATHER THAN REASSURING: the check fires only when a head moves mid-checkout, so a sample drawn where the condition did not arise discriminates nothing and no count of it is worth carrying. **THAT UNCHECKABILITY IS ITSELF WHY THE TRIGGER NAMES A CAPABILITY AND NOT AN ARTIFACT** -- a trigger pointing at a file this repository cannot see would be satisfied or falsified by nothing observable here, which is the restoration-promise failure one row over. Until that exists this row is the mitigation and citing it as coverage is rung inflation.**", evidence: [] }

data proxy_observation_mistaken_for_action_semantics: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "proxy_observation_mistaken_for_action_semantics" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a destructive action is judged by a PROXY observation, never by the action's own semantics** (INVALID STATE: an actor destroys something -- deletes an edge, a file, a roster row, an authority -- and reads the verdict off an observation that stands in a PROXY relation to what the destruction MEANS. 'Strip the imports and see whether the compile exits 0' is the canonical shape. The proxy is only ever as strong as the checking path that produces it, and the semantic question -- does every occurrence that crossed the destroyed edge still bind to exactly one accepted declaration identity, and does that identity project a provider the closure reaches -- is never asked. **HARM: DESIGN section 5 silent wrongness, and directionally the worst member of its family, because the proxy and the semantics agree EXACTLY WHERE THE CHECKER IS SOUND AND DIVERGE EXACTLY WHERE IT FAILS OPEN.** The green is therefore densest on the population the destruction actually damages, and a count of green subjects reads as coverage while being a census of the checker's absorbing arm. **RECOGNITION RULE, and it is mechanical rather than a matter of judgement: name the acceptance path that produced the observation, and ask what that path does when the property under test is ABSENT -- refuse, or substitute.** If any arm on it fabricates, widens, defaults or falls back, the observation is a proxy and its green is a statement about that arm. **DISTINCT FROM ITS THREE NEIGHBOURS, and the repairs differ.** `absorbing_fallback` is the fail-open arm itself; here the arm may be long known, correctly filed and owned by somebody else -- the defect is the READING of a destruction's green taken across it. `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content` is a report complete for its own promise and read past it; here the observation is not incomplete at all, it answers a DIFFERENT QUESTION than the actor's. `executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing` cannot discriminate anywhere; a proxy discriminates perfectly on the sound half of its population, which is what makes it credible. **SPECIMEN, ALREADY MEASURED AND ON THE RECORD IN THIS REPOSITORY, which is why the class is filed rather than the instance re-investigated: the import strip, `docs/plans/import-strip-witness-discovery-cascade-diagnosis.md` section 15.4.** 1,773 of the 2,574 stripped files produced no diagnostic, and that 69% was available to be read as 'these files' references are independently resolvable'. Section 14 of the same document had ALREADY established by execution that a type present in the pool but not structurally bound is FABRICATED AS AN ANONYMOUS PRODUCT rather than refused, and that the production type-reference discriminator is measurement-only -- normal compile, resolve, run and emit stay on the legacy fail-open path unless measurement mode is armed. So the 69% is a joint statement about which providers happened to be in the pool and which failures the fabrication arm absorbed, and the document says so in its own words: a clean file may be clean because its provider happened to be loaded. **THE SUBSTITUTE, STATED SO THIS ROW NAMES A TEST AND NOT ONLY A DEFECT, and it is section 15.4's own terminal test: not 'delete imports, compile exits 0', but every cross-module occurrence has exactly one accepted declaration identity; every accepted identity projects its provider file; the loader closure equals that provider projection; adding or removing an unrelated loaded module changes neither binding nor closure; type, value, callee and emitter consumers all consume the accepted edge; no fallback or fabrication arm is reachable; and compile AND execution are green.** **THE STANDING OBLIGATION THIS CLASS CREATES, AND IT LANDS ON THIS PROJECT'S OWN CENSUS METHOD: THE DESTRUCTION-WITNESS PRECONDITION.** DESIGN section 3 grounds delete-first on 'the deletion is the census -- every real dependent refuses loudly'. That sentence is CONDITIONAL on the substrate being fail-closed ON THE AXIS DESTROYED, and it is the conditional, not the sentence, that a destruction witness must discharge: before a deletion's green may be read as 'nothing depended on it', exhibit BY EXECUTION, on the SAME acceptance path the green will be read from, one case where the destroyed edge is genuinely required and the path goes RED. Absent that red the green is a property of the path's failure arm rather than of the corpus, and no number of green subjects repairs it -- a vacuous check does not become discriminating by being run more times. The precondition is carried by `docs/plans/replacement-migration-doctrine.md`, filed beside the sibling already recorded there in which the census is empty because the referent is NAMED rather than imported: same conclusion by a different mechanism, and the pair is the point -- there nothing refuses because nothing was ever an edge, here the edge exists and the checker declines to judge it. **RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable.** The divergence was caught by a reader holding the observation up against the checker that produced it, after a wave had already been sized on the proxy. **CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed, and reachable rather than aspirational, because the disqualifying fact is decidable from the substrate:** whether the acceptance path a witness reads has a reachable fabrication or fallback arm on the axis under test is a property of that path's own graph, not of the world. **NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY AND NOT AS AN ARTIFACT: a destruction witness declares the axis it destroys and the acceptance path it reads, and the executor REFUSES the witness when that path carries a reachable fail-open arm on that axis** -- so the precondition is discharged by the runner rather than remembered by an author. Until that capability exists this row and the doctrine section are the mitigation, and citing either as coverage is the rung inflation DESIGN section 4b(1) names.", evidence: [] }

data realization_arms_diverge_on_whether_the_program_refuses: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "realization_arms_diverge_on_whether_the_program_refuses" as NonEmptyStr,
  authored: "realization arms diverge on WHETHER THE PROGRAM REFUSES (two realizations of one accepted program agree on the returned value and disagree on whether an evaluation-time refusal fires, because the fact that decides it -- evaluation order -- is modeled nowhere and each arm improvises). INVALID STATE: a connective whose operand evaluation strategy is unmodeled, realized strictly by one arm and lazily by another. gunbc v1 today: v1.compiler.interpreter eval_expr_inner's ExprBinOp arm evaluates BOTH operands through `?` before dispatching. eval_binop DOES carry And and Or arms -- `Value::Bool(left.is_truthy() && right.is_truthy())` -- and they are irrelevant to this class and worth naming precisely because they look like the repair: they run on operands ALREADY EVALUATED at the call site, so their Rust && is over two bools and short-circuits nothing. A reader grepping eval_binop for And finds a hit and concludes the case is handled, while std.operator_realization maps BinOp::And and BinOp::Or to OperatorRealization::HostOperator, rendered as Rust && and ||, which short-circuit. HARM: the guard idiom -- a cheap precondition guarding an expression that can refuse -- means two different programs. The interpreter runs the guarded expression when the guard is FALSE and refuses; emitted Rust never runs it and returns a value. Silent in both directions and invisible to any oracle comparing returned values on guard-true inputs, which is every value-comparison oracle we have. DISCRIMINATING RED, executed 2026-09-02, not asserted: `fn guarded_division(n: Int) -> Bool { n != 0 && (100 / n) > 1 }`. At n=0 the interpreter refuses DivisionByZero and the emitted Rust returns false; at n=5 both return true. Division by zero was chosen deliberately because BOTH realizations abort identically IF the expression is evaluated, so evaluation order is the only variable in the pair. CONTROLS, because a false from a harness that cannot observe an abort is a vacuous green: the same function with the guard forced true and n=0 PANICKED with 'attempt to divide by zero' and was caught and reported, so the harness can see the abort; and the guard-true positive control agrees across both arms. HONESTY BOUND ON THE EVIDENCE: the interpreter arm ran on the real acceptance path via `gunbc run`; the emitted arm executed the emitted function bodies extracted VERBATIM into a rustc harness, not the whole emitted crate. WHY IT IS NOT refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime: that class is a compiler writing a refusal construct INTO the artifact while reporting success. Here no refusal is written anywhere and the compile is honest; the two arms simply disagree at run time about whether one fires. Same neighbourhood, different invalid state, different repair. THE POPULATION IS SURVIVORSHIP-FILTERED AND A GREP UNDERSTATES IT BY CONSTRUCTION. The interpreter is the STRICTER arm, so any author who wrote the guard idiom over a refusing right operand hit the refusal while authoring and rewrote it -- most likely into a nested if or match. So the sites matching `cheap_guard && expensive` are the SURVIVORS, the cases where the right operand happens not to refuse; the cases carrying the correctness consequence were already edited away. A LOW COUNT IS THEREFORE NOT EVIDENCE THE CLASS IS MINOR AND MUST NOT BE REPORTED AS ONE. The honest population is sites where an author WANTED the guard idiom, which lives in the rewrites and is not reachable by the same needle. RECOGNITION RULE, stated to generalise past this operator: wherever a construct is realized independently by the interpreter and by an emission target, ask what fact decides its behaviour and where that fact is DECLARED. If the deciding fact is absent from the authority both arms are supposed to consult, the arms are not implementing one semantics, they are each inventing one, and agreement on the values you happened to test is not evidence they agree. The tell is a realization shape -- HostOperator -- that names WHO evaluates without naming WHAT is evaluated. RUNG: mitigatable at best, and only because one arm refuses loudly; against a source-to-emission path this is silent wrongness, which DESIGN section 4b places outside the ladder. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability and not an artifact: EVALUATION ORDER MODELED AS A PROPERTY OF A CONNECTIVE IN THE .dag AUTHORITY AND CONSULTED BY BOTH REALIZATIONS -- sufficient for the interpreter's binop arm to derive its strictness from the same row the emitter derives its rendering from, so that a connective's operand strategy cannot be stated twice or left unstated. A grep across dag/, src/v2/ and src/v1/*.dag on 2026-09-02 found no such fact: every short-circuit hit is prose in a comment or a witness name. NOT REPAIRED HERE: changing the interpreter to short-circuit is a corpus-wide evaluation-semantics change and needs its own subject, population and review; filing it against the missing carrier is the point of this row.",
  evidence: [],
}
data declared_return_disagrees_with_the_generic_it_returns: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "declared_return_disagrees_with_the_generic_it_returns" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a declared return type disagrees with the type its body actually produces, because the body's type comes from a GENERIC CALL'S INSTANTIATION** (INVALID STATE: a function declares `-> F<A>` and returns the result of `g<T>(...)` instantiated at `T = B`, so the produced type is `F<B>`. The declaration is authored independently of the body and nothing joins them, so `A` and `B` never meet. Every consumer then reads the DECLARATION, passes the value into a parameter typed `A`, and the mismatch surfaces -- if it surfaces at all -- as a runtime type error inside a callee that names neither the declaration nor the drift. HARM: this is the loud-but-hidden corner of section 5 rather than silent wrongness. The abort is honest when it happens; what is silent is the CLASS, because the drifted arm is commonly the one that is rarely reached, so the function reads as working while one of its inhabitants is unwritable-through. **DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS.** `state_space_conflation` is a domain modelled with too few constructors; here the domain is right and the CARRIER's parameter is wrong. `hollow_alias` is a second name for one concept; here there is one name and two types. **SPECIMEN (keen-ferret-172, gunbc#10109, 2026-09-02), and the two halves of it carry different warrants.** VERIFIED BY SOURCE, independently by two readers: `v2.std.runtime` `RuntimePrimitiveValue.bytes` is `List<Byte>`; `v2.std.collection` `list_at_optional<T>(xs: List<T>, index: Int) -> Optional<T>` therefore yields `Optional<Byte>`; `v2.std.native_agreement` `runtime_value_discriminant_octet` declares `-> Optional<Int>` and returns exactly that call; its `Present` arm feeds the value to `octet_display(octet: Int)`. VERIFIED BY EXECUTION, by one reader: `runtime_value_octet_label` over a `RuntimePrimitive` carrying two bytes aborts with `TypeError { msg: \"cannot apply Lt to Record and Int\" }`, while the same call over a zero-byte primitive returns `\"?\"` -- re-derive with the enrolled pair `label_of_a_two_byte_primitive` and `label_of_an_empty_primitive_is_unknown`, the first of which aborts against the pre-repair generation and the second of which passes in BOTH states and is therefore not a presence-detector for the repair. **WHY IT SURVIVED: THE ONLY REACHED ARM WAS THE ABSENT ONE.** `list_at_optional` at index 1 returns `Absent` for the short primitives the live paths carry, and `Absent` answers `\"?\"` without ever constructing the drifted value. So the formatter whose carrier note exists BECAUSE a revert once reported member and values unknown could itself abort exactly when a divergence was being reported. **RECOGNITION RULE, mechanical and cheap: for any function whose declared return is a GENERIC APPLICATION, name the call that produces the returned value and instantiate its type parameters from its ARGUMENTS, not from the enclosing declaration.** If the argument is a `List<B>` and the declaration says `F<A>` with `A` != `B`, the drift is there to read. The tell that makes it worth checking at all is a declared parameter of a primitive type -- `Int`, `String`, `Bool` -- reached from a container whose element type is a record. **A SECOND TELL, and it is the one that generalises past types: THE FUNCTION WAS UNWITNESSABLE.** This drift was found only after a fold's parameter was narrowed from a whole `TestClaimRun` to the `Verdict` it actually read, because the wide parameter required a cache receipt no witness could construct. THE TWO HALVES ARE DISTINCT AND AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS ROW CONFLATED THEM, which is corrected here rather than annotated: what ADMITTED the defect is the missing return-agreement judgment, and what left it UNEXPOSED is the oversized parameter, which deprived the affected fold of a constructible executing witness so that the incomplete typecheck was the only exercised admission path. So `a parameter wider than what the body reads` is a standing prompt to narrow it and then execute. AND SOURCE READING CAN ESTABLISH THE DRIFT: the recognition rule above is exactly that procedure, and two readers followed it independently -- `List<Byte>` instantiates `T = Byte`, so the produced type is `Optional<Byte>` against a declared `Optional<Int>`. Execution is required for the runtime abort and its observed message, NOT for the type disagreement; the earlier claim that reading cannot find this class was false, and it was false in a row whose own recognition rule refutes it. **RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable.** The failure is a typed runtime abort with containment but no locality: it names an operator and two shapes, not the declaration that lied. **CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed, and not 4.** A declared return is authored independently of the body, so a source file can always SPELL the disagreement; what is attainable is that no `Accepted` program contains one, by deriving the body's type and refusing the mismatch. It is decidable and fully modelled -- both types are in hand at the same grain -- so anything below 3 is a correctness gap rather than a ceiling. **NEXT TRIGGER, named as the CAPABILITY: return-type agreement checked at the declaration boundary, comparing a declared return against the body's inferred type THROUGH A GENERIC CALL'S INSTANTIATION.** The qualifier is the whole trigger and not decoration: a checker that compares only concrete returns is satisfied by this specimen while the class stays alive, because the drift enters through `T`. Until that capability exists this row is a review discipline, and citing it as coverage is rung inflation.", evidence: [] }
data non_execution_undifferentiated_by_what_it_silenced: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "non_execution_undifferentiated_by_what_it_silenced" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a required row does not execute, and NOTHING DECLARES WHAT ITS EXECUTION ESTABLISHED, so every non-execution looks alike** (INVALID STATE: a row that is preempted, skipped or otherwise reaches no verdict is reported as undecided, and the report carries no fact separating a row whose absence merely leaves a question open from a row whose absence REMOVES A WALL. HARM: the second kind is silently decoverage. The row PASSES in the ordinary case, so preempting it turns a standing guarantee off with nothing red anywhere -- and because the population cannot be ordered by consequence, the expensive rows get the optimisation attention while the load-bearing ones are invisible. A retry that draws a faster runner then buys a green OVER REFUSALS THAT DID NOT EXECUTE, which is why re-running is not an exit. SPECIMEN, and the two concepts are DISJOINT rather than conflated -- the opposite of what the lane suspected before it read the setter. `v1.cli_run` `InterruptedBeforeVerdict.enrolled_expected_red` is KnownRed QUARANTINE and nothing else: it is set true on exactly one branch of the required-floor claim loop, the expected-red arm reaching `ExpectedRedArm::BudgetRefused`, and it means the identity is rostered as DECLARED-TO-FAIL. The rows whose silencing motivated this class carry it FALSE. `test.claim.self_host_compile_phase_live_gate_witness` `a_live_tree_that_gained_an_identity_refuses_and_names_it` and `a_live_tree_that_swapped_an_identity_at_equal_cardinality_refuses` are ordinary PASSING rows on no expected-red, cost-debt or quarantine roster in the tree; their content is that `live_tree_frontier_verdict` returns `LiveFrontierRefused` and NAMES the planted identity. The second carries an in-source comment stating that it is precisely the probe that would go green if the join were replaced by a population-size comparison -- so preempting that one row makes that sentence stop being true while the run reports one more undecided claim. THAT IS THE WHOLE SEVERITY, and it is why the quarantine flag cannot stand in for the missing fact: quarantine names rows expected to be RED, and the silenced rows are GREEN by construction. Two different questions, one of them unasked. THE CARRIER FOR THE MISSING FACT ALREADY EXISTS AND IS INERT, which is what makes this one missing consumer rather than two problems. `std.witness_purpose` `WitnessPurpose` declares the authored taxonomy -- BehavioralDiscriminator, BoundaryCrossing, PopulationTotality, ExternalFidelity, ResourceContract -- landed under the operator's 2026-08-04 witness-cost-derives-from-purpose ruling, its own header stating that purpose is AUTHORED AND NOT INFERRED FROM IMPLEMENTATION. It is rostered in `v2.lens.inert_carrier` with the reason that it landed ahead of the consumer that derives witness size from it: zero witnesses declare one, zero consumers read one, and its only reference is its own taxonomy test `test.claim.witness_purpose_taxonomy_witness`. So the purpose vocabulary landed, the consumer slices never did, and in the meantime the required floor grew a cost mechanism that JUDGES ROWS WITH NO ACCESS TO WHAT ANY ROW IS FOR. The cpu_deadline population is unrankable for the same reason witness size is underivable. AN OBSERVABILITY FACT THAT MUST NOT BE RESTATED AS THE GAP, because this lane's first framing had it backwards and the correction is the load-bearing half. WHICH rows were preempted is ALREADY a joinable run product: `v1.cli_run` `write_required_floor_claim_cost_tsv` emits one row per EXECUTED claim carrying identity, module, outcome and `verdict_reached`, and the occurrence is minted in `v1.cli_run.required_floor_runner`'s claim loop BEFORE any classification branches, so preempted rows are present with `verdict_reached` false rather than dropped. The identities are not log-only. Reading the `INTERRUPTED-BEFORE-VERDICT` diagnostic lines as the population is `instrument_output_read_as_subject_content` and was committed twice in one lane. What is missing is not the population but the RANKING KEY over it. RECOGNITION RULE: when a mechanism reports that a check did not run, ask what the report lets a reader conclude about WHAT STOPPED BEING CHECKED. If the answer is nothing -- if a silenced wall and an open question produce the same row -- the mechanism counts non-executions without ranking them, and no amount of per-row cost detail supplies the missing fact. A second tell, which is what caught this one: a flag that looks like the distinction but is set on exactly one branch for a different reason. Read the SETTER before concluding a fact is represented. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The line does stop -- a non-verdict on a required claim blocks, typed and located -- so nothing is admitted that should not be; what is absent is the ability to rank what was lost. CEILING, and it is split rather than single because the two halves have different decidability. That every enrolled witness CARRIES a declared purpose is structurally guaranteeable: make the declaration mandatory at admission and a purposeless enrolled row has no constructor. That a declared purpose is TRUE of the row's body is undeclared intent and stays OUTSIDE the modeled guarantee -- observed and refused at a declared boundary, never inferred from the test body, which the taxonomy's own header forbids. Between them the join is mechanically preventable: a preempted row whose declared purpose is refusal-establishing reports as its own counted disposition, and rows with no declaration report as PURPOSE-UNDECLARED rather than as safe, which is the fail-closed direction. NEXT TRIGGER -- AN AUTHORED PURPOSE DECLARATION A FLOOR CONSUMER CAN JOIN AGAINST, and it is stated as the CAPABILITY because a trigger naming less gets satisfied while the capability stays dead. It must be sufficient for all three: (i) an operator ruling on whether refusal-establishing is a REFINEMENT of `BehavioralDiscriminator` carrying what the row requires to be refused, or a peer arm -- the coarse existing arm covers a positive control equally well, so spending it here would buy a key cited as coverage for a distinction it does not draw, which is the 4b(1) inflation that stops a class ever ranking for climbing; (ii) a purpose declared at IDENTITY grain that a witness authors, as a REAL DECLARATION BINDING A `DeclarationRef` TO THE ROW rather than a source annotation -- 4c forecloses the cheap version of this outright, because semantic passes receive only the ANNOTATION-ERASED PROJECTION, so an annotated purpose is unreadable by the floor BY CONSTRUCTION and would be a declaration no consumer could ever join against. That is 4c's own rule that an annotation is never evidence a machine claim holds, applied to this fact; it is recorded here so the annotation is not re-proposed as an economy later. And not a roster of interesting rows kept by hand -- this class has already retracted one hand-derivation described as a run product, and selecting a first population out of the non-verdict arm would be that shape a third time, since the selection would be derived from the very run product whose membership is redrawn per attempt; (iii) a floor consumer joining that declaration against `verdict_reached` and counting the undeclared remainder. THE CONSUMER DESIGN IS BLOCKED ON THE RULING AND IS NOT REJECTED ON MERIT -- recorded so the next lane does not re-derive it and does not read the absence as a refusal of the approach. NOT PROPOSED, AND EXCLUDED BY THE OPERATOR WHEN ASKED: raising the 500ms ceiling, widening a budget, moving rows to a laxer lane, or making the floor stop refusing on non-verdicts. Each hides the class rather than ranking it, and the last also deletes the refusal that makes the silencing detectable at all. This row is about what is REPORTED, never about what is ADMITTED. RELATED: `non_verdict_disposition_surfaces_as_refusal` carries the aggregate-boundary half, and the `gunbc.rung_drop` row `floor_cost_claim_qualification_unavailable` carries the cost half -- neither names the missing purpose join, which is why this is its own row.", evidence: [] }

data authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**the GENERATED PROJECTION is merge-protected and the HAND-AUTHORED AUTHORITY it is derived from is not, so the file where losing a fact is unrecoverable is exactly the file git resolves silently** (INVALID STATE: a repository binds a refusing merge driver to a path because that path is machine-derived and a wrong merge there is undetectable by reading, while the declaration file the projection is derived FROM matches no merge attribute at all and falls through to vanilla three-way text merge. The protection is attached to the CHEAP side. A bad merge in the projection is repaired by regenerating it; a bad merge in the authority destroys a fact that exists nowhere else, and the projection then faithfully renders the loss. HARM: DESIGN section 5's fail-closed arm holds on the derived artifact and fails open on the source of truth, in the same repository, for the same class of content, by omission rather than by decision. THREE MEASUREMENTS, all against origin/main on 2026-09-03 and each re-derivable by the command named beside it. (1) GRAIN. `git show origin/main:dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode.dag | awk '\{print NR\": \"length($0)}' | sort -t: -k2 -rn | head -3` reports line 144 at 16,792 characters, next 14,309, next 10,080. One row is one line by this carrier's own deliberate design -- see the WHY EVERY ROW IS ONE LINE block above -- so git's merge grain, the line, is coarser than the unit of authorship, the receipt. Several lanes appending several receipts to one class produce one both-sides-changed line, and the only resolutions the tool offers are ours, theirs, or hand composition. (2) POLARITY. `git check-attr merge -- <path>` over the pairs: `docs/design-failure-modes.md` and `docs/design-rung-drops.md` resolve to `merge: generated-artifact`; `dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode.dag` and `dag/gunbc/rung_drop.dag` resolve to `merge: unspecified`. Grepping `.gitattributes` for either authority module name returns zero matches. The driver is bound to three `dag/gunbc/stage0/*_generated.dag` files, DESIGN.md, and the stage0 Rust mirrors -- every one of them machine-derived. That is the polarity, and it is not an oversight in the attribute file so much as a consequence of deriving the rule from GENERATEDNESS rather than from IRRECOVERABILITY. (3) PRESSURE. `git log --since='6 hours ago' origin/main -- dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode.dag` reports seven commits in six hours from distinct lanes. This is not a rare collision; it is the busiest hand-authored file in the tree during a fan-out. WHY THIS OUTRANKS THE PROJECTION-DRIFT CLASS AND MUST NOT BE FOLDED INTO IT. Different mechanism: there, a driver runs and refuses, and the repair is to regenerate. Here NO driver runs, git answers with a plain textual merge, and there is nothing to regenerate from. Different failure signature: the projection class announces itself as an unmerged path with a printed recipe; this class announces nothing at all -- it produces a clean merge, a green build, and a passing gate, because a roster that lost one receipt is still well-formed .dag and still projects. Different repair: the projection class is already at its rung; this one has no mechanism yet. THE SILENT LOSS IS THE WHOLE POINT, stated concretely because the abstract version reads as tolerable: with seven lanes on one file and one class-row spanning 16,792 characters, a fifth lane taking `--ours` or `--theirs` on that line deletes another lane's receipt with no conflict marker surviving, no test red, and no reviewer signal, since the diff it presents is a plausible edit to a paragraph nobody reads end to end. The receipt is gone and the row still says what it said. CORRECT HANDLING, and it is verified by CONTENT rather than by the merge succeeding -- that distinction is this row's practical advice. On 2026-09-02 this exact collision occurred on line 144 between this lane and calm-boar-314. The resolution was COMPOSITION: neither side taken, both receipts re-read and merged into one sentence sequence by hand. It was then checked by asserting properties OF THE RESULTING TEXT -- all four expected receipt markers present, zero conflict markers anywhere in the file, and every double-quote in the composed line either a field delimiter or escaped, counted against the pre-merge blob -- not by observing that `git merge` exited zero. A successful merge is evidence about the TOOL, not about the CONTENT, and on an unprotected path with a coarse grain it is specifically the evidence that is available when the content is wrong. THE QUOTE CHECK EARNS ITS PLACE SEPARATELY, AND ITS FIRST FORMULATION WAS WRONG IN A WAY WORTH CARRYING: counting quotes and requiring an EVEN total is not an invariant of this carrier at all, because an escaped quote inside a row's prose is a single legal character and rows freely carry odd numbers of them -- this row itself does. A parity oracle therefore reds on correct compositions and, worse, greens on a composition that dropped one escaped quote and gained another. The discriminating form is POSITIONAL: enumerate every double-quote in the line and require each to be either one of the four field delimiters or immediately preceded by a backslash, which is `grep -oP '(?<!\\)\"'` returning exactly four. The reason to record the wrong version beside the right one is that the wrong one was chosen because it was cheap to compute and it passed on the specimen. THE DEFECT IT GUARDS: composition inside a 16,792-character line splits an escaped `\\\"` pair if the insertion point is chosen by searching for a substring that also occurs inside some other row's prose, which happened once in this lane and was caught only because the check was run against the PRISTINE file first to establish what a clean reading looks like. TWO FURTHER OCCURRENCES ON 2026-09-03, WHICH IS WHAT MOVES THIS FROM ONE SPECIMEN TO A RECURRENCE, and both are LOUD -- recorded because a row about silent loss must not imply every reach is silent. (a) `dag/gunbc/guarantee_rung_drop.dag`: gunbc#10021 and this lane each appended one row to `all_guarantee_stalls`, git reported CONFLICT with markers, and the resolution was additive because the two subjects are disjoint. (b) `dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode.dag` itself, appending this very row: a marker conflict on the roster line against another lane's new class. **OCCURRENCE (b) EXHIBITED BOTH ARMS OF THE POLARITY IN ONE MERGE, which is the cleanest evidence this row will get.** The same `git merge` left the unprotected `.dag` authority conflicted WITH markers and left the driver-bound `docs/design-failure-modes.md` marked unmerged with ZERO markers -- one command, two paths, two different failure surfaces, exactly as the attribute file predicts. WHAT THE LOUD CASES ESTABLISH AND WHAT THEY DO NOT: they show that a roster-line collision between two APPENDING lanes is visible, because two additions at one insertion point differ textually. They say nothing about the silent case this row is filed for, which is two lanes editing ONE 16,792-character row, where the conflict is over a line neither lane authored in full and a side can be taken without any marker surviving to say what was dropped. The frequency is the finding: three reaches in about twenty-four hours on two carriers, so the busy path is real and the coarse-grain case is a matter of when, not whether. PROJECTIONS ARE REGENERATED AND NEVER MERGED, which occurrence (b) also demonstrates: the correct handling of the driver's markerless refusal is to resolve the AUTHORITY and re-derive the document from it, and any attempt to hand-compose the `.md` would be authoring a projection by hand. RECOGNITION RULE, stated to generalise past this repository: for every path a merge policy protects, name the file that path is DERIVED FROM and check whether it is protected too. If the derived side is guarded and the source side is bare, the policy is protecting the recoverable half. The tell is a `.gitattributes` whose predicate is `generated` -- generatedness is a proxy for the real predicate, which is whether a wrong merge is DETECTABLE BY READING THE RESULT. A generated file fails that test because nobody reads it; a 16,792-character hand-authored roster line fails it for the identical reason, and the attribute file cannot see the resemblance. RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable, and only by author diligence -- the mitigation is that a human composed instead of choosing a side, which is not a mechanism and does not survive the next tired lane. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. Membership is decidable: whether a path's merge result preserves both sides' semantic additions is decidable for a ROSTER, because a roster is a set of identified rows and a merge that drops one is a merge whose output set is not the union of the two input sets. That is an identity join, not a count comparison -- DESIGN section 5 -- and it is exactly the shape a refusing merge driver over the .dag parse tree could compute. Rung 4 is not attainable while the carrier is a text file, since the invalid state remains spellable by hand. NEXT TRIGGER, named as the CAPABILITY and not as an artifact: A SEMANTIC MERGE DRIVER OVER .dag DECLARATION IDENTITY -- sufficient to take two versions of a roster carrier, resolve them at DECLARATION grain rather than line grain, admit a merge only when every identity present in either side is present in the output, and REFUSE with a located diagnostic naming the dropped identity otherwise. WHAT DOES NOT DISCHARGE THIS: binding the existing `generated-artifact` driver to these two authority paths. That driver refuses on every both-sides-changed reach, which on the busiest hand-authored file in the tree converts a nightly composition task into a nightly line-stop, and it still resolves at line grain, so it would neither detect the loss nor permit the correct composition -- it would only make the loss loud by making all merging impossible. Nor does splitting the row further discharge it: finer rows reduce the collision RATE, which is worth doing on its own merits, and leave the silent-loss MECHANISM untouched for any row two lanes do share. NOT REPAIRED HERE, and the reason is this row's own subject: writing a merge driver is a carrier-level capability with its own population and review, and filing it against the missing capability is the point of the row.", evidence: [] }
data external_mechanism_asserted_under_a_correct_conclusion: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "external_mechanism_asserted_under_a_correct_conclusion" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a MECHANISM about external reality is asserted as the reason for a conclusion that is independently CORRECT, so nothing the repository can execute ever refutes it** (INVALID STATE: a carrier states WHY an external system behaves as it does -- this platform suppresses that trigger, that endpoint rate-limits, this token cannot start a run -- and derives a design decision from it. The DECISION is right; the mechanism was never measured. HARM: DESIGN section 5 silent wrongness, and it is the immunised variety. A wrong premise attached to a wrong conclusion dies the first time the conclusion is tested. Here every test of the conclusion PASSES, so the premise is confirmed by association and hardens into the sentence later readers plan against -- and it is consumed for facts the conclusion never covered, which is where it is false. THE DISCRIMINATING QUESTION IS ALWAYS THE SAME: the conclusion says the good outcome does not HAPPEN; the mechanism says the machinery does not EXIST. Those differ exactly on cost and on remedy. If the thing exists and is merely withheld, something can release it, something already paid for it, and a second copy is a duplicate. RECOGNITION RULE, mechanical: for any prose of the form THE PLATFORM DOES NOT DO X, name the observation that would show X happening and say whether anyone ran it. If the only evidence offered is that the conclusion held, the mechanism is unmeasured. The sharpest tell is a mechanism stated in an ABSENCE form -- starts no run, sends no event, creates nothing -- beside a conclusion stated in an OUTCOME form; absence and non-execution are two states and the carrier collapsed them. DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOURS. `unbacked_execution_claim` is about an in-repository relation an authority could have backed and did not; here the subject is OUTSIDE the modeled guarantee, so no authority in the tree could have backed it and the only route is observation at the boundary. `state_space_conflation` names too few constructors for a modelled domain; here the domain is unmodelled and the prose supplies a two-state story for a three-state world. SPECIMEN (cool-koi-623, 2026-09-03). `gunbc.rung_drop` `floor_cut_heal` and the annotation above `gunbc.ci_spec` `gunbc_ci_heal_commit_push_script` both said an Actions-credential push starts no workflow run, GitHub suppressing that edge to stop a job triggering itself, and concluded that heal must exit nonzero rather than speak for a head nothing judged. The rung_drop row carries the correction; the ci_spec annotation still carries the refuted sentence AT THE TIME THIS ROW IS FILED, because that carrier is held by a concurrent lane and a second lane editing one premise from its own verdict is how one fact acquires two authorities -- recorded here as an observation rather than repaired here. The conclusion is correct and remains in force. The mechanism is false: over the whole heal-push population a pull_request run was CREATED 4 times out of 4, and it is EXECUTION that is withheld -- 0 of the 4 started a single job on the triggering attempt. The receipts and the re-derivation recipe are carried in that rung_drop row rather than restated here. WHAT THE FALSE MECHANISM CONCEALED, which is the harm made concrete: under starts-no-run a dispatched revalidation is free, and measured it is a SECOND run on that head whose check runs a name-keyed reader cannot separate from the held run s; and the human action that releases a healed head is an approve on that specific held run, not the re-run the annotation offered. A METHOD NOTE THAT IS PART OF THE CLASS RATHER THAN OF THE SPECIMEN: the first two readers of this population both read a run s TOP-LEVEL conclusion and its start timestamp and concluded the runs had executed. A run can conclude failure having started zero jobs, and a later attempt can execute after a human acts. When the subject is EXECUTION, count jobs on the attempt the event created, never read the latest attempt. RUNG FOUND AT: 1 ON AXIS (i) BELOW, mitigatable. The harm is contained because the conclusion the premise was offered for is independently sound; nothing was admitted that should not have been. A SECOND HARM THE SPECIMEN MADE VISIBLE AND THE CLASS SHOULD CARRY: the unmeasured mechanism was stated UNSCOPED, so the sentence is true at the moment it is written and can stop being true with nobody touching it -- here a held run may be released hours later and judge the head, at which point 'a head nothing judged' is simply false. Measure the mechanism, and then say WHEN the claim holds. THE SUBJECT OF THIS ROW IS A CARRIER IN THIS REPOSITORY, NOT THE EXTERNAL SYSTEM, and an earlier revision of this row got that backwards -- corrected here rather than annotated, because the error is exactly the one section 4b's carve-out exists to prevent. That revision assigned a LADDER RUNG to external reality, which section 4b deliberately keeps OFF the ladder, and then declined to name a trigger; between them those two moves let 'we do not model GitHub' stand where a rankable in-repository defect actually sits. The invalid state is an AUTHORING ACT that is wholly in the tree: a carrier states an unobserved mechanism as the reason for a decision. That is decidable from the carrier alone, so it ranks, and it is obligated to climb. TWO AXES, WITH DIFFERENT CEILINGS BECAUSE THEY HAVE DIFFERENT DECIDABILITY, and only the first is a ladder subject at all. (i) THE SEPARATION -- is this mechanism claim backed by an observation? Decidable by reading the carrier. CEILING: 4, structurally impossible, and DERIVED rather than aspirational: if the only construction able to express an external-system mechanism requires the observation that produced it, an unbacked mechanism claim has no constructor, and validation becomes unnecessary because the bad state cannot be written. Anything below 4 on this axis is a correctness gap, not a ceiling. (ii) THE TRUTH of the external fact -- whether the observed behaviour still holds. OUTSIDE THE MODELED GUARANTEE, not a rung and never one: observed, refused or mitigated at a declared boundary, never fabricated. It is named here precisely so it cannot be mistaken for a weak implementation that should climb. NEXT TRIGGER FOR AXIS (i), NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY AND NOT AS AN ARTIFACT: an external-system mechanism claim is expressible ONLY through a typed construction carrying the observation that produced it -- the query, the population, the date -- together with a consumer that ENUMERATES carriers stating such a claim without one. The pairing is the whole trigger: the construction alone makes the honest form available, and only the enumerating consumer makes the dishonest form unwritable rather than merely noticed once. Authoring one such row by hand discharges nothing and is the artifact-for-capability substitution section 4b(3) forbids. It is CAN-CLIMB-NOW-BUT-UNBUILT rather than blocked on grounding: `extdeps` already owns the shape for cited upstream facts. SECTION 4c DECIDES WHERE THIS CANNOT LIVE, recorded so the cheap version is not proposed later as an economy: semantic passes receive only the annotation-erased projection, so an annotation can never carry the observation and the construction must be a real declaration. WHAT THE DISCHARGED TRIGGER DOES NOT BUY, stated so it is not read as covering axis (ii): every mechanism claim would then carry a receipt, and a receipt is not currency -- a system that changes without notice makes any observation a statement about a past world. That residual is axis (ii) and stays outside the guarantee by construction. WHAT IS ASYMMETRIC ABOUT THIS CLASS, and it is why it survives review rather than why it cannot be ranked: the DEFECT is visible from inside the tree -- a claim with no observation beside it -- while the REFUTATION lives in the external system and no lens, gate or witness reading this tree can reach it. So the class is detectable here and falsifiable only there, which is what lets a wrong mechanism sit unchallenged beside a correct conclusion for as long as nobody goes outside to look. Until axis (i)'s trigger is built this row is a reading discipline and citing it as coverage is the rung inflation section 4b(1) names.", evidence: [] }

data obligation_fields_as_prose_make_their_own_grain_check_undecidable: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "obligation_fields_as_prose_make_their_own_grain_check_undecidable" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**the facts an obligation REQUIRES are carried as one prose field, so the obligation's own consistency is not a join any consumer can run -- and the mismatch it hides is then found, if at all, by a human reading a paragraph** (INVALID STATE: a typed carrier whose record declares identity and a few labels while every fact the governing rule NAMES lives inside one `String`. DESIGN section 4b(3) names five for a rung drop -- previous rung, temporary rung, reason, bounded population, restoration trigger -- and `gunbc.rung_drop`'s `RungDrop` has a field for none of them. HARM, and it is not that prose is ugly: the rule's OWN review tell becomes unmechanisable. 4b(3) tells reviewers to watch for a grain mismatch between the loss sentence and the trigger sentence -- a plural loss with a singular trigger, a corpus loss with a per-module trigger. That is a JOIN over two populations, decidable the moment both are typed, and undecidable while both are sentences. THE SPECIMEN IS MEASURED, NOT HYPOTHETICAL (gunbc#10154, 2026-09-03). `floor_cut`'s loss clause named EIGHT lost capabilities; its restoration trigger enumerated FIVE siblings; one of those five had ALREADY RETIRED. On that path the row would have retired with three undeclared-dead guarantees under it, no row standing over them and no trigger left to fire. **THE AGGRAVATING FACT IS THAT THE GAP SURVIVED A REPAIR AUTHORED AGAINST THE EXACT TELL.** The trigger had been rewritten once already, on 2026-09-01, specifically to replace a prose-edit trigger with capability-grain siblings -- and that rewrite enumerated five against a loss sentence naming eight, in the same paragraph, without anyone noticing. A defect that survives its own targeted repair is evidence about the MEDIUM, not about the author's care. AND IT WAS NOT FOUND BY AUDIT: it surfaced from the floor's refusal of an unrelated PR. Nothing was looking. WHY THIS IS NOT `check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim`, which is the nearest row and answers a different question. There, a check EXECUTES, is reached, goes green, and its implementation ranges over less than its declared subject -- the repair is to widen the check's range. Here NO check exists or can exist over the subject at all, because the two populations to be joined are not addressable; the repair is to type the fields so that a check becomes WRITABLE. One is a wall with too narrow a range; the other is a wall that cannot be built. They will co-occur -- once the fields are typed, the resulting join can itself under-range, which is that row and not this one. WHAT THIS ROW DOES NOT CLAIM, because the carrier already argued the other side and it argued it well. `gunbc.rung_drop`'s own module note pre-registers this exact point: it records that splitting `authored` into the five fields was deliberately NOT attempted, because deciding per row which sentence is the reason and which the population is semantic rewriting with no oracle, and because doing it inside a relocation would make a content change indistinguishable from a move. That reasoning is sound and this row does not contest it -- the note is CITED rather than restated (DESIGN section 3). **WHAT THIS ROW ADDS IS THE CONSEQUENCE, WHICH CHANGES THE PRIORITY WITHOUT CHANGING THE ARGUMENT.** The note reasons from AUTHORING COST -- the split is expensive and unoracled, so defer it. The measured consequence is that while it is deferred, the obligation's own consistency check cannot be written, and a grain mismatch of exactly the kind 4b(3) warns about survived in a load-bearing row until an unrelated refusal exposed it. That converts the field split from tidiness into a correctness obligation with a demonstrated cost, and DESIGN section 4b is explicit that below ceiling is a correctness gap and never optional elegance. THE SEQUENCING THE NOTE ITSELF ASKED FOR IS NOW ARRIVING: the note says the field work lands in a follow-up where each row is a readable diff, and gunbc#10197 splits the carrier one row per file, which is that condition. Before it, the change is dozens of edits to one file with no reviewable unit; after it, each row is an independent diff. So the blocker the note names is dissolving on another lane's schedule, and this row exists so the obligation is not forgotten when it does. RECOGNITION RULE, stated to generalise past this carrier: **for any rule that NAMES the facts a declaration must carry, count how many of those names are FIELDS.** If the count is zero and the rule also supplies a review tell, the tell is unmechanisable by construction and the rule is enforced by attention alone. The tell that you are looking at an instance rather than at ordinary prose is a governing document that enumerates required facts, plus a carrier whose record shape does not mention any of them, plus a review instruction phrased as something a reader should NOTICE. A SECOND, SHARPER TELL: the carrier has a SIBLING that types the same family of obligation. `gunbc.guarantee_rung_drop`'s `GuaranteeStall` carries subject, current rung, ceiling, blocker, population and next-rung trigger as typed fields, and has TWO EXECUTING CONSUMERS over them -- `every_live_stall_is_below_its_ceiling` and `every_live_stall_names_a_next_rung_trigger`. Two carriers for two genuinely distinct 4b obligations is correct and is NOT a section 3 fork; what is not correct is that one of them can check itself and the other cannot. The sibling is the existence proof that the fields are authorable. **A BOUND ON THE TRIGGER BELOW, ESTABLISHED BY SOMEONE BUILDING THE WRONG VERSION OF IT (zesty-gull-732, 2026-09-03), recorded so this row's own remedy is not cited past its subject.** I proposed to that lane a neighbouring invariant -- every sibling identity a row NAMES resolves to a file -- and they implemented it, which falsified it twice. FIRST, the general form is not computable from `authored` at all: a backticked name in prose may be a sibling drop, a function, a data row in another module or a config key, and a prefix heuristic reported 21 UNRESOLVED across 10 rows, every one a false positive. A smuggled heuristic standing exactly where the structure is missing, which is an INSTANCE of this row rather than a check that could precede it. SECOND and sharper: narrowed to the one family a naming convention makes decidable, it ran GREEN on a tree carrying five siblings where main had eight. A whole-file restructure keeps its whole side, so the trigger TEXT and the sibling ROWS are lost together and the family stays internally consistent while being three guarantees short. **A self-consistency check cannot discriminate a CONSISTENT STALE COPY** -- green before the loss, green after it, green on the merged tree -- so it would be cited as coverage for a class it never touches. WHAT THAT DOES AND DOES NOT BOUND. It does NOT weaken the trigger below, whose subject is the grain relation WITHIN one row -- does this row's trigger population span this row's loss population -- which is decidable once both are fields and is exactly what no reader reliably performs. It DOES establish that such a join is confined to one tree, so it can never detect rows LOST BETWEEN TREES; that defect lives in the relationship between two versions and is invisible to anything reading one. Those are different subjects with different oracles, the second being an external comparison against another tree, and this row claims only the first. The general lesson is the cheaper one: the way that limit was found was by BUILDING the check and running it against the tree it was supposed to refuse. A proposed invariant that has not been run against its own discriminating red is a specification, and DESIGN section 5 says so. I proposed it without doing that; they did it, and the proposal did not survive. RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder. The failure is silent by construction -- a mismatched row is well-formed, projects cleanly, and passes every gate, because nothing reads inside the field. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. Once previous rung, temporary rung, reason, population and trigger are typed, 'the trigger's population spans the loss population' is a decidable join at identity grain, and a row failing it need not be `Accepted`. Rung 4 is not attainable while a population is a list of names an author writes, since a wrong name is still spellable. NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY: **the five 4b(3) facts carried as TYPED FIELDS on the drop carrier, with an executing consumer that joins a row's trigger population against its loss population and REFUSES a row whose trigger does not span it** -- sufficient for the `floor_cut` five-against-eight state to be refused rather than reviewed. Typing the fields WITHOUT that consumer does not discharge this: the sibling carrier shows fields plus consumers is the shape that works, and fields alone would leave the same tell unmechanised in a nicer record. Nor does the one-row-per-file split discharge it -- that removes the CONFLICT grain and leaves every fact still inside one prose field, which is how this row is known to be a distinct subject from gunbc#10197 rather than a restatement of it.)", evidence: [] }
data absence_classifier_default_bucket: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "absence_classifier_default_bucket" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**absence-classifier default bucket, unprotected by its residual refusal** (a classifier whose ACCEPTED bucket is defined by the ABSENCE of properties is only as complete as the enumeration of kinds it was derived from, and it fails silently TOWARD THE DEFAULT rather than toward its refusal arm. The refusal reads as coverage and is not: a residual can only catch kinds whose absence PATTERN differs from the accepted one, which is a strictly smaller population than the kinds that exist. RECOGNITION RULE: A RESIDUAL REFUSAL DOES NOT PROTECT A CLASSIFIER WHOSE ACCEPTED BUCKET IS DEFINED BY ABSENCE; A NEW KIND CAN SILENTLY RESEMBLE THE DEFAULT. THE CLASS HAS NOW PRODUCED BOTH POLARITIES FROM ONE CLASSIFIER, which is what makes it structural rather than anecdotal. v1.compiler.parse decided 'this module item is a type declaration' from no body AND no transport AND no type annotation. OVER-STAMPING: `resource Filesystem` / `Clock` / `Entropy` in std.resources carry none of those three, so all three were stamped TYPE DECLARATIONS -- and the exhaustive match's ModuleItemUnrecognized arm could not fire, because a resource is not unrecognised, it is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a type under that rule. The premise that the item kinds were four was falsified by the parser's own item error, which names ten: alias, type, fn, func, service, resource, data, extern, pattern, interface. UNDER-STAMPING: the repair keyed the resource arm on `properties` being non-empty, and `type X sole_constructor { .. }` carries a property too -- so 202 sole-constructor type declarations across 100 modules were classified as RESOURCES and vanished from the declaration population. Opposite direction, same classifier, same root: an absence-and-presence heuristic standing where a positive kind belongs. WHY EXCLUSION-BY-NAME IS NOT THE FIX EITHER, though it is what stands today: the surviving repair excludes the ONE modifier the minting authority owns, and it is complete by ENUMERATION OF MINTING SITES rather than by grep -- v1.compiler.parse has exactly two, parsed_sole_constructor_properties (one field-init named sole_constructor, the only source every type-item constructor passes along) and parse_resource_entries; nominal_opaque is dropped lexically by drop_leading_type_modifier and mints nothing; mint_parsed_optional_int_property is confined to nested where-predicate nodes. A one-member set established by construction is worth more than a longer list found by search. But a second modifier that MINTS a property on a type item reintroduces this in the same silent direction, and no longer list can prevent that. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: parse constructors that CARRY the module-item kind they already dispatched on, consumed by an exhaustive match with NO DEFAULT TYPE BUCKET -- at which point membership is decided at construction and the residual refusal becomes real rather than decorative. THE SECOND SPECIMEN IS IN A DIFFERENT AUTHORITY AND IS FILED, NOT REPAIRED: v1.compiler.emit_core_support is_bare_leaf_item reads a CAPABILITY-LESS resource as a type declaration -- `resource Network` and `resource AuthContext` in std.resources have no children, no body, no params and no connective -- so the emit-side shape predicates carry the same defect in the same direction. Two specimens, one module, unrepaired here because it is a change to a different authority and smuggling it into a parser change would fork the subject. THE COUNTERMEASURE, AND IT IS THE MOST TRANSFERABLE THING IN THIS ROW: those two were invisible while ONE classifier answered, because both readers of the question AGREED they were types -- the agreed-wrong pair a disagreement census cannot see by construction ([[disagreement_census_blind_to_agreed_wrong]]), and no amount of running that census harder finds it. Splitting the question across two INDEPENDENTLY DERIVED readers -- absence-of-body/transport/annotation in the parser versus connective/params/children in the emitter -- converted their agreement into a disagreement, which is the only form the census can report. That split arrived here as a side effect of building the population join, not as a design goal, which is exactly why it is written down: RECOGNITION RULE: WHERE A CENSUS COMPARES TWO READERS, A THIRD INDEPENDENTLY-DERIVED READER IS THE ONLY THING THAT CAN FALSIFY THEIR AGREEMENT -- reach for it ON PURPOSE when an agreed-wrong population is suspected. The corpus-wide instrument is `type_occurrence_binding_census --establish`, joining the two readers at occurrence-id grain with uniqueness on both sides and no extra members.)", evidence: [] }

data green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**an instrument reports GREEN over a population it does not own, so a fact can be filed in an authority, absent from the projection readers are pointed at, and nothing refuses** (INVALID STATE: two actuators split one generated-artifact population, and the one lanes habitually run denominates only its own half. `claim_executor --required-regen` reports `first_generation_equal=true planned=155 executed=155 adjudicated=155` while `docs/design-failure-modes.md` is STALE, because the ledger projections are produced by a different actuator entirely -- `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry dag/gunbc/instruments/generated_artifact_gate.dag --function main_wet`. HARM: a lane files a row in `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode`, runs the regen, sees 155/155/155, and stops -- having shipped a row that exists in the authority and nowhere a reader can see it, since DESIGN.md points readers at the projection and not at the .dag. The green is not merely uninformative about the projection; it is READ as covering it, because the instrument's name and its round numbers make no distinction between the population it adjudicated and the population it was asked about. SPECIMEN, and it is the row filed beside this one: `absence_classifier_default_bucket` was authored into the authority, `--required-regen` returned first_generation_equal=true, and the projection still did not contain it. The gap was found by GREPPING THE PROJECTION for the row just filed, which is not a step any gate performs. THE TWO NEIGHBOURS THIS IS NOT, cited so the family is readable and this row is not consolidated into either. [[incidental_denominator_as_wall]] is THE SAME DENOMINATOR SHAPE WITH THE OPPOSITE SIGN: there, `is_compared_generated_basename` -- whose job is to denominate the DRIFT COMPARISON -- accidentally CREATED safety by never handing an installer a dangerous input, so nothing is wrong today and the harm is that the protection is uncredited and dissolves silently when the upstream question changes. Here the same accident runs the other way: a denominator written for one question accidentally DESTROYS COVERAGE while continuing to report green, and something IS wrong today. Uncredited protection versus credited assurance that is not there. [[authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded]] is a MERGE-TIME protection asymmetry over the same file pair -- projection driver-bound, hand-authored authority matching no merge attribute -- repaired by binding the driver to the authority path. This row is REGEN-TIME and is reachable with no merge in sight. (Two notes worth keeping. That merge row landed in the very merge that conflicted the branch filing this one, and it had already measured the 16,792-character line 144 that made the conflict hazardous -- the hazard was filed by another lane before this one hit it. And it has since been observed firing in production on a SIBLING lane's head: `git merge-tree --write-tree` returned rc=1 with BOTH projections refusing while `gh pr view` reported mergeable=MERGEABLE on that same commit, observed simultaneously -- a cleaner specimen of that row than the one it was filed with, and a second instrument disagreeing with a green.) A SECOND SPECIMEN, RECORDED BECAUSE THE AUTHOR OF THIS ROW COMMITTED THE SAME SHAPE WITHIN THE HOUR OF FILING IT, IN THE OPPOSITE DIRECTION: asked whether CI would ever run on a merge-conflicted head, they polled one branch once a minute for six minutes, observed no run, and reported that GitHub does not create runs for a head it cannot merge -- a NEVER claimed from an instrument whose denominator was one branch and six minutes. The control was one command away and refuted it: three other DIRTY pull requests in the same repository carried six and seven check-runs each, while the two heads at zero were simply the two most recently pushed, one dirty and one clean, under a backlog of sixty-two unfinished runs. Recency separated the population perfectly and dirtiness did not separate it at all. The general form is this row's own, with the sign flipped: there an instrument's GREEN was read as covering a population it never enumerated; here an instrument's SILENCE was. A transient state proves nothing about membership without duration or a control already sitting in the state being called impossible -- and DESIGN section 5 names the tell in advance, since NEVER is the word that lets a ratchet pass as a wall. RECOGNITION RULE: when an instrument reports a clean round count, ask WHICH ARTIFACTS ITS DENOMINATOR ENUMERATES and whether the artifact you changed is among them -- a per-artifact count is evidence about the artifacts counted and says nothing whatever about the ones the actuator does not own, while reading exactly like whole-population coverage. The tell is two actuators over one declared population with no join between their denominators. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: ONE adjudication over the whole declared generated-artifact population, so that a stale projection is a refusal from the same run that adjudicates the mirrors; failing that, a green that NAMES ITS OWN BOUNDARY -- reporting the artifacts it did not adjudicate rather than a bare count -- which is the weaker form and turns silent non-coverage into a stated one. RUNG: mitigatable. NOT REPAIRED HERE: extending an actuator's population or splitting its report is a change to the regen authority and does not belong in the diff that discovered it.)", evidence: [] }

data artifact_declares_a_threshold_it_is_not_measured_against: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "artifact_declares_a_threshold_it_is_not_measured_against" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**an artifact's column names a governing threshold and carries a constant that is not the threshold enforced, so the artifact cannot predict the refusal it exists to explain** (INVALID STATE: a machine-readable receipt carries a field named for the limit its subject is judged against, and the value is a constant unrelated to the limit the judge actually applies. MEASURED on gunbc#10200's required run (run 33722461610, artifact `required-floor-claim-cost`, 2026-09-03): all 3534 rows of `required_floor_claim_cost.tsv` declare `cost_line_ms=100`, while the same run's floor refuses rows against a 500ms per-claim CPU budget and says so in its own refusal text. **300 of 3534 rows exceed the line the FILE declares; 13 exceed the line actually ENFORCED.** A consumer computing an over-cost population from the artifact gets a set 23 times too large, in a well-formed way, with no error anywhere and no column missing. HARM: the artifact is the only durable record of per-claim cost, so it is what anyone reaches for to ask whether a refusal was predictable, whether a row is near the line, or whether a population regressed. Every one of those questions is answered wrongly by the same factor, and the wrongness is invisible because 100 is a plausible per-claim budget. **THE SHARP POINT, AND IT IS WHY THIS IS ITS OWN ROW: THE PRESCRIBED REMEDY FOR THE NEIGHBOURING HAZARD DOES NOT PROTECT AGAINST THIS ONE, AND LOOKS LIKE IT DOES.** `gunbc.floor_cost_distribution` already records this constant, as a COLUMN-ORDERING hazard: `eval_steps` was inserted into the artifact between vintages, so a parser keyed on index 6 reads `cost_line_ms` -- the constant 100 -- as a step count and produces microsecond figures three orders of magnitude off, measured on three of eleven sampled runs. That note's remedy is DESIGN section 3's standing rule: locate columns by NAME, never by position. That remedy is correct for its own hazard and is exactly what fails here. A consumer who follows it perfectly -- reads the header, finds `cost_line_ms` by name, uses it as the line -- still computes the wrong population, because the defect is not WHERE the column is but WHAT IT SAYS. Citing by name protects a reader from a moved column; nothing protects them from a column whose name asserts a role its value does not fill. That note is CITED here, not restated, and the addition is that its constant is not merely a parsing trap but a false statement about the enforced line. WHY IT IS NOT `meaning_fork`: that class is one name carrying two material referents under hidden state, and its recognition rule is to hold the naming surface constant and vary the hidden state until the referent changes. Here there are not two referents. There is ONE name making ONE assertion -- this is the line this row is judged against -- which is simply false, at every vintage, for every row, with no state to vary. The dual is nicknaming and this is neither: it is a field whose name claims an authority relation its value does not have. THE DISTRIBUTION IS THE RECEIPT AND IT IS WHAT MAKES THE 5x GAP CONSEQUENTIAL RATHER THAN COSMETIC. Against the enforced 500ms line, that same run's rows sit at p50=2ms, p90=84ms, p99=364ms, p99.9=514ms, max=541ms, with 8 rows in 400-450, 8 in 450-500, 12 in 500-525, 1 in 525-550 and NOTHING above 541. So the only rows the line can ever separate are the 29 above 400ms, and 21 of those 29 sit within ten percent of it. A reader using the artifact's own column would place the threshold at 100ms, where 300 rows sit above it and the nearest rows are not clustered at all -- a completely different and far healthier-looking picture of the same run. The artifact does not merely mis-state the line; it conceals the clustering that makes the real line a change detector rather than an oracle. RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder, and this is the honest placement rather than rung 1. Nothing fails, nothing refuses, and no diagnostic fires: the file is well-formed, the column is present and correctly named by position and by header, and every value parses. The wrongness is silent and is discovered only by someone who happens to hold both the artifact and a refusal message from the same run and notices they disagree. CEILING: 4, structurally impossible. The line a claim is judged against is a fact the judge already holds at the moment it judges, so an artifact that carries the judge's own value rather than a literal cannot state a different one. That is construction rather than validation, and it is available today. NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY: **each cost row emits the line ACTUALLY applied to that row, derived from the same authority the enforcement reads, so that the over-cost population computed from the artifact alone is the set the floor refused** -- sufficient for `rows where cpu_ms >= cost_line_ms` over the artifact to equal the run's refusal set, demonstrated by a discriminating red on a fixture where a row's declared line differs from its enforced one. Changing the constant from 100 to 500 does NOT discharge this: a second hand-authored literal agreeing with the current line by coincidence reproduces the class the moment either moves, and the defect is that the value is authored at all rather than derived. NOT REPAIRED HERE: the emit-family cost work and the mis-grounding of the 500ms line itself are separate subjects with their own dispatch; this row is the modelling defect in the instrument, which is what makes it filable independently of either.)", evidence: [] }
data per_argument_exhaustive_matrix_blind_to_a_cross_argument_relation: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode { identity: "per_argument_exhaustive_matrix_blind_to_a_cross_argument_relation" as NonEmptyStr, authored: "**a per-argument exhaustive matrix cannot see a cross-argument relation, and it READS as exhaustive precisely because it is** (INVALID STATE: a gate function takes two independently derived arguments -- here `wet_route_gate_disposition(standing:admission:)`, whose `standing` came from one receipt envelope and whose `admission` came from a lease pinned to a DIFFERENT envelope. Every arm of `admission` was enumerated and refused correctly for that argument in isolation; every arm of `standing` likewise. The reachable OFF-DIAGONAL state -- lease-admits-A composed with standing-derived-from-B -- inhabits no single argument, so no per-argument enumeration contains it. HARM: the author reports the enumeration as complete, and the report is TRUE. That is what makes this worse than a false completeness claim: a false one is refuted by any counterexample within its stated domain, while a true one over an UNSTATED domain has no counterexample inside the domain it names, so the reader cannot separate `all cases of the argument` from `all cases of the decision`. SPECIMEN (gunbc#9725): five refusal arms of the bootstrap-lease admission were each shown going red under mutation, and `six arms of one argument is not the gate; the gate is the relation between two` was the correction. The repair was structural rather than another arm -- FUSE THE DOOR: the gate no longer accepts a pre-computed admission, it derives the admission itself from the envelope it is judging, so the mismatched pair has no constructor. RECOGNITION RULE: when a matrix is enumerated per argument, ask WHICH RELATIONS BETWEEN ARGUMENTS THE FUNCTION SIGNATURE ADMITS. If two parameters can be derived from different subjects, the product space -- not the union of the axes -- is the domain, and an axis-wise sweep is exhaustive over a projection of it. The tell is a decision function whose arguments are each independently derivable by a caller. THE NEIGHBOUR THIS IS NOT: [[check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim]] is a subject mismatch that a reader can catch by comparing the claim to the check; here the claim and the check agree exactly, and the narrowing is in the DOMAIN both of them share. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: deriving a decision's dependent inputs INSIDE the decision rather than accepting them, wherever two parameters name the same subject -- which is the fused-door move generalized, and makes the off-diagonal unconstructible instead of merely unenumerated. RUNG FOUND AT: mechanically preventable, by a probe that had to be written to construct the state. CEILING: structurally impossible, and reached for this specimen.)", evidence: [] }

data recurring_failure_mode_roster: List<RecurringFailureMode> = [
  censored_estimator_drops_its_own_tail,
  selection_view_read_as_population,
  unlanded_citation_indistinguishable_at_the_citing_end,
  hollow_alias,
  state_space_conflation,
  absorbing_fallback,
  empty_observation_narrow,
  cache_impurity,
  reflection_evidence_structural_proof,
  coercion_proven_by_normalized_round_trip,
  parallel_representation_debt,
  internal_review_finds_missing_tests_external,
  unmarked_workaround,
  self_authorized_dissolution,
  positional_citation,
  bound_shaped_closure,
  authority_substitution,
  reachability_read_as_occupancy,
  total_at_the_level_examined_blind,
  execution_provenance_loss,
  remediation_mutated_view,
  diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent,
  identity_absent_graph_traversal,
  generated_binding_shadows_bare_render,
  resolved_reference_outside_execution_closure,
  surface_shorthand_preempts_resolved_identity,
  meaning_fork,
  externalized_degradation,
  mistyped_body_radiates_nonlocal_diagnostics,
  instrument_output_read_as_subject_content,
  executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing,
  unbacked_execution_claim,
  admitted_module_without_judged_standing,
  refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime,
  mitigation_injected_where_judgment_declined,
  transport_close_read_as_completion,
  merge_region_excludes_shared_tail,
  sealing_property_erases_structure,
  disagreement_census_blind_to_agreed_wrong,
  undecided_fraction_read_as_denominator,
  restoration_promise_names_a_route_that_does_not_exist,
  alias_resolution_collides_with_kernel_spelling,
  restored_bytes_reviewed_as_authorship,
  review_summary_inverts_roles_and_affirms_the_join,
  fabricated_debt,
  yaml_inline_comment_ingested_as_scalar_content,
  accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target,
  incidental_denominator_as_wall,
  compensating_errors_cancel_in_the_aggregate,
  one_refusal_two_destinations,
  join_answers_with_one_arm_others_unjudged,
  liveness_probe_read_as_currency,
  non_verdict_disposition_surfaces_as_refusal,
  empty_capture_read_as_clean_result,
  unhandled_state_falls_to_the_not_yet_arm,
  salience_instrument_blind_to_the_record_it_sizes,
  ambient_process_state_read_by_a_concurrent_reader,
  predicate_vacuously_true_on_an_empty_domain,
  check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim,
